          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"cryptsetup" name=3D"cryptsetup"></a>cryptsetup-2=
.7.4
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to cryptsetup
              </h3>
              <p>
                cryptsetup is used to set up transparent encryption of bloc=
k
                devices using the kernel crypto API.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470536037808" name=3D"idm140470536037808"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://w=
ww.kernel.org/pub/linux/utils/cryptsetup/v2.7/cryptsetup-2.7.4.tar.xz">
                      https://www.kernel.org/pub/linux/utils/cryptsetup/v2.=
7/cryptsetup-2.7.4.tar.xz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 26ffe48f65d144af91b2a9639425d08c
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 11 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 35 MB (add 5 MB for
                      tests)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.2 SBU (add 8.1 SBU for tests)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470536028928" name=3D"idm140470536028928"></=
a>cryptsetup Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470536028240" name=3D"idm140470536028240"></=
a>Required
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#json-c" title=3D"JS=
ON-C-0.17">JSON-C-0.17</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#lvm2" t=
itle=3D"LVM2-2.03.26">LVM2-2.03.26</a>, and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https=
://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochu=
nks.html#popt" title=3D"Popt-1.19">popt-1.19</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470536024560" name=3D"idm140470536024560"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#asciidoctor" title=
=3D"Asciidoctor-2.0.23">asciidoctor-2.0.23</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"h=
ttps://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-n=
ochunks.html#libpwquality" title=3D"libpwquality-1.4.5">libpwquality-1.4.5<=
/a>, <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://github.com/P-H-C/phc-winner-argon2"=
>argon2</a>,
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://www.libssh.org/">libssh<=
/a>,
                and <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://www.openwall.com/pas=
swdqc/">passwdqc</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"cryptsetup-kernel" name=3D"cryptsetup-kernel"></a>=
Kernel
                Configuration
              </h3>
              <p>
                Encrypted block devices require kernel support. To use it,
                the appropriate kernel configuration parameters need to be
                set:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"blue">D</span>evice Driv=
ers ---&gt;
  [*] M<span class=3D"blue">u</span>ltiple devices driver support (RAID and=
 LVM) ---&gt;                   [MD]
    &lt;*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">D</span>evice mapper support          =
                           [BLK_DEV_DM]
    &lt;*/M&gt;   <span class=3D"blue">C</span>rypt target support         =
                             [DM_CRYPT]

-*- <span class=3D"blue">C</span>ryptographic API ---&gt;                  =
                            [CRYPTO]
  <span class=3D"blue">B</span>lock ciphers ---&gt;
    &lt;*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">A</span>ES (Advanced Encryption Standa=
rd)                        [CRYPTO_AES]
    # For tests:
    &lt;*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">T</span>wofish                        =
                       [CRYPTO_TWOFISH]
  <span class=3D"blue">L</span>ength-preserving ciphers and modes ---&gt;
    &lt;*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">X</span>TS (XOR Encrypt XOR with ciphe=
rtext stealing)            [CRYPTO_XTS]
  H<span class=3D"blue">a</span>shes, digests, and MACs ---&gt;
    &lt;*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">S</span>HA-224 and SHA-256            =
                        [CRYPTO_SHA256]
  <span class=3D"blue">U</span>serspace interface ---&gt;
    &lt;*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">S</span>ymmetric key cipher algorithms=
             [CRYPTO_USER_API_SKCIPHER]</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of cryptsetup
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">cryptsetup</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr       \
            --disable-ssh-token \
            --disable-asciidoc  &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the result, issue as the <code class=3D"systemitem"=
>root</code> user: <span class=3D"command"><strong>make check</strong></spa=
n>. Some tests will
                fail if appropriate kernel configuration options are not se=
t.
                Some additional options that may be needed for tests are:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><code class=3D"literal">CONFIG_SCSI_LOW=
LEVEL,
CONFIG_SCSI_DEBUG,
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_DM_BUILTIN,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_CRYPTD,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_LRW,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_XTS,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_ESSIV,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_CRCT10DIF,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_TI,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_NI_INTEL,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_BLOWFISH,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_CAST5,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_SERPENT,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_SERPENT_SSE2_X86_64,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_SERPENT_AVX_X86_64,
CONFIG_CRYPTO_SERPENT_AVX2_X86_64, and
CONFIG_CRYPTO_TWOFISH_X86_64</code></pre>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-ssh-token</code></e=
m>:
                This switch is required if the optional libssh dependency i=
s
                not installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-asciidoc</code></em=
>:
                This switch disables regeneration of the man pages. Remove
                this switch if you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://w=
ww.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.=
html#asciidoctor" title=3D"Asciidoctor-2.0.23">asciidoctor-2.0.23</a> insta=
lled
                and wish to regenerate the man pages. Note that even if thi=
s
                switch is used, the pre-generated man pages are shipped in
                the tarball and they'll still be installed.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring cryptsetup
              </h3>
              <p>
                Because of the number of possible configurations, setup of
                encrypted volumes is beyond the scope of the BLFS book.
                Please see the configuration guide in the cryptsetup
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://gitlab.com/cryptsetup/cr=
yptsetup/wikis/FrequentlyAskedQuestions#2-setup">
                FAQ</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
