            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of GnuPG
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">GnuPG</span> by running=
 the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

../configure --prefix=3D/usr           \
             --localstatedir=3D/var    \
             --sysconfdir=3D/etc       \
             --docdir=3D/usr/share/doc/gnupg-2.4.5 &amp;&amp;
make &amp;&amp;

makeinfo --html --no-split -I doc -o doc/gnupg_nochunks.html ../doc/gnupg.t=
exi &amp;&amp;
makeinfo --plaintext       -I doc -o doc/gnupg.txt           ../doc/gnupg.t=
exi &amp;&amp;
make -C doc html</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#texlive=
" title=3D"texlive-20240312-source">texlive-20240312</a> installed and
                you wish to create documentation in the pdf format, issue t=
he
                following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make -C doc p=
df</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install &amp;=
&amp;

install -v -m755 -d /usr/share/doc/gnupg-2.4.5/html            &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644    doc/gnupg_nochunks.html \
                    /usr/share/doc/gnupg-2.4.5/html/gnupg.html &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644    ../doc/*.texi doc/gnupg.txt \
                    /usr/share/doc/gnupg-2.4.5 &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644    doc/gnupg.html/* \
                    /usr/share/doc/gnupg-2.4.5/html</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you created the pdf format of the documentation, install
                them using the following command as the <code class=3D"syst=
emitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -m644 d=
oc/gnupg.pdf \
                 /usr/share/doc/gnupg-2.4.5</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>mkdir build &amp;&amp; cd
                build</strong></span>: the Gnupg2 developers recommend to
                build the package in a dedicated directory.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--docdir=3D/usr/share/doc/gnu=
pg-2.4.5</code></em>:
                This switch changes the default docdir to <code class=3D"fi=
lename">/usr/share/doc/gnupg-2.4.5</code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-all-tests</code>: This swit=
ch
                allows more tests to be run with <span class=3D"command"><s=
trong>make check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-g13</code>: This switch ena=
bles
                building the g13 program.
              </p>
            </div>
