            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of GnuTLS
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">GnuTLS</span> by runnin=
g
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr \
            --docdir=3D/usr/share/doc/gnutls-3.8.7.1 \
            --with-default-trust-store-pkcs11=3D"pkcs11:" &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                One test hangs the test procedure. Disable it: <span class=
=3D"command"><strong>sed '/ocsp-must-staple-connection/d' -i
                tests/Makefile</strong></span>. To test the results, now
                issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong>make
                check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, install the package as the <code class=3D"systemitem">=
root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-default-trust-store-pk=
cs11=3D"pkcs11:"</code></em>:
                This switch tells gnutls to use the PKCS #11 trust store as
                the default trust. Omit this switch if <a class=3D"xref" hr=
ef=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2=
-sysv-nochunks.html#p11-kit" title=3D"p11-kit-0.25.5">p11-kit-0.25.5</a> is=
 not
                installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-default-trust-store-file=3D/e=
tc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt</code>:
                This switch tells <span class=3D"command"><strong>configure=
</strong></span> where to find the
                legacy CA certificate bundle and to use it instead of PKCS
                #11 module by default. Use this if <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#p11-kit" title=3D"p11-kit-0.25.5">p11-kit-0.25.5</a> is n=
ot
                installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-gtk-doc</code>: Use this
                parameter if <span class=3D"application">GTK-Doc</span> is
                installed and you wish to rebuild and install the API
                documentation.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-openssl-compatibility</code=
>:
                Use this switch if you wish to build the OpenSSL
                compatibility library.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--without-p11-kit</code>: use this
                switch if you have not installed <span class=3D"application=
">p11-kit</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-included-unistring</code>: us=
es
                the bundled version of libunistring, instead of the system
                one. Use this switch if you have not installed <a class=3D"=
xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-B=
OOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libunistring" title=3D"libunistring-1.2">libuni=
string-1.2</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--disable-dsa</code>: completely
                disables DSA algorithm support.
              </p>
