2-sysv-nochunks.html#clisp" title=3D"Clisp-2.49">Clisp-2.49</a>, <a class=
=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BL=
FS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#qt5-components" title=3D"qt5-components-5.1=
5.14">qt5-components-5.15.14</a>, and
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#swig" title=3D"SWIG=
-4.2.1">SWIG-4.2.1</a> (for language bindings)
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of GPGME
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">GPGME</span> by running=
 the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

../configure --prefix=3D/usr --disable-gpg-test &amp;&amp;
make PYTHONS=3D</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#swig" title=3D"S=
WIG-4.2.1">SWIG-4.2.1</a> is installed, build the Python 3
                binding as a wheel:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">if swig -vers=
ion &gt; /dev/null; then
  srcdir=3D$PWD/../lang/python \
  top_builddir=3D$PWD          \
  pip3 wheel -w dist --no-build-isolation --no-deps --no-cache-dir $PWD/lan=
g/python
fi</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, you should have <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#gnupg2" title=3D"GnuPG-2.4.5">GnuPG-2.4.5</a> installed a=
nd
                remove the <code class=3D"option">--disable-gpg-test</code>
                above. If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromsc=
ratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#swig" tit=
le=3D"SWIG-4.2.1">SWIG-4.2.1</a> is installed, it's necessary to
                adapt the test suite to use the Python 3 binding just built
                as a wheel as well. Issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">if swig -vers=
ion &gt; /dev/null; then
  python3 -m venv testenv                                              &amp=
;&amp;
  testenv/bin/pip3 install --no-index --find-links=3Ddist --no-cache-dir \
                           gpg                                         &amp=
;&amp;
  sed '/PYTHON/s#run-tests.py#&amp; --python-libdir=3D/dev/null#'          =
  \
      -i lang/python/tests/Makefile
fi &amp;&amp;

make -k check PYTHONS=3D PYTHON=3D$PWD/testenv/bin/python3</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                One test named <code class=3D"filename">t-quick-key-manipul=
ation.py</code> is known to
                fail.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install PYTHO=
NS=3D</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#swig" title=3D"S=
WIG-4.2.1">SWIG-4.2.1</a> is installed, still as the
                <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user, install the Py=
thon
                3 binding:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">if swig -version &=
gt; /dev/null; then
  pip3 install --no-index --find-links=3Ddist --no-cache-dir --no-user gpg
fi</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-gpg-test</code></em=
>:
                if this parameter is not passed to configure, the test
                programs are built during <span class=3D"command"><strong>m=
ake</strong></span> stage, which requires
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gnupg2" title=3D"Gn=
uPG-2.4.5">GnuPG-2.4.5</a>. This parameter is not needed
                if <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gnupg2" title=3D=
"GnuPG-2.4.5">GnuPG-2.4.5</a> is installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>PYTHONS=3D</code></em>: Disab=
le
                building Python binding using the deprecated <span class=3D=
"command"><strong>python3 setup.py build</strong></span>
                command. The explicit instruction to build the Python 3
                binding with the <span class=3D"command"><strong>pip3
                wheel</strong></span> command is provided.
              </p>
