              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534995328" name=3D"idm140470534995328"></=
a>Required
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#cracklib" title=3D"=
CrackLib-2.10.2">CrackLib-2.10.2</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534993344" name=3D"idm140470534993344"></=
a>Recommended
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#linux-pam" title=3D=
"Linux-PAM-1.6.1">Linux-PAM-1.6.1</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of libpwquality
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">libpwquality</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr                      \
            --disable-static                   \
            --with-securedir=3D/usr/lib/security \
            --disable-python-bindings          &amp;&amp;
make &amp;&amp;
pip3 wheel -w dist --no-build-isolation --no-deps --no-cache-dir $PWD/pytho=
n</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install &amp;=
&amp;
pip3 install --no-index --find-links=3Ddist --no-cache-dir --no-user pwqual=
ity</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-python-bindings</co=
de></em>: This
                parameter disables building Python bindings with the
                deprecated <span class=3D"command"><strong>python3 setup.py
                build</strong></span> command. The explicit instruction to
                build the Python 3 binding with the <span class=3D"command"=
><strong>pip3 wheel</strong></span> command is
                provided.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring libpwquality
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"application">libpwquality</span> is intended=
 to
                be a functional replacement for the now-obsolete <code clas=
s=3D"filename">pam_cracklib.so</code> PAM module. To configure
                the system to use the <code class=3D"filename">pam_pwqualit=
y</code> module, execute the following
                commands as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user=
:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mv /etc/pam.d/syst=
em-password{,.orig} &amp;&amp;
cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/system-password &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal"># Begin /etc/pam.d/system-password

# check new passwords for strength (man pam_pwquality)
password  required    pam_pwquality.so   authtok_type=3DUNIX retry=3D1 difo=
k=3D1 \
                                         minlen=3D8 dcredit=3D0 ucredit=3D0=
 \
                                         lcredit=3D0 ocredit=3D0 minclass=
=3D1 \
                                         maxrepeat=3D0 maxsequence=3D0 \
                                         maxclassrepeat=3D0 gecoscheck=3D0 =
\
                                         dictcheck=3D1 usercheck=3D1 \
                                         enforcing=3D1 badwords=3D"" \
                                         dictpath=3D/usr/lib/cracklib/pw_di=
ct

# use yescrypt hash for encryption, use shadow, and try to use any
# previously defined authentication token (chosen password) set by any
# prior module.
password  required    pam_unix.so        yescrypt shadow try_first_pass

# End /etc/pam.d/system-password</code>
EOF
</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
