              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#valgrind" title=3D"=
Valgrind-3.23.0">Valgrind-3.23.0</a> (optional for the
                tests)
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Nettle
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Nettle</span> by runnin=
g
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr --disable-static &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install &amp;=
&amp;
chmod   -v   755 /usr/lib/lib{hogweed,nettle}.so &amp;&amp;
install -v -m755 -d /usr/share/doc/nettle-3.10 &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644 nettle.{html,pdf} /usr/share/doc/nettle-3.10</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-static</code></em>:
                This switch prevents installation of static versions of the
                libraries.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">nettle-hash, nettle-lfib-stream=
,
                    nettle-pbkdf2, pkcs1-conv and sexp-conv</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Libraries:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">libhogweed.so and
                    libnettle.so</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Directory:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">/usr/include/nettle and
                    /usr/share/doc/nettle-3.10</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"variablelist">
                <h4>
                  <a id=3D"idm140470534625584" name=3D"idm140470534625584">=
</a>Short Descriptions
                </h4>
                <table border=3D"0" class=3D"variablelist">
                  <colgroup>
                    <col align=3D"left" valign=3D"top">
                    <col>
                  </colgroup>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"nettle-hash" name=3D"nettle-hash"></a><s=
pan class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>nettle-hash</strong></sp=
an></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          calculates a hash value using a specified algorit=
hm
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"nettle-lfib-stream" name=3D"nettle-lfib-=
stream"></a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>nettle-lfi=
b-stream</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          outputs a sequence of pseudorandom
                          (non-cryptographic) bytes, using Knuth's lagged
                          fibonacci generator. The stream is useful for
                          testing, but should not be used to generate
                          cryptographic keys or anything else that needs re=
al
                          randomness
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"nettle-pbkdf2" name=3D"nettle-pbkdf2"></=
a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>nettle-pbkdf2</stron=
g></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a password-based key derivation function that
                          takes a password or a passphrase as input and
                          returns a strengthened password, which is protect=
ed
                          against pre-computation attacks by using salting
                          and other expensive computations.
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"pkcs1-conv" name=3D"pkcs1-conv"></a><spa=
n class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>pkcs1-conv</strong></span>=
</span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          converts private and public RSA keys from PKCS #1
                          format to sexp format
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"sexp-conv" name=3D"sexp-conv"></a><span =
class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>sexp-conv</strong></span></s=
pan>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          converts an s-expression to a different encoding
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"nss" name=3D"nss"></a>NSS-3.103
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to NSS
              </h3>
              <p>
                The Network Security Services (<span class=3D"application">=
NSS</span>) package is a set of libraries
                designed to support cross-platform development of
                security-enabled client and server applications. Applicatio=
ns
                built with NSS can support SSL v2 and v3, TLS, PKCS #5, PKC=
S
                #7, PKCS #11, PKCS #12, S/MIME, X.509 v3 certificates, and
                other security standards. This is useful for implementing S=
SL
                and S/MIME or other Internet security standards into an
                application.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534595504" name=3D"idm140470534595504"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://a=
rchive.mozilla.org/pub/security/nss/releases/NSS_3_103_RTM/src/nss-3.103.ta=
r.gz">
                      https://archive.mozilla.org/pub/security/nss/releases=
/NSS_3_103_RTM/src/nss-3.103.tar.gz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 2823082a44b9dd71d6281108e0bab03f
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 73 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 304 MB (add 149 MB for
                      tests)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.8 SBU (with parallelism=3D4, =
add
                      16 SBU for tests on AMD Ryzens or at least 30 SBU on
                      Intel machines)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534587952" name=3D"idm140470534587952"></=
a>Additional Downloads
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Required patch: <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/nss-3.103-standalone-1.patch">
                      https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/ns=
s-3.103-standalone-1.patch</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534584368" name=3D"idm140470534584368"></=
a>NSS
                Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534583680" name=3D"idm140470534583680"></=
a>Required
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#nspr" title=3D"NSPR=
-4.35">NSPR-4.35</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534581632" name=3D"idm140470534581632"></=
a>Recommended
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#sqlite" title=3D"SQ=
Lite-3.46.1">SQLite-3.46.1</a> and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
p11-kit" title=3D"p11-kit-0.25.5">p11-kit-0.25.5</a>
                (runtime)
              </p>
              <p class=3D"usernotes">
                Editor Notes: <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://wiki.linux=
fromscratch.org/blfs/wiki/nss">https://wiki.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/wiki/=
nss</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of NSS
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">NSS</span> by running t=
he
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">patch -Np1 -i=
 ../nss-3.103-standalone-1.patch &amp;&amp;

cd nss &amp;&amp;

make BUILD_OPT=3D1                      \
  NSPR_INCLUDE_DIR=3D/usr/include/nspr  \
  USE_SYSTEM_ZLIB=3D1                   \
  ZLIB_LIBS=3D-lz                       \
  NSS_ENABLE_WERROR=3D0                 \
  $([ $(uname -m) =3D x86_64 ] &amp;&amp; echo USE_64=3D1) \
  $([ -f /usr/include/sqlite3.h ] &amp;&amp; echo NSS_USE_SYSTEM_SQLITE=3D1=
)</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To run the tests, execute the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cd tests &amp=
;&amp;
HOST=3Dlocalhost DOMSUF=3Dlocaldomain ./all.sh
cd ../</kbd></pre>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  Some information about the tests:
                </p>
                <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                  <ul class=3D"compact">
                    <li class=3D"listitem">
                      <p>
                        HOST=3Dlocalhost and DOMSUF=3Dlocaldomain are requi=
red.
                        Without these variables, a FQDN is required to be
                        specified and this generic way should work for
                        everyone, provided <code class=3D"systemitem">local=
host.localdomain</code> is defined
                        <span class=3D"phrase">in <code class=3D"filename">=
/etc/hosts</code>, as done in <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://www.linuxf=
romscratch.org/lfs/view/12.2/chapter09/network.html#ch-config-hosts">
                        the LFS book</a>.</span>
                      </p>
                    </li>
                    <li class=3D"listitem">
                      <p>
                        The tests take a long time to run. If desired there
                        is information in the all.sh script about running
                        subsets of the total test suite.
                      </p>
                    </li>
                    <li class=3D"listitem">
                      <p>
                        When interrupting the tests, the test suite fails t=
o
                        spin down test servers that are run. This leads to =
an
                        infinite loop in the tests where the test suite tri=
es
                        to kill a server that doesn't exist anymore because
                        it pulls the wrong PID.
                      </p>
                    </li>
                    <li class=3D"listitem">
                      <p>
                        Test suite results (in HTML format!) can be found a=
t
                        ../../test_results/security/localhost.1/results.htm=
l
                      </p>
                    </li>
                    <li class=3D"listitem">
                      <p>
                        A few tests might fail on some Intel machines for
                        unknown reasons.
                      </p>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cd ../dist        =
                                                  &amp;&amp;

install -v -m755 Linux*/lib/*.so              /usr/lib              &amp;&a=
mp;
install -v -m644 Linux*/lib/{*.chk,libcrmf.a} /usr/lib              &amp;&a=
mp;

install -v -m755 -d                           /usr/include/nss      &amp;&a=
mp;
cp -v -RL {public,private}/nss/*              /usr/include/nss      &amp;&a=
mp;

install -v -m755 Linux*/bin/{certutil,nss-config,pk12util} /usr/bin &amp;&a=
mp;

install -v -m644 Linux*/lib/pkgconfig/nss.pc  /usr/lib/pkgconfig</kbd></pre=
>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>BUILD_OPT=3D1</code></em>: Th=
is
                option is passed to <span class=3D"command"><strong>make</s=
trong></span> so that the build is
                performed with no debugging symbols built into the binaries
                and the default compiler optimizations are used.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>NSPR_INCLUDE_DIR=3D/usr/inclu=
de/nspr</code></em>:
                This option sets the location of the nspr headers.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>USE_SYSTEM_ZLIB=3D1</code></e=
m>:
                This option is passed to <span class=3D"command"><strong>ma=
ke</strong></span> to ensure that the
                <code class=3D"filename">libssl3.so</code> library is linke=
d to
                the system installed <span class=3D"application">zlib</span=
>
                instead of the in-tree version.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>ZLIB_LIBS=3D-lz</code></em>: =
This
                option provides the linker flags needed to link to the syst=
em
                <span class=3D"application">zlib</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>$([ $(uname -m) =3D x86_64 =
]
                &amp;&amp; echo USE_64=3D1)</strong></span>: The <em class=
=3D"parameter"><code>USE_64=3D1</code></em> option is <span class=3D"emphas=
is"><em>required on x86_64</em></span>, otherwise
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>make</strong></span> will t=
ry
                (and fail) to create 32-bit objects. The [ $(uname -m) =3D
                x86_64 ] test ensures it has no effect on a 32 bit system.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>([ -f /usr/include/sqlite3.=
h ]
                &amp;&amp; echo NSS_USE_SYSTEM_SQLITE=3D1)</strong></span>:
                This tests if <span class=3D"application">sqlite</span> is
                installed and if so it <span class=3D"command"><strong>echo=
</strong></span>s the option
                NSS_USE_SYSTEM_SQLITE=3D1 to <span class=3D"command"><stron=
g>make</strong></span> so that <code class=3D"filename">libsoftokn3.so</cod=
e> will link against the system
                version of sqlite.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">NSS_DISABLE_GTESTS=3D1</code>: If yo=
u
                don't need to run NSS test suite, append this option to
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>make</strong></span> comman=
d,
                to prevent the compilation of tests and save some build tim=
e.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring NSS
              </h3>
              <p>
                If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#p11-kit" title=
=3D"p11-kit-0.25.5">p11-kit-0.25.5</a> is installed, the
                <span class=3D"application">p11-kit</span> trust module
                (<code class=3D"filename">/usr/lib/pkcs11/p11-kit-trust.so<=
/code>) can be
                used as a drop-in replacement for <code class=3D"filename">=
/usr/lib/libnssckbi.so</code> to transparently
                make the system CAs available to <span class=3D"application=
">NSS</span> aware applications, rather than the
                static library provided by <code class=3D"filename">/usr/li=
b/libnssckbi.so</code>. As the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user,=
 execute the following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ln -sfv ./pkcs11/p=
11-kit-trust.so /usr/lib/libnssckbi.so</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Additionally, for dependent applications that do not use th=
e
                internal database (<code class=3D"filename">/usr/lib/libnss=
ckbi.so</code>), the <code class=3D"filename">/usr/sbin/make-ca</code> scri=
pt included on the
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#make-ca" title=3D"m=
ake-ca-1.14">make-ca-1.14</a> page can generate a system
                wide NSS DB with the <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-n</code=
></em> switch, or by modifying the
                <code class=3D"filename">/etc/make-ca/make-ca.conf</code> f=
ile.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">certutil, nss-config, and
                    pk12util</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Libraries:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">libcrmf.a, libfreebl3.so,
                    libfreeblpriv3.so, libnss3.so, libnssckbi.so,
                    libnssckbi-testlib.so, libnssdbm3.so, libnsssysinit.so,
                    libnssutil3.so, libpkcs11testmodule.so, libsmime3.so,
                    libsoftokn3.so, and libssl3.so</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Directories:</stro=
ng>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">/usr/include/nss</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"variablelist">
                <h4>
                  <a id=3D"idm140470534519248" name=3D"idm140470534519248">=
</a>Short Descriptions
                </h4>
                <table border=3D"0" class=3D"variablelist">
                  <colgroup>
                    <col align=3D"left" valign=3D"top">
                    <col>
                  </colgroup>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"certutil" name=3D"certutil"></a><span cl=
ass=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>certutil</strong></span></span=
>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is the Mozilla Certificate Database Tool. It is a
                          command-line utility that can create and modify t=
he
                          Netscape Communicator cert8.db and key3.db databa=
se
                          files. It can also list, generate, modify, or
                          delete certificates within the cert8.db file and
                          create or change the password, generate new publi=
c
                          and private key pairs, display the contents of th=
e
                          key database, or delete key pairs within the
                          key3.db file
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"nss-config" name=3D"nss-config"></a><spa=
n class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>nss-config</strong></span>=
</span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is used to determine the NSS library settings of
                          the installed NSS libraries
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"pk12util" name=3D"pk12util"></a><span cl=
ass=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>pk12util</strong></span></span=
>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a tool for importing certificates and keys fro=
m
                          pkcs #12 files into NSS or exporting them. It can
                          also list certificates and keys in such files
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"openssh" name=3D"openssh"></a>OpenSSH-9.8p1
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to OpenSSH
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">OpenSSH</span> package cont=
ains
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>ssh</strong></span> clients=
 and
                the <span class=3D"command"><strong>sshd</strong></span>
                daemon. This is useful for encrypting authentication and
                subsequent traffic over a network. The <span class=3D"comma=
nd"><strong>ssh</strong></span> and <span class=3D"command"><strong>scp</st=
rong></span> commands are secure
                implementations of <span class=3D"command"><strong>telnet</=
strong></span> and <span class=3D"command"><strong>rcp</strong></span> resp=
ectively.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534492336" name=3D"idm140470534492336"></=
a>Package Information
