              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gtk-doc" title=3D"G=
TK-Doc-1.34.0">GTK-Doc-1.34.0</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
libxslt" title=3D"libxslt-1.1.42">libxslt-1.1.42</a>, and
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#nss" title=3D"NSS-3=
.103">nss-3.103</a>
                (runtime)
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of p11-kit
              </h3>
              <p>
                Prepare the distribution specific anchor hook:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed '20,$ d' =
-i trust/trust-extract-compat &amp;&amp;

cat &gt;&gt; trust/trust-extract-compat &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal"># Copy existing anchor modifications to /etc/ssl/lo=
cal
/usr/libexec/make-ca/copy-trust-modifications

# Update trust stores
/usr/sbin/make-ca -r</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">p11-kit</span> by runni=
ng
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir p11-bui=
ld &amp;&amp;
cd    p11-build &amp;&amp;

meson setup ..            \
      --prefix=3D/usr       \
      --buildtype=3Drelease \
      -D trust_paths=3D/etc/pki/anchors &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>LC_ALL=3DC ninja test</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install &amp=
;&amp;
ln -sfv /usr/libexec/p11-kit/trust-extract-compat \
        /usr/bin/update-ca-certificates</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                trust_paths=3D/etc/pki/anchors</code></em>: this switch set=
s
                the location of trusted certificates used by libp11-kit.so.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D hash_impl=3Dfreebl</code>: Use th=
is
                switch if you want to use the Freebl library from
                <span class=3D"application">NSS</span> for SHA1 and MD5
                hashing.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D gtk_doc=3Dtrue</code>: Use this s=
witch
                if you have installed <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www=
.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.ht=
ml#gtk-doc" title=3D"GTK-Doc-1.34.0">GTK-Doc-1.34.0</a> and <a class=3D"xre=
f" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK=
-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libxslt" title=3D"libxslt-1.1.42">libxslt-1.1.42</=
a> and wish
                to rebuild the documentation and generate manual pages.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring p11-kit
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">p11-kit</span> trust module
                (<code class=3D"filename">/usr/lib/pkcs11/p11-kit-trust.so<=
/code>) can be
                used as a drop-in replacement for <code class=3D"filename">=
/usr/lib/libnssckbi.so</code> to transparently
                make the system CAs available to <span class=3D"application=
">NSS</span> aware applications, rather than the
                static list provided by <code class=3D"filename">/usr/lib/l=
ibnssckbi.so</code>. As the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user, ex=
ecute the following
                commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ln -sfv ./pkcs11/p=
11-kit-trust.so /usr/lib/libnssckbi.so</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">p11-kit, trust, and
                    update-ca-certificates</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Libraries:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">libp11-kit.so and
                    p11-kit-proxy.so</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Directories:</stro=
ng>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">/etc/pkcs11,
                    /usr/include/p11-kit-1, /usr/lib/pkcs11,
                    /usr/libexec/p11-kit, /usr/share/gtk-doc/html/p11-kit,
                    and /usr/share/p11-kit</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"variablelist">
                <h4>
                  <a id=3D"idm140470534285968" name=3D"idm140470534285968">=
</a>Short Descriptions
                </h4>
                <table border=3D"0" class=3D"variablelist">
                  <colgroup>
                    <col align=3D"left" valign=3D"top">
                    <col>
                  </colgroup>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"p11-kit-prog" name=3D"p11-kit-prog"></a>=
<span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>p11-kit</strong></span=
></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a command line tool that can be used to perfor=
m
                          operations on PKCS#11 modules configured on the
                          system
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"trust" name=3D"trust"></a><span class=3D=
"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>trust</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a command line tool to examine and modify the
                          shared trust policy store
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"update-ca-certificates" name=3D"update-c=
a-certificates"></a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>up=
date-ca-certificates</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a command line tool to both extract local
                          certificates from an updated anchor store, and
                          regenerate all anchors and certificate stores on
                          the system. This is done unconditionally on BLFS
                          using the <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--force</=
code></em> and
                          <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--get</code></em> f=
lags
                          to <span class=3D"command"><strong>make-ca</stron=
g></span> and
                          should likely not be used for automated updates
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"libp11-kit" name=3D"libp11-kit"></a><spa=
n class=3D"term"><code class=3D"filename">libp11-kit.so</code></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          contains functions used to coordinate
                          initialization and finalization of any PKCS#11
                          module
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"p11-kit-proxy" name=3D"p11-kit-proxy"></=
a><span class=3D"term"><code class=3D"filename">p11-kit-proxy.so</code></sp=
an>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is the PKCS#11 proxy module
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"polkit" name=3D"polkit"></a>Polkit-125
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Polkit
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"application">Polkit</span> is a toolkit for
                defining and handling authorizations. It is used for allowi=
ng
                unprivileged processes to communicate with privileged
                processes.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534253360" name=3D"idm140470534253360"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://g=
ithub.com/polkit-org/polkit/archive/125/polkit-125.tar.gz">
                      https://github.com/polkit-org/polkit/archive/125/polk=
it-125.tar.gz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 8e9f2377fc7b4010bd29b97d2e288b4f
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 444 KB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 7.2 MB (with tests)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.3 SBU (with tests; using
                      parallelism=3D4)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534244384" name=3D"idm140470534244384"></=
a>Polkit Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534243696" name=3D"idm140470534243696"></=
a>Required
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#glib2" title=3D"GLi=
b-2.80.4">GLib-2.80.4</a> (GObject Introspection
                recommended)
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534241648" name=3D"idm140470534241648"></=
a>Recommended
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#duktape" title=3D"d=
uktape-2.7.0">duktape-2.7.0</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linu=
xfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#li=
bxslt" title=3D"libxslt-1.1.42">libxslt-1.1.42</a>,
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#linux-pam" title=3D=
"Linux-PAM-1.6.1">Linux-PAM-1.6.1</a><span class=3D"phrase">,
                and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.=
org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#elogind" title=
=3D"elogind-255.5">elogind-255.5</a></span>
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  Since <span class=3D"phrase"><span class=3D"command"><str=
ong>elogind</strong></span></span> uses PAM
                  to register user sessions, it is a good idea to build
                  <span class=3D"application">Polkit</span> with PAM suppor=
t so
                  <span class=3D"phrase"><span class=3D"command"><strong>el=
ogind</strong></span></span> can track
                  <span class=3D"application">Polkit</span> sessions.
                </p>
              </div>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470534231616" name=3D"idm140470534231616"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gtk-doc" title=3D"G=
TK-Doc-1.34.0">GTK-Doc-1.34.0</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
python-dbusmock" title=3D"dbusmock-0.32.1">dbusmock-0.32.1</a> (required fo=
r tests),
                and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.=
org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#spidermonkey" t=
itle=3D"SpiderMonkey from firefox-115.14.0">SpiderMonkey from
                Firefox-115.14.0</a> (can be used in place of duktape)
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"polkit-agent" name=3D"polkit-agent"></a> Optional
                Runtime Dependencies
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                One polkit authentication agent for using polkit in the
                graphical environment: <span class=3D"application">polkit-k=
de-agent</span> in <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#plasma-build" ti=
tle=3D"Building Plasma">Plasma-6.1.4</a>
                for KDE, the agent built in <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https=
://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochu=
nks.html#gnome-shell" title=3D"gnome-shell-46.4">gnome-shell-46.4</a>
                for GNOME3, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#polkit-=
gnome" title=3D"polkit-gnome-0.105">polkit-gnome-0.105</a> for XFCE, and
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#lxqt-policykit" tit=
le=3D"lxqt-policykit-2.0.0">lxqt-policykit-2.0.0</a> for LXQt
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch=
.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libxslt" title=
=3D"libxslt-1.1.42">libxslt-1.1.42</a> is installed, then
                  <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.or=
g/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#DocBook" title=3D=
"docbook-xml-4.5">docbook-xml-4.5</a> and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https:/=
/www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunk=
s.html#docbook-xsl" title=3D"docbook-xsl-nons-1.79.2">docbook-xsl-nons-1.79=
.2</a> are
                  required. If you have installed <a class=3D"xref" href=3D=
"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv=
-nochunks.html#libxslt" title=3D"libxslt-1.1.42">libxslt-1.1.42</a>, but
                  you do not want to install any of the DocBook packages
                  mentioned, you will need to use <code class=3D"option">-D
                  man=3Dfalse</code> in the instructions below.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"polkit-test-kernel" name=3D"polkit-test-kernel"></=
a>Kernel Configuration
              </h3>
              <p>
                Some tests need user namespace. If running the test suite,
                enable it:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"blue">G</span>eneral set=
up ---&gt;
  -*- N<span class=3D"blue">a</span>mespaces support ---&gt;               =
                        [NAMESPACES]
    [*] <span class=3D"blue">U</span>ser namespace                         =
                        [USER_NS]</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Polkit
              </h3>
              <p>
                There should be a dedicated user and group to take control =
of
                the <span class=3D"command"><strong>polkitd</strong></span>
                daemon after it is started. Issue the following commands as
                the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -fg 27 po=
lkitd &amp;&amp;
useradd -c "PolicyKit Daemon Owner" -d /etc/polkit-1 -u 27 \
        -g polkitd -s /bin/false polkitd</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                First fix a build problem for sysV based systems:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -i '/syst=
emd_sysusers_dir/s/^/#/' meson.build</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Polkit</span> by runnin=
g
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup ..                    \
      --prefix=3D/usr               \
      --buildtype=3Drelease         \
      -D man=3Dtrue                 \
      -D session_tracking=3Delogind \
      -D tests=3Dtrue</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Build the package:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja</kbd></=
pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, first ensure that the system
                <span class=3D"application">D-Bus</span> daemon is running,=
 and
                both <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch=
.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#dbus-python" t=
itle=3D"D-Bus Python-1.3.2">D-Bus Python-1.3.2</a> and <a class=3D"xref" hr=
ef=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2=
-sysv-nochunks.html#python-dbusmock" title=3D"dbusmock-0.32.1">dbusmock-0.3=
2.1</a> are installed. Then run
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>ninja test</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D tests=3Dtrue</code></em>: =
This
                switch allows to run the test suite of this package. As
                <span class=3D"application">Polkit</span> is used for
                authorizations, its integrity can affect system security. S=
o
                it's recommended to run the test suite building this packag=
e.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D js_engine=3Dmozjs</code>: This sw=
itch
                allows using the <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linu=
xfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#sp=
idermonkey" title=3D"SpiderMonkey from firefox-115.14.0">SpiderMonkey from
                Firefox-115.14.0</a> JavaScript engine instead of the
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#duktape" title=3D"d=
uktape-2.7.0">duktape-2.7.0</a> JavaScript engine.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D os_type=3Dlfs</code>: Use this sw=
itch
                if you did not create the <code class=3D"filename">/etc/lfs=
-release</code> file or distribution auto
                detection will fail and you will be unable to use
                <span class=3D"application">Polkit</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D authfw=3Dshadow</code>: This swit=
ch
                enables the package to use the <span class=3D"application">=
Shadow</span> rather than the <span class=3D"application">Linux PAM</span> =
Authentication framework. Use
                it if you have not installed <span class=3D"application">Li=
nux
                PAM</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D introspection=3Dfalse</code>: Use=
 this
                option if you are certain that you do not need
                gobject-introspection files for polkit, or do not have
                installed <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromsc=
ratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#glib2" ti=
tle=3D"GLib-2.80.4">GLib-2.80.4</a> with GObject Introspection.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D man=3Dfalse</code>: Use this opti=
on to
                disable generating and installing manual pages. This is
