                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470534101408" name=3D"idm14047053410=
1408"></a>Automatic Startup
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  For the authentication framework to work, <span class=3D"=
command"><strong>polkit-gnome-authentication-agent-1</strong></span>
                  needs to be started. However, <span class=3D"command"><st=
rong>make install</strong></span> did not
                  install a startup file for the <span class=3D"application=
">Polkit GNOME</span> so you have to create it
                  by yourself.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Issue the following commands as the <code class=3D"system=
item">root</code> user to create a startup file for
                  <span class=3D"application">Polkit GNOME</span>:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -p /etc/xd=
g/autostart &amp;&amp;
cat &gt; /etc/xdg/autostart/polkit-gnome-authentication-agent-1.desktop &lt=
;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">[Desktop Entry]
Name=3DPolicyKit Authentication Agent
Comment=3DPolicyKit Authentication Agent
Exec=3D/usr/libexec/polkit-gnome-authentication-agent-1
Terminal=3Dfalse
Type=3DApplication
Categories=3D
NoDisplay=3Dtrue
OnlyShowIn=3DGNOME;XFCE;Unity;
AutostartCondition=3DGNOME3 unless-session gnome</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              </div>
