          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"dosfstools" name=3D"dosfstools"></a>dosfstools-4=
.2
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to dosfstools
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">dosfstools</span> package
                contains various utilities for use with the FAT family of
                file systems.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470533367264" name=3D"idm140470533367264"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://g=
ithub.com/dosfstools/dosfstools/releases/download/v4.2/dosfstools-4.2.tar.g=
z">
                      https://github.com/dosfstools/dosfstools/releases/dow=
nload/v4.2/dosfstools-4.2.tar.gz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 49c8e457327dc61efab5b115a27b087a
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 314 KB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 4.5 MB (with tests)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: less than 0.1 SBU
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"dosfstools-kernel" name=3D"dosfstools-kernel"></a>=
Kernel
                Configuration
              </h3>
              <p>
                Enable the following option in the kernel configuration and
                recompile the kernel if you need to mount a FAT-family
                filesystem:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"blue">F</span>ile system=
s ---&gt;
  <span class=3D"blue">D</span>OS/FAT/EXFAT/NT Filesystems ---&gt;
    &lt; /*/M&gt; M<span class=3D"blue">S</span>DOS fs support             =
                             [MSDOS_FS]
    &lt;*/M&gt;   <span class=3D"blue">V</span>FAT (Windows-95) fs support =
                              [VFAT_FS]</pre>
              <p>
                Note that <code class=3D"option">CONFIG_MSDOS_FS</code>
                deliberately does not support long file names. <code class=
=3D"option">CONFIG_VFAT_FS</code> should be used instead unless
                you really want to enforce the DOS-style <span class=3D"quo=
te">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D"quote">8.3</span>=E2=80=9D</span> file names.
              </p>
              <p>
                You can mount a FAT-family filesystem once the kernel
                supports it. If you don't need to create, check, or relabel=
 a
                FAT-family system, you may skip this package.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of dosfstools
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">dosfstools</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr            \
            --enable-compat-symlinks \
            --mandir=3D/usr/share/man  \
            --docdir=3D/usr/share/doc/dosfstools-4.2 &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-compat-symlinks</cod=
e></em>: This
                switch creates the <span class=3D"application">dosfsck</spa=
n>,
                <span class=3D"application">dosfslabel</span>, <span class=
=3D"application">fsck.msdos</span>, <span class=3D"application">fsck.vfat</=
span>, <span class=3D"application">mkdosfs</span>, <span class=3D"applicati=
on">mkfs.msdos</span>, and <span class=3D"application">mkfs.vfat</span> sym=
links required by some
                programs.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">fatlabel, fsck.fat, and
                    mkfs.fat</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
