                <a id=3D"idm140470532945312" name=3D"idm140470532945312"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                An <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#server-mail" tit=
le=3D"Chapter&nbsp;21.&nbsp;Mail Server Software">MTA</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"mdadm-kernel" name=3D"mdadm-kernel"></a>Kernel
                Configuration
              </h3>
              <p>
                Enable the following options in the kernel configuration an=
d
                recompile the kernel, if necessary. Only the RAID types
                desired are required.
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"blue">D</span>evice Driv=
ers ---&gt;
  [*] M<span class=3D"blue">u</span>ltiple devices driver support (RAID and=
 LVM) ---&gt;                   [MD]
    &lt;*/M&gt;   <span class=3D"blue">R</span>AID support                 =
                           [BLK_DEV_MD]
    [*]       <span class=3D"blue">A</span>utodetect RAID arrays during ker=
nel boot          [MD_AUTODETECT]
    # Only the RAID types desired are required:
    &lt; /*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">R</span>AID-0 (striping) mode       =
                             [MD_RAID0]
    &lt; /*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">R</span>AID-1 (mirroring) mode      =
                             [MD_RAID1]
    &lt; /*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">R</span>AID-10 (mirrored striping) m=
ode                         [MD_RAID10]
    &lt; /*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">R</span>AID-4/RAID-5/RAID-6 mode    =
                           [MD_RAID456]</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of mdadm
              </h3>
              <p>
                Build <span class=3D"application">mdadm</span> by running t=
he
                following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make</kbd></p=
re>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a working test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make BINDIR=3D/usr=
/sbin install</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>make
                everything</strong></span>: This optional target creates
