            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"nano" name=3D"nano"></a>Nano-8.1
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Nano
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">Nano</span> package contain=
s a
                small, simple text editor which aims to replace <span class=
=3D"application">Pico</span>, the default editor in the
                <span class=3D"application">Pine</span> package.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470531536528" name=3D"idm140470531536528"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://w=
ww.nano-editor.org/dist/v8/nano-8.1.tar.xz">https://www.nano-editor.org/dis=
t/v8/nano-8.1.tar.xz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 9eb581845590ad70ba89c04509c7a386
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 1.6 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 23 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.2 SBU
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Nano
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Nano</span> by running =
the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr     \
            --sysconfdir=3D/etc \
            --enable-utf8     \
            --docdir=3D/usr/share/doc/nano-8.1 &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install &amp;=
&amp;
install -v -m644 doc/{nano.html,sample.nanorc} /usr/share/doc/nano-8.1</kbd=
></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-utf8</code></em>: Th=
is
                switch enables unicode support in <span class=3D"applicatio=
n">Nano</span>.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring nano
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"nano-config" name=3D"nano-config"></a>Conf=
ig
                        Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/nanorc</code> and <code cla=
ss=3D"filename">~/.nanorc</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470531511520" name=3D"idm14047053151=
1520"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Example configuration (create as a system-wide <code clas=
s=3D"filename">/etc/nanorc</code> or a personal <code class=3D"filename">~/=
.nanorc</code> file)
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"screen"><code class=3D"literal">set autoinden=
t
set constantshow
set fill 72
set historylog
set multibuffer
set nohelp
set positionlog
set quickblank
set regexp</code></pre>
                <p>
                  Check the <code class=3D"filename">sample.nanorc</code> f=
ile
                  in the installed documentation directory. It includes col=
or
                  configurations and has some documentation included in the
                  comments.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Syntax highlighting is provided for several file types, i=
n
                  <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/nano/</code> director=
y.
                  E.g., for shell scripts, you can insert <code class=3D"op=
tion">include /usr/share/nano/sh.nanorc</code> in the
                  personal or global configuration file. If you wish
                  highlighting for all supported files, use <code class=3D"=
option">include /usr/share/nano/*.nanorc</code>. This
                  include does not descend into the <code class=3D"filename=
">extra</code> directory. Move required files one
                  level up.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">nano and rnano (symlink)</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Libraries:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">None</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Directories:</stro=
ng>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">/usr/share/nano and
                    /usr/share/doc/nano-8.1</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"variablelist">
                <h4>
                  <a id=3D"idm140470531498176" name=3D"idm140470531498176">=
</a>Short Descriptions
                </h4>
                <table border=3D"0" class=3D"variablelist">
                  <colgroup>
                    <col align=3D"left" valign=3D"top">
                    <col>
                  </colgroup>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"nano-prog" name=3D"nano-prog"></a><span =
class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>nano</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a small, simple text editor which aims to
                          replace <span class=3D"application">Pico</span>, =
the
                          default editor in the <span class=3D"application"=
>Pine</span> package
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"rnano-prog" name=3D"rnano-prog"></a><spa=
n class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>rnano</strong></span></spa=
n>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a restricted mode for <span class=3D"command">=
<strong>nano</strong></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
