                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"vim" name=3D"vim"></a>Vim-9.1.0660
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Vim
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">Vim</span> package, which i=
s an
                abbreviation for VI IMproved, contains a <span class=3D"com=
mand"><strong>vi</strong></span> clone with extra
                features as compared to the original <span class=3D"command=
"><strong>vi</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                The default LFS instructions install <span class=3D"applica=
tion">vim</span> as a part of the base system. If you
                would prefer to link <span class=3D"application">vim</span>
                against <span class=3D"application">X</span>, you should
                recompile <span class=3D"application">vim</span> to enable =
GUI
                mode. There is no need for special instructions since
                <span class=3D"application">X</span> support is automatical=
ly
                detected.
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  The version of vim changes daily. To get the latest
                  version, go to <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://github.=
com/vim/vim/releases">https://github.com/vim/vim/releases</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470531472368" name=3D"idm140470531472368"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://g=
ithub.com/vim/vim/archive/v9.1.0660/vim-9.1.0660.tar.gz">
                      https://github.com/vim/vim/archive/v9.1.0660/vim-9.1.=
0660.tar.gz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: c512a99b3704f193be1a181cc644b2b2
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 17 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 134 MB (add 74 MB for
                      tests)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.3 SBU (with parallelism=3D4; =
add
                      11 SBU for tests)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470531464896" name=3D"idm140470531464896"></=
a>Vim
                Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470531464208" name=3D"idm140470531464208"></=
a>Recommended
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#x-window-system" ti=
tle=3D"Chapter&nbsp;24.&nbsp;Graphical Environments">a graphical
                environment</a> and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.l=
inuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html=
#gtk3" title=3D"GTK+-3.24.43">GTK+-3.24.43</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470531461552" name=3D"idm140470531461552"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gpm" title=3D"GPM-1=
.20.7">GPM-1.20.7</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscrat=
ch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#lua" title=
=3D"Lua-5.4.7">Lua-5.4.7</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfr=
omscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#ruby"=
 title=3D"Ruby-3.3.4">Ruby-3.3.4</a>, and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https:/=
/www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunk=
s.html#rsync" title=3D"rsync-3.3.0">rsync-3.3.0</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Vim
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If you recompile <span class=3D"application">Vim</span> t=
o
                  link against <span class=3D"application">X</span> and you=
r
                  <span class=3D"application">X</span> libraries are not on=
 the
                  root partition, you will no longer have an editor for use
                  in emergencies. You may choose to install an additional
                  editor, not link <span class=3D"application">Vim</span>
                  against <span class=3D"application">X</span>, or move the
                  current <span class=3D"command"><strong>vim</strong></spa=
n>
                  executable to the <code class=3D"filename">/bin</code>
                  directory under a different name such as <code class=3D"f=
ilename">vi</code>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Vim</span> by running t=
he
                following commands:
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If you intend to run the tests and have not installed Xor=
g
                  in /usr, append LDFLAGS=3D'-L$XORG_PREFIX/lib' to the
                  configure line below.
                </p>
              </div>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">echo '#define=
 SYS_VIMRC_FILE  "/etc/vimrc"' &gt;&gt;  src/feature.h &amp;&amp;
echo '#define SYS_GVIMRC_FILE "/etc/gvimrc"' &gt;&gt; src/feature.h &amp;&a=
mp;

./configure --prefix=3D/usr        \
            --with-features=3Dhuge \
            --enable-gui=3Dgtk3    \
            --with-tlib=3Dncursesw &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If the global configuration file <code class=3D"filename"=
>/etc/vimrc</code> references the <code class=3D"envar">VIMRUNTIME</code> e=
nvironment variable, some tests
                  may complain about being unable to find the corresponding
                  directory and wait for user input. If this is the case,
                  this file should be saved and removed before running the
                  tests. Or if <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxf=
romscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#bubb=
lewrap" title=3D"Bubblewrap-0.9.0">bubblewrap-0.9.0</a> is installed, it's
                  also possible to create a lightweight container environme=
nt
                  where this file is hidden and run the tests in the
                  container.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make -j1 test</strong></span> Test
                failures, if any, will produce the file <code class=3D"file=
name">test.log</code> in <code class=3D"filename">src/testdir</code>. The r=
emaining tests will still
                be executed. If all goes well, the log will report
                <code class=3D"literal">ALL DONE</code>. Some tests labelle=
d as
                <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D"quote">flaky<=
/span>=E2=80=9D</span>
                may fail occasionally and can be ignored. The tests are kno=
wn
                to fail if the output is redirected to a file, and also if
                they are run in a 'screen' session.
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If running the tests with <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https=
://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochu=
nks.html#bubblewrap" title=3D"Bubblewrap-0.9.0">bubblewrap-0.9.0</a>
                  and <code class=3D"filename">/etc/vimrc</code> hidden, us=
e
                  <span class=3D"command"><strong>bwrap --dev-bind / /
                  --dev-bind /dev/null /etc/vimrc make -j1
                  test</strong></span>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  Some color tests expect to be executed under the
                  <span class=3D"command"><strong>xterm</strong></span>
                  terminal emulator.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
              <p>
                By default, Vim's documentation is installed in <code class=
=3D"filename">/usr/share/vim</code>. The following symlink
                allows the documentation to be accessed via <code class=3D"=
filename">/usr/share/doc/vim-9.1.0660</code>, making it
                consistent with the location of documentation for other
                packages:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ln -snfv ../vim/vi=
m91/doc /usr/share/doc/vim-9.1.0660</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"bold"><strong>If</strong></span> you wish to
                update the runtime files, issue the following command
                (requires <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromsc=
ratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#rsync" ti=
tle=3D"rsync-3.3.0">rsync-3.3.0</a>) to download it:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">rsync -avzcP =
--exclude=3D"/dos/" --exclude=3D"/spell/" \
    ftp.nluug.nl::Vim/runtime/ ./runtime/</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                And then install the updated runtime files and regenerate t=
he
                <code class=3D"filename">tags</code> file, as the <code cla=
ss=3D"systemitem">root</code> user issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make -C src i=
nstallruntime &amp;&amp;
vim -c ":helptags /usr/share/doc/vim-9.1.0660" -c ":q"</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-features=3Dhuge</code>=
</em>:
                This switch enables all the additional features available i=
n
                <span class=3D"application">Vim</span>, including support f=
or
                multibyte characters.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-tlib=3Dncursesw</code>=
</em>:
                This switch forces Vim to link against the <code class=3D"f=
ilename">libncursesw</code> library.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-gui=3Dno</code>: This will
                prevent compilation of the GUI. <span class=3D"application"=
>Vim</span> will still link against <span class=3D"application">X</span>, s=
o that some features such as the
                client-server model or the x11-selection (clipboard) are
                still available.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--without-x</code>: If you prefer no=
t to
                link <span class=3D"application">Vim</span> against
                <span class=3D"application">X</span>, use this switch.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-luainterp</code>, <code cla=
ss=3D"option">--enable-perlinterp</code>, <code class=3D"option">--enable-p=
ython3interp=3Ddynamic</code>, <code class=3D"option">--enable-tclinterp --=
with-tclsh=3Dtclsh</code>,
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-rubyinterp</code>: These
                options include the Lua, Perl, Python3, Tcl, or Ruby
                interpreters that allow using other application code in
                <span class=3D"application">vim</span> scripts. All the
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-*</code> options can accept
                <code class=3D"option">=3Ddynamic</code> to dynamically loa=
d the
                interpreter when needed. This is required for <span class=
=3D"application">Python 3</span> to prevent segmentation faults.
                For <span class=3D"application">tcl</span>, it is necessary=
 to
                indicate the name of the <span class=3D"command"><strong>tc=
lsh</strong></span> executable, since
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>configure</strong></span> o=
nly
                searches versioned names with old versions.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Vim
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"vim-config" name=3D"vim-config"></a>Config=
 Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/vimrc</code> and <code clas=
s=3D"filename">~/.vimrc</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"vim-init" name=3D"vim-init"></a>Configurat=
ion
                        Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <span class=3D"application">Vim</span> has an integrated
                  spell checker which you can enable by issuing the followi=
ng
                  in a vim window:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"screen"><code class=3D"literal">:setlocal spe=
ll spelllang=3Dru</code></pre>
                <p>
                  This setting will enable spell checking for the Russian
                  language for the current session.
                </p>
                <p>
                  By default, <span class=3D"application">Vim</span> only
                  installs spell files for the English language. If a spell
                  file is not available for a language, then <span class=3D=
"application">Vim</span> will call the <code class=3D"filename">$VIMRUNTIME=
/plugin/spellfile.vim</code> plugin
                  and will try to obtain the *.spl and optionally *.sug fro=
m
                  the vim ftp server, by using the <code class=3D"filename"=
>$VIMRUNTIME/plugin/netrwPlugin.vim</code>
                  plugin.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Alternatively you can manually download the *.spl and *.s=
ug
                  files from: <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"ftp://ftp.vim.org/=
