                Introduction to Apr
              </h3>
              <p>
                The Apache Portable Runtime (APR) is a supporting library f=
or
                the Apache web server. It provides a set of application
                programming interfaces (APIs) that map to the underlying
                Operating System (OS). Where the OS doesn't support a
                particular function, APR will provide an emulation. Thus
                programmers can use the APR to make a program portable acro=
ss
                different platforms.
              </p>
