m
                  locale; see <code class=3D"literal">LC_PAPER</code> in
                  <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://man.archlinux.org/man/=
locale.7">locale(7)</a>. If
                  you want to override it, create a <code class=3D"filename=
">papersize</code> file in the user configuration
                  directory. For example:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -pv ~=
/.config &amp;&amp;
echo "a4" &gt; ~/.config/papersize</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  If you want to override the paper size globally (for all
                  users), set up the <code class=3D"envar">PAPERSIZE</code>
                  environment variable. For example:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">echo "PAPER=
SIZE=3Da4" &gt; /etc/profile.d/libpaper.sh</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  You may use a different paper size, such as <code class=
=3D"literal">letter</code>.
                </p>
