              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to libsigsegv
              </h3>
              <p>
                libsigsegv is a library for handling page faults in user
                mode. A page fault occurs when a program tries to access to=
 a
                region of memory that is currently not available. Catching
                and handling a page fault is a useful technique for
                implementing pageable virtual memory, memory-mapped access =
to
                persistent databases, generational garbage collectors, stac=
k
                overflow handlers, and distributed shared memory.
              </p>
