                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RPATH=3DON</code></em>: This switch make=
s
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>cmake</strong></span> remov=
e
                hardcoded library search paths (rpath) when installing a
                binary executable file or a shared library. This package do=
es
                not need rpath once it's installed into the standard
                location, and rpath may sometimes cause unwanted effects or
                even security issues.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D JAS_ENABLE_DOC=3DNO</code>=
</em>:
                This option disables rebuilding the pdf documentation if
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#texlive" title=3D"t=
exlive-20240312-source">texlive-20240312</a> is installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                ALLOW_IN_SOURCE_BUILD=3DYES</code></em>: This switch allows
                building from within the source tree. In our case, this is
                needed to allow us to build inside of the BUILD directory
                instead of needing to create another directory outside of t=
he
                source tree.
              </p>
