            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of opencv
              </h3>
              <p>
                If you downloaded the optional modules, unpack them now:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">tar -xf ../op=
encv_contrib-4.10.0.tar.gz</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">opencv</span> by runnin=
g
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

cmake -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=3D/usr      \
      -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease       \
      -D ENABLE_CXX11=3DON                \
      -D BUILD_PERF_TESTS=3DOFF           \
      -D WITH_XINE=3DON                   \
      -D BUILD_TESTS=3DOFF                \
      -D ENABLE_PRECOMPILED_HEADERS=3DOFF \
      -D CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RPATH=3DON    \
      -D BUILD_WITH_DEBUG_INFO=3DOFF      \
      -W no-dev  ..                     &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                The package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RPATH=3DON</code></em>: This switch make=
s
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>cmake</strong></span> remov=
e
                hardcoded library search paths (rpath) when installing a
                binary executable file or a shared library. This package do=
es
                not need rpath once it's installed into the standard
                location, and rpath may sometimes cause unwanted effects or
                even security issues.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D WITH_XINE=3DON</code></em>=
: This
                option instructs the make procedure to use <a class=3D"xref=
" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-=
12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#xine-lib" title=3D"xine-lib-1.2.13">xine-lib-1.2.13=
</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                ENABLE_PRECOMPILED_HEADERS=3DOFF</code></em>: This option i=
s
                needed for compatibility with gcc-6.1 and later.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D
                OPENCV_EXTRA_MODULES_PATH=3D../opencv_contrib-4.10.0/module=
s</code>:
                instructs the build system to build additional modules.
              </p>
            </div>
