            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Poppler
              </h3>
              <p>
                Now, install <span class=3D"application">Poppler</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build  =
                       &amp;&amp;
cd    build                         &amp;&amp;

cmake -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease   \
      -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=3D/usr  \
      -D TESTDATADIR=3D$PWD/testfiles \
      -D ENABLE_QT5=3DOFF             \
      -D ENABLE_UNSTABLE_API_ABI_HEADERS=3DON \
      -G Ninja ..                   &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                In order to run the test suite, some testcases are needed a=
nd
                can be obtained only from a git repository. The command to
                download them is: <span class=3D"command"><strong>git clone
                --depth 1 https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/poppler/test.git
                testfiles</strong></span>. Then issue: <span class=3D"comma=
nd"><strong>LC_ALL=3Den_US.UTF-8 ninja
                test</strong></span>. One subtest of
                check_qt6_signature_basics is known to fail.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
              <p>
                To install the documentation, run the following commands as
                <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code>:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -m755 -=
d           /usr/share/doc/poppler-24.08.0 &amp;&amp;
cp -vr ../glib/reference/html /usr/share/doc/poppler-24.08.0</kbd></pre>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470523321760" name=3D"idm140470523321760"></=
a>Poppler Data
              </h4>
              <p>
                If you downloaded the additional encoding data package,
                install it by issuing the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">tar -xf ../..=
/poppler-data-0.4.12.tar.gz &amp;&amp;
cd poppler-data-0.4.12</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make prefix=3D/usr=
 install</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease</code></em>: This switch is used=
 to
                apply a higher level of compiler optimizations.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                TESTDATADIR=3D$PWD/testfiles</code></em>: Tells the test
                programs where the auxiliary files are located.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D ENABLE_QT5=3DOFF</code></e=
m>:
                This switch is needed to prevent an error when Qt5 is not
                installed. Remove it if you have installed <a class=3D"xref=
" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-=
12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#qt5-components" title=3D"qt5-components-5.15.14">qt=
5-components-5.15.14</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                ENABLE_UNSTABLE_API_ABI_HEADERS=3DON</code></em>: Installs =
some
                old <span class=3D"application">Xpdf</span> headers require=
d by
                certain programs.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D ENABLE_GTK_DOC=3DON</code>: Use t=
his
                parameter if GTK-Doc is installed and you wish to rebuild a=
nd
                install the API documentation.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D ENABLE_QT6=3DOFF</code>: Use this
                parameter if <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfro=
mscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#qt6" t=
itle=3D"Qt-6.7.2">Qt-6.7.2</a> is not installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D ENABLE_BOOST=3DOFF</code>: Use th=
is
                parameter if you have not installed <span class=3D"applicat=
ion">boost</span> (the Splash backend for Qt5
                recommends boost).
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D ENABLE_NSS3=3DOFF</code>: Use thi=
s
                parameter if you have not installed <span class=3D"applicat=
ion">nss</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D ENABLE_GPGME=3DOFF</code>: Use th=
is
                parameter if you have not installed <span class=3D"applicat=
ion">gpgme</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D ENABLE_LIBTIFF=3DOFF</code>: Use =
this
                parameter if you have not installed <span class=3D"applicat=
ion">libtiff</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>LC_ALL=3Den_US.UTF-8 ninja
                test</strong></span>: Runs the test suite. The environment
                variable LC_ALL=3Den_US.UTF-8 is only needed if the default
                locale does not include UTF-8.
              </p>
            </div>
