              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Graphviz
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">Graphviz</span> package
                contains graph visualization software. Graph visualization =
is
                a way of representing structural information as diagrams of
                abstract graphs and networks. <span class=3D"application">G=
raphviz</span> has several main graph layout
                programs. It also has web and interactive graphical
                interfaces, auxiliary tools, libraries, and language
                bindings.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470522627760" name=3D"idm140470522627760"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://g=
itlab.com/graphviz/graphviz/-/archive/12.1.0/graphviz-12.1.0.tar.bz2">
                      https://gitlab.com/graphviz/graphviz/-/archive/12.1.0=
/graphviz-12.1.0.tar.bz2</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 2c3ed90a06a2496c67b12ef3d5f93c5a
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 25 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 217 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.7 SBU (using parallelism=3D4)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470522620320" name=3D"idm140470522620320"></=
a>Graphviz Dependencies
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  Basic usage of <span class=3D"application">Graphviz</span=
>
                  does not require any libraries out of what is found in th=
e
                  LFS book. Its <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=
=3D"quote">core</span>=E2=80=9D</span> rendering engine is able to
                  generate several graphic formats, such as Postscript, SVG=
,
                  VML, .fig, and Tk. Those formats can be converted to almo=
st
                  any other format using tools from packages such as
                  <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.or=
g/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#imagemagick" titl=
e=3D"ImageMagick-7.1.1-36">ImageMagick-7.1.1-36</a>. The
                  dependencies below add the ability to generate graph imag=
es
                  in bitmap format, to display the graph image on screen, t=
o
                  edit a graph by viewing the resulting image directly, or =
to
                  view large graphs. Since <span class=3D"application">Grap=
hviz</span> is a dependency of several
                  other packages in this book, it is suggested that you fir=
st
                  build it without any dependencies, and then rebuild it wh=
en
                  you have built enough packages to suit your needs.
                </p>
              </div>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470522615280" name=3D"idm140470522615280"></=
a>Optional, for various bitmap outputs
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#pango" title=3D"Pan=
go-1.54.0">Pango-1.54.0</a>, with <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.lin=
uxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#c=
airo" title=3D"Cairo-1.18.0">Cairo-1.18.0</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"ht=
tps://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-no=
chunks.html#xorg7-lib" title=3D"Xorg Libraries">Xorg
                Libraries</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxf=
romscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#font=
config" title=3D"Fontconfig-2.15.0">Fontconfig-2.15.0</a>, and <a class=3D"=
xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-B=
OOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libpng" title=3D"libpng-1.6.43">libpng-1.6.43</=
a>, to generate images in
                bitmap SVG, postscript, PNG, and PDF formats, or to display
                the image on screen. The PNG output is required for buildin=
g
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gegl" title=3D"gegl=
-0.4.48">gegl-0.4.48</a>
              </p>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                Adding <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://download.gnome.or=
g/sources/gtk+/2.24/">GTK+-2</a>
                with <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch=
.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libjpeg" title=
=3D"libjpeg-turbo-3.0.1">libjpeg-turbo-3.0.1</a> adds support
                for JPEG, BMP, TIF, and ICO formats, and allows displaying
                the image in a GTK+ window
              </p>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://www.libgd.org/">GD Libra=
ry</a>
                may be used instead of <span class=3D"application">Pango</s=
pan>. It adds the ability to generate
                images in GIF, VRML, and GD formats, but <span class=3D"app=
lication">Pango</span> provides better outputs for the
                other formats, and is needed for displaying images
              </p>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                Other formats may be added with <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"h=
ttps://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-n=
ochunks.html#libwebp" title=3D"libwebp-1.4.0">libwebp-1.4.0</a> (WebP
                support is considered experimental), <a class=3D"ulink" hre=
f=3D"https://openil.sourceforge.net/projects.php">DevIL</a>,
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://sourceforge.net/projects=
/lasi/">libLASi</a>, and
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://www.freedesktop.org/wiki=
/Software/glitz">glitz</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470522600688" name=3D"idm140470522600688"></=
a>Optional (to load graphics that may
                be displayed inside the nodes of a graph)
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <code class=3D"filename">libgs.so</code> from <a class=3D"x=
ref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BO=
OK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gs" title=3D"ghostscript-10.03.1">ghostscript-10=
.03.1</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/=
downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#librsvg" title=3D"librsv=
g-2.58.3">librsvg-2.58.3</a>, and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.lin=
uxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#p=
oppler" title=3D"Poppler-24.08.0">Poppler-24.08.0</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470522596336" name=3D"idm140470522596336"></=
a>Optional (to build more tools)
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
