://www.joypixels.com/">EmojiOne</a>, and <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https:/=
/github.com/AyatanaIndicators/libdbusmenu">libdbusmenu</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of ibus
              </h3>
              <p>
                First, install the Unicode Character Database as the
                <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -p          =
     /usr/share/unicode/ucd &amp;&amp;
unzip -o ../UCD.zip -d /usr/share/unicode/ucd</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Fix an issue with deprecated schema entries:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -e 's@/de=
sktop/ibus@/org/freedesktop/ibus@g' \
    -i data/dconf/org.freedesktop.ibus.gschema.xml</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gtk-doc" title=
=3D"GTK-Doc-1.34.0">GTK-Doc-1.34.0</a> is not installed, remove
                the references to it:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">if ! [ -e /us=
r/bin/gtkdocize ]; then
  sed '/docs/d;/GTK_DOC/d' -i Makefile.am configure.ac
fi</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">ibus</span> by running =
the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">SAVE_DIST_FIL=
ES=3D1 NOCONFIGURE=3D1 ./autogen.sh &amp;&amp;

PYTHON=3Dpython3                     \
./configure --prefix=3D/usr          \
            --sysconfdir=3D/etc      \
            --disable-python2      \
            --disable-appindicator \
            --disable-emoji-dict   \
            --disable-gtk2         \
            --disable-systemd-services &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make -k check</strong></span>. The test
                named ibus-compose fails because it uses some locales not
                installed in LFS. The test named ibus-keypress will fail if
                running in a Wayland session.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-appindicator</code>=
</em>: This
                switch disables use of libdbusmenu. Omit if you installed t=
he
                optional dependency.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-emoji-dict</code></=
em>:
                This switch disables the use of emoticon dictionaries. Omit
                if you installed the optional package.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-gtk2</code></em>: T=
his
                switch removes the dependency on <span class=3D"application=
">GTK+-2</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-gtk4</code>: This switch
                enables building the <span class=3D"application">GTK 4</spa=
n>
                immodule. Use it if you have installed <span class=3D"appli=
cation">GTK 4</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-python-library</code>: This
                switch enables building the <span class=3D"application">Pyt=
hon</span> support library. Use it if you
                have installed the optional Python modules.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-wayland</code>: This switch
                enables building the <span class=3D"application">Wayland</s=
pan>
                support programs. It's automatically enabled if both
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libxkbcommon" title=
=3D"libxkbcommon-1.7.0">libxkbcommon-1.7.0</a> and <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#wayland" title=3D"Wayland-1.23.0">Wayland-1.23.0</a> are =
installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"envar">NOCONFIGURE=3D1</code>: Prevent
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>autogen.sh</strong></span> =
from
                running the generated <span class=3D"command"><strong>confi=
gure</strong></span> script. We'll run
                the script manually instead of relying on <span class=3D"co=
mmand"><strong>autogen.sh</strong></span> to run it,
                because <span class=3D"command"><strong>autogen.sh</strong>=
</span> would set
                <code class=3D"option">-fsanitize=3Daddress
                -fsanitize=3Dleak</code> in <code class=3D"envar">CFLAGS</c=
ode>
                running <span class=3D"command"><strong>configure</strong><=
/span>, but those
                compiler options are not suitable for productive use and th=
ey
                may also cause a build failure.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"envar">PYTHON=3Dpython3</code>: This environ=
ment
                variable makes the <span class=3D"command"><strong>configur=
e</strong></span> script look for
                <span class=3D"application">Python 3</span>. Use it if you =
want
                to build the <span class=3D"application">Python 3</span>
                support library.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"envar">SAVE_DIST_FILES=3D1</code>: This
                environment variable makes the <span class=3D"command"><str=
ong>autogen.sh</strong></span> script save some
                pre-generated header files instead of overwriting them when
                it is run. This prevents build failures when generating
                <code class=3D"filename">ibusemojigen.h</code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-gtk-doc</code>: Use this
                parameter if <span class=3D"application">GTK-Doc</span> is
                installed and you wish to rebuild and install the API
                documentation.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Ibus
              </h3>
              <p>
                If GTK+-3 is installed and <code class=3D"option">--disable=
-gtk3</code> is not used, the ibus IM
                module for GTK+-3 will be installed. As the <code class=3D"=
systemitem">root</code> user, update a cache file of GTK+-3
                so the GTK-based applications can find the newly installed =
IM
                module and use ibus as an input method:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">gtk-query-imm=
odules-3.0 --update-cache</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                The command above updates the cache file for GTK+-3. GTK-4
                does not require a cache file for IM modules.
              </p>
            </div>
