blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#linux-pam" title=3D=
"Linux-PAM-1.6.1">Linux-PAM-1.6.1</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of at
              </h3>
              <p>
                Before building <span class=3D"application">at</span>, as t=
he
                <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user you should crea=
te
                the group and user <code class=3D"systemitem">atd</code> wh=
ich
                will run the <span class=3D"command"><strong>atd</strong></=
span> daemon:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -g 17 atd=
                                                  &amp;&amp;
useradd -d /dev/null -c "atd daemon" -g atd -s /bin/false -u 17 atd</kbd></=
pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">at</span> with the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-with-daemon_username=3Datd        \
            --with-daemon_groupname=3Datd       \
            --with-jobdir=3D/var/spool/atjobs   \
            --with-atspool=3D/var/spool/atspool \
            SENDMAIL=3D/usr/sbin/sendmail       &amp;&amp;
make -j1</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make test</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install docdi=
r=3D/usr/share/doc/at-3.2.5 \
             atdocdir=3D/usr/share/doc/at-3.2.5</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring at
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"at-config" name=3D"at-config"></a>Config F=
iles
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/at.allow</code> and
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/at.deny</code> determines w=
ho
                  can submit jobs via at or batch.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470520991568" name=3D"idm14047052099=
1568"></a>Linux PAM Configuration
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  If <span class=3D"application">At</span> has been built w=
ith
                  <span class=3D"application">Linux PAM</span> support, you
                  need to create a <span class=3D"application">PAM</span>
                  configuration file, to get it working correctly with BLFS=
.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Issue the following commands as the <code class=3D"system=
item">root</code> user to create the configuration
                  file for <span class=3D"application">Linux PAM</span>:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/pa=
m.d/atd &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal"># Begin /etc/pam.d/atd

auth     required pam_unix.so
account  required pam_unix.so
password required pam_unix.so
session  required pam_unix.so

# End /etc/pam.d/atd</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
