              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of D-Bus
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">D-Bus</span> by running=
 the
                following commands (you may wish to review the output from
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>./configure
                --help</strong></span> first and add any desired parameters
                to the <span class=3D"command"><strong>configure</strong></=
span> command shown
                below):
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr                        \
            --sysconfdir=3D/etc                    \
            --localstatedir=3D/var                 \
            --runstatedir=3D/run                   \
            --disable-doxygen-docs               \
            --disable-xml-docs                   \
            --disable-static                     \
            --with-systemduserunitdir=3Dno         \
            --with-systemdsystemunitdir=3Dno       \
            --docdir=3D/usr/share/doc/dbus-1.14.10  \
            --with-system-socket=3D/run/dbus/system_bus_socket &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                See below for test instructions.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
              <p>
                If you are using a DESTDIR install, <span class=3D"command"=
><strong>dbus-daemon-launch-helper</strong></span>
                needs to be fixed afterwards. Issue, as <code class=3D"syst=
emitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">chown -v root:mess=
agebus /usr/libexec/dbus-daemon-launch-helper &amp;&amp;
chmod -v      4750       /usr/libexec/dbus-daemon-launch-helper</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you are still building your system in chroot or you did
                not start the daemon yet, but you want to compile some
                packages that require <span class=3D"application">D-Bus</sp=
an>,
                generate the <span class=3D"application">D-Bus</span> UUID =
to
                avoid warnings when compiling some packages with the
                following command as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</c=
ode>
                user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">dbus-uuidgen --ens=
ure</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If using <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscr=
atch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#elogind" t=
itle=3D"elogind-255.5">elogind-255.5</a>, create a symlink to the
                <code class=3D"filename">/var/lib/dbus/machine-id</code> fi=
le:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ln -sfv /var/lib/d=
bus/machine-id /etc</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Many tests are disabled unless both <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#dbus-python" title=3D"D-Bus Python-1.3.2">D-Bus
                Python-1.3.2</a> and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.=
linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.htm=
l#pygobject3" title=3D"PyGObject-3.48.2">PyGObject-3.48.2</a> have been
                installed. They must be run as an unprivileged user from a
                local session with bus address. To run the standard tests
                issue <span class=3D"command"><strong>make
                check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                If you want to run the unit regression tests, configure
                requires additional parameters which expose additional
                functionality in the binaries that are not intended to be
                used in a production build of <span class=3D"application">D=
-Bus</span>. If you would like to run the
                tests, issue the following commands (for the tests, you don=
't
                need to build the docs):
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make distclea=
n                                    &amp;&amp;
PYTHON=3Dpython3 ./configure --enable-tests         \
                           --enable-asserts       \
                           --disable-doxygen-docs \
                           --disable-xml-docs     &amp;&amp;
make                                              &amp;&amp;
make check</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                One test, test-autolaunch, is known to fail. There have als=
o
                been reports that the tests may fail if running inside a
                Midnight Commander shell. You may get out-of-memory error
                messages when running the tests. These are normal and can b=
e
                safely ignored.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-doxygen-docs</code>=
</em>: This
                switch disables doxygen documentation build and install, if
                you have <span class=3D"application">doxygen</span> install=
ed.
                If <span class=3D"application">doxygen</span> is installed,=
 and
                you wish to build them, remove this parameter.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-xml-docs</code></em=
>:
                This switch disables html documentation build and install, =
if
                you have <span class=3D"application">xmlto</span> installed=
. If
                <span class=3D"application">xmlto</span> is installed, and =
you
                wish to build them, remove this parameter.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-static</code></em>:
                This switch prevents installation of static versions of the
                libraries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-systemd{user,system}un=
itdir=3Dno</code></em>:
                These switches disable installation of systemd units on
                elogind based systems.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-system-socket=3D/run/d=
bus/system_bus_socket</code></em>:
                This parameter specifies the location of the system bus
                socket.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-tests</code></em>:
                Builds extra parts of the code to support all tests. Do not
                use on a production build.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-embedded-tests</code>: Buil=
ds
                extra parts of the code to support only unit tests. Do not
                use on a production build.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-asserts</code></em>:
                Enables debugging code to run assertions for statements
                normally assumed to be true. This prevents a warning that
                '<em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-tests</code></em>' =
on
                its own is only useful for profiling and might not give tru=
e
                results for all tests, but adds its own NOTE that this shou=
ld
                not be used in a production build.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring D-Bus
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"dbus-config" name=3D"dbus-config"></a>Conf=
ig
                        Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/dbus-1/session.conf</code>,
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/dbus-1/system.conf</code> a=
nd
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/dbus-1/system.d/*</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"dbus-session-config" name=3D"dbus-session-=
config"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  The configuration files listed above should probably not =
be
                  modified. If changes are required, you should create
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/dbus-1/session-local.conf</=
code> and/or
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/dbus-1/system-local.conf</c=
ode>
                  and make any desired changes to these files.
                </p>
                <p>
                  If any packages install a <span class=3D"application">D-B=
us</span> <code class=3D"filename">.service</code> file outside of the stan=
dard
                  <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/dbus-1/services</code=
>
                  directory, that directory should be added to the local
                  session configuration. For instance, <code class=3D"filen=
ame">/usr/local/share/dbus-1/services</code> can be
                  added by performing the following commands as the
                  <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/db=
us-1/session-local.conf &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">&lt;!DOCTYPE busconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD D-BUS Bus Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/busconfig.dtd"&gt;
&lt;busconfig&gt;

  &lt;!-- Search for .service files in /usr/local --&gt;
  &lt;servicedir&gt;/usr/local/share/dbus-1/services&lt;/servicedir&gt;

&lt;/busconfig&gt;</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"dbus-session" name=3D"dbus-session"></a>D-=
Bus
                        Session Daemon
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  To automatically start <span class=3D"command"><strong>db=
us-daemon</strong></span> when the
                  system is rebooted, install the <code class=3D"filename">=
/etc/rc.d/init.d/dbus</code> bootscript from the
                  <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.or=
g/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#bootscripts" titl=
e=3D"BLFS Boot Scripts">blfs-bootscripts-20240416</a> package.
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-dbu=
s</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  If this is the first time to install <span class=3D"appli=
cation">D-Bus</span> on the system and you are not
                  operating in a chroot environment, you can immediately
                  start <span class=3D"command"><strong>dbus-daemon</strong=
></span> without
                  rebooting the system:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">/etc/init.d=
/dbus start</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Note that this boot script only starts the system-wide
                  <span class=3D"application">D-Bus</span> daemon. Each use=
r
                  requiring access to <span class=3D"application">D-Bus</sp=
an>
                  services will also need to run a session daemon as well.
                  There are many methods you can use to start a session
                  daemon using the <span class=3D"command"><strong>dbus-lau=
nch</strong></span> command.
                  Review the <span class=3D"command"><strong>dbus-launch</s=
trong></span> man page for
                  details about the available parameters and options. Here
                  are some suggestions and examples:
                </p>
                <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                  <ul class=3D"compact">
                    <li class=3D"listitem">
                      <p>
                        Add <span class=3D"command"><strong>dbus-launch</st=
rong></span> to the
                        line in the <code class=3D"filename">~/.xinitrc</co=
de>
                        file that starts your graphical desktop environment=
.
                      </p>
                    </li>
                    <li class=3D"listitem">
                      <p>
                        If you use <span class=3D"command"><strong>gdm</str=
ong></span> or some other
                        display manager that calls the <code class=3D"filen=
ame">~/.xsession</code> file, you can add
                        <span class=3D"command"><strong>dbus-launch</strong=
></span> to the
                        line in your <code class=3D"filename">~/.xsession</=
code> file that starts your
                        graphical desktop environment. The syntax would be
                        similar to the example in the <code class=3D"filena=
me">~/.xinitrc</code> file.
                      </p>
                    </li>
                    <li class=3D"listitem">
                      <p>
                        The examples shown previously use <span class=3D"co=
mmand"><strong>dbus-launch</strong></span> to
                        specify a program to be run. This has the benefit
                        (when also using the <em class=3D"parameter"><code>=
--exit-with-x11</code></em>
                        parameter) of stopping the session daemon when the
                        specified program is stopped. You can also start th=
e
                        session daemon in your system or personal startup
                        scripts by adding the following lines:
                      </p>
                      <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command"><code=
 class=3D"literal"># Start the D-Bus session daemon
eval `dbus-launch`
export DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS</code></kbd></pre>
                      <p>
                        This method will not stop the session daemon when y=
ou
                        exit your shell, therefore you should add the
                        following line to your <code class=3D"filename">~/.=
bash_logout</code> file:
                      </p>
                      <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command"><code=
 class=3D"literal"># Kill the D-Bus session daemon
kill $DBUS_SESSION_BUS_PID</code></kbd></pre>
                    </li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
