          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"gpm" name=3D"gpm"></a>GPM-1.20.7
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to GPM
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">GPM</span> (General Purpose
                Mouse daemon) package contains a mouse server for the conso=
le
                and <span class=3D"command"><strong>xterm</strong></span>. =
It
                not only provides cut and paste support generally, but its
                library component is used by various software such as
                <span class=3D"application">Links</span> to provide mouse
                support to the application. It is useful on desktops,
                especially if following (Beyond) Linux From Scratch
                instructions; it's often much easier (and less error prone)
                to cut and paste between two console windows than to type
                everything by hand!
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470519916288" name=3D"idm140470519916288"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://a=
nduin.linuxfromscratch.org/BLFS/gpm/gpm-1.20.7.tar.bz2">
                      https://anduin.linuxfromscratch.org/BLFS/gpm/gpm-1.20=
.7.tar.bz2</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: bf84143905a6a903dbd4d4b911a2a2b8
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 820 KB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 7.4 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.1 SBU
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470519908880" name=3D"idm140470519908880"></=
a>Additional Downloads
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Required patch: <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/gpm-1.20.7-consolidated-1.patch">
                      https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/gp=
m-1.20.7-consolidated-1.patch</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470519906128" name=3D"idm140470519906128"></=
a>GPM
                Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470519905440" name=3D"idm140470519905440"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#texlive" title=3D"t=
exlive-20240312-source">texlive-20240312</a> (for
                documentation)
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"gpm-kernel" name=3D"gpm-kernel"></a>Kernel Configu=
ration
              </h3>
              <p>
                Enable the following option in the kernel configuration and
                recompile the kernel if necessary:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"blue">D</span>evice Driv=
ers ---&gt;
  <span class=3D"blue">I</span>nput device support ---&gt;
    -*-   <span class=3D"blue">G</span>eneric input layer (needed for keybo=
ard, mouse, ...)          [INPUT]
    &lt;*/M&gt;   M<span class=3D"blue">o</span>use interface              =
                       [INPUT_MOUSEDEV]</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of GPM
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">GPM</span> by running t=
he
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">patch -Np1 -i=
 ../gpm-1.20.7-consolidated-1.patch                &amp;&amp;
./autogen.sh                                                    &amp;&amp;
./configure --prefix=3D/usr --sysconfdir=3D/etc ac_cv_path_emacs=3Dno &amp;=
&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#texlive" title=
=3D"texlive-20240312-source">texlive-20240312</a> is installed,
                build the GPM manual as dvi, ps, and pdf formats:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make -C doc g=
pm.{dvi,ps} &amp;&amp;
dvipdfm doc/gpm.dvi -o doc/gpm.pdf</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install      =
                                    &amp;&amp;

install-info --dir-file=3D/usr/share/info/dir           \
             /usr/share/info/gpm.info                 &amp;&amp;

rm -fv /usr/lib/libgpm.a                              &amp;&amp;
ln -sfv libgpm.so.2.1.0 /usr/lib/libgpm.so            &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644 conf/gpm-root.conf /etc              &amp;&amp;

install -v -m755 -d /usr/share/doc/gpm-1.20.7/support &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644    doc/support/*                     \
                    /usr/share/doc/gpm-1.20.7/support &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644    doc/{FAQ,HACK_GPM,README*}        \
                    /usr/share/doc/gpm-1.20.7</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#texlive" title=
=3D"texlive-20240312-source">texlive-20240312</a> is installed
                and you've built GPM manual as dvi, ps, and pdf formats,
                install them as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code>
                user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -vm644 doc=
/gpm.{dvi,ps,pdf} /usr/share/doc/gpm-1.20.7</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>./autogen.sh</strong></span=
>:
                This command creates the missing <span class=3D"command"><s=
trong>configure</strong></span> script.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>ac_cv_path_emacs=3Dno</code><=
/em>:
                This variable works around an issue causing the package fai=
l
                to build with <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfr=
omscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#emacs=
" title=3D"Emacs-29.4">Emacs-29.4</a> installed. It also suppresses the
                installations of some <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span =
class=3D"quote">Emacs support files</span>=E2=80=9D</span> shipped with GPM=
.
                These files are quite outdated and they should be supersede=
d
                with <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch=
.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#emacs" title=
=3D"Emacs-29.4">Emacs-29.4</a> built-in GPM support. If you need
                to use <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscrat=
ch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#emacs" title=
=3D"Emacs-29.4">Emacs-29.4</a> in Linux console with mouse
                support, you should install (or reinstall) <a class=3D"xref=
" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-=
12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#emacs" title=3D"Emacs-29.4">Emacs-29.4</a> <span cl=
ass=3D"bold"><strong>after</strong></span> GPM.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>install-info
                ...</strong></span>: This package installs a <code class=3D=
"filename">.info</code> file, but does not update the system
                <code class=3D"filename">dir</code> file. This command make=
s
                the update.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>ln -v -sfn libgpm.so.2.1.0
                /usr/lib/libgpm.so</strong></span>: This command is used to
                create (or update) the <code class=3D"filename">.so</code>
                symlink to the library.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring GPM
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"gpm-init" name=3D"gpm-init"></a><span clas=
s=3D"phrase">Boot Script</span>
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Install the <code class=3D"filename">/etc/rc.d/init.d/gpm=
</code> init script included
                  in the <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscr=
atch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#bootscript=
s" title=3D"BLFS Boot Scripts">blfs-bootscripts-20240416</a> package.
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-gpm=
</kbd></pre>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"gpm-config" name=3D"gpm-config"></a>Config=
 Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/gpm-root.conf</code> and
                  <code class=3D"filename">~/.gpm-root</code>: The default =
and
                  individual user <span class=3D"command"><strong>gpm-root<=
/strong></span> configuration
                  files.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/sysconfig/mouse</code>: Thi=
s
                  file contains the name of your mouse device and the
                  protocol it uses. To create this file, run the following =
as
                  the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/sy=
sconfig/mouse &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal"># Begin /etc/sysconfig/mouse

MDEVICE=3D"<em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;yourdevice&gt;</code></em>"
PROTOCOL=3D"<em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;yourprotocol&gt;</code></em=
>"
GPMOPTS=3D"<em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;additional options&gt;</code=
></em>"

# End /etc/sysconfig/mouse</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470519844144" name=3D"idm14047051984=
4144"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Examples of values to set <code class=3D"envar">MDEVICE</=
code>, <code class=3D"envar">PROTOCOL</code>, and <code class=3D"envar">GPM=
OPTS</code> to are:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"screen"><code class=3D"literal">MDEVICE=3D"/d=
ev/input/mice"
PROTOCOL=3D"imps2"
GPMOPTS=3D""</code></pre>
                <p>
                  A list of which protocol values are known can be found by
                  running <span class=3D"command"><strong>gpm -m <em class=
=3D"replaceable"><code>[device]</code></em> -t
                  -help</strong></span>. The <code class=3D"envar">MDEVICE<=
/code> setting depends on which type of
                  mouse you have. For example, <code class=3D"filename">/de=
v/ttyS0</code> for a serial mouse (on Windows
                  this is COM1), <code class=3D"filename">/dev/input/mice</=
code> is often used for USB
                  mice and <code class=3D"filename">/dev/psaux</code> for P=
S2
                  mice. <code class=3D"envar">GPMOPTS</code> is the 'catch =
all'
                  for any additional options that are needed for your
                  hardware.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
