          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"power-profiles-daemon" name=3D"power-profiles-da=
emon"></a>Power-profiles-daemon-0.21
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Power-profiles-daemon
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">Power-profiles-daemon</span=
>
                package provides a program that allows modification of the
                system power/behavior state. This is used on many laptops a=
nd
                can be used by a Desktop Environment to activate power savi=
ng
                or performance CPU governors through dbus. On other systems=
,
                Power-profiles-daemon can be used as a streamlined way to s=
et
                the CPU governor in order to increase system performance at
                the cost of energy usage.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470519077536" name=3D"idm140470519077536"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://g=
itlab.freedesktop.org/upower/power-profiles-daemon/-/archive/0.21/power-pro=
files-daemon-0.21.tar.gz">
                      https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/upower/power-profiles-=
daemon/-/archive/0.21/power-profiles-daemon-0.21.tar.gz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 0196aae5798263d3d8f33a9280a6cb10
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 76 KB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 3.2 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: less than 0.1 SBU (with tests)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470519070048" name=3D"idm140470519070048"></=
a>Power-profiles-daemon Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470519069344" name=3D"idm140470519069344"></=
a>Required
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#polkit" title=3D"Po=
lkit-125">Polkit-125</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromsc=
ratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#pygobject=
3" title=3D"PyGObject-3.48.2">PyGObject-3.48.2</a>
                (pycairo is <span class=3D"bold"><strong>not</strong></span=
>
                needed), and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfro=
mscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#upower=
" title=3D"UPower-1.90.4">UPower-1.90.4</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470519065328" name=3D"idm140470519065328"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gtk-doc" title=3D"G=
TK-Doc-1.34.0">GTK-Doc-1.34.0</a>, The rest are for the
                tests, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscrat=
ch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#python-dbusm=
ock" title=3D"dbusmock-0.32.1">dbusmock-0.32.1</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#umockdev" title=3D"Umockdev-0.18.3">umockdev-0.18.3</a>,
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://github.com/PyCQA/isort">=
isort</a>, and <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://github.com/PyCQA/mccabe">=
mccabe</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"power-profiles-daemon-kernel" name=3D"power-profil=
es-daemon-kernel"></a>Kernel Configuration
              </h3>
              <p>
                Enable the following options in the kernel configuration an=
d
                recompile the kernel if necessary:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"blue">P</span>ower manag=
ement and ACPI options ---&gt;
  <span class=3D"blue">C</span>PU Frequency scaling ---&gt;
    -*-   <span class=3D"blue">C</span>PU Frequency scaling                =
                       [CPU_FREQ]
    -*-     '<span class=3D"blue">p</span>erformance' governor             =
       [CPU_FREQ_GOV_PERFORMANCE]
    &lt;*/M&gt;   '<span class=3D"blue">p</span>owersave' governor         =
               [CPU_FREQ_GOV_POWERSAVE]
    # Select if CPU is Intel:
    [ /*]   <span class=3D"blue">I</span>ntel P state control              =
               [X86_INTEL_PSTATE]
    # Select if CPU is AMD:
    [ /*]   <span class=3D"blue">A</span>MD Processor P-State driver       =
                 [X86_AMD_PSTATE]

<span class=3D"blue">D</span>evice Drivers ---&gt;
  # Some drivers under this submenu provide "platform profile" support
  # and power-profiles-daemon can take advantage from platform profiles;
  # select a driver if suitable for your platform:
  [ /*] <span class=3D"blue">X</span>86 Platform Specific Device Drivers --=
-&gt;         [X86_PLATFORM_DEVICES]</pre>
              <p>
                Select the appropriate sub-options that appear when the abo=
ve
                options are selected. As much as possible, the layout shoul=
d
                be the same as in kernel configuration menus.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Power-profiles-daemon
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Power-profiles-daemon</=
span> by running the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd build &amp;&amp;

meson setup                        \
      --prefix=3D/usr                \
      --buildtype=3Drelease          \
      -D gtk_doc=3Dfalse             \
      -D tests=3Dfalse               \
      -D systemdsystemunitdir=3D/tmp \
      .. &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have installed the external dependencies, to test th=
e
                results issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong>ninja
                test</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
              <p>
                Now, clean up an unneeded systemd unit installed into /tmp:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">rm -fv /tmp/power-=
profiles-daemon.service</kbd>
</pre>
              <p>
                Create a directory required for persistent power states aft=
er
                reboot:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -vdm755 /v=
ar/lib/power-profiles-daemon</kbd>
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D gtk_doc=3Dfalse</code></em=
>:
                Prevents building the documentation. Remove this if you hav=
e
                <span class=3D"application">GTK-Doc</span> installed and wi=
sh
                to build the documentation.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D tests=3Dfalse</code></em>:
                Prevents building the tests because they cannot be run with=
in
                the boundaries of BLFS. Remove this if you have installed t=
he
                external dependencies and wish to run the tests.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                systemdsystemunitdir=3D/tmp</code></em>: Removes the depend=
ency
                on <span class=3D"application">systemd</span>.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Power-profiles-daemon
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"power-profiles-daemon-init" name=3D"power-=
profiles-daemon-init"></a>Boot Script
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  To automatically start the <span class=3D"command"><stron=
g>power-profiles-daemon</strong></span>
                  when the system is rebooted, install the <code class=3D"f=
ilename">/etc/rc.d/init.d/power-profiles-daemon</code>
                  bootscript from the <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www=
.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.ht=
ml#bootscripts" title=3D"BLFS Boot Scripts">blfs-bootscripts-20240416</a> a=
s
                  the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-pow=
er-profiles-daemon</kbd></pre>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470519017968" name=3D"idm14047051901=
7968"></a>Select a Power Profile
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  To list all supported power profiles, issue:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">powerprofil=
esctl</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  To activate a power profile (for example <em class=3D"rep=
laceable"><code>performance</code></em>), issue:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">powerprofil=
esctl set <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>performance</code></em></kbd></pr=
e>
                <p>
                  Some desktop environments (for example GNOME and KDE) als=
o
                  provide a graphical interface to interact with <span clas=
s=3D"command"><strong>power-profiles-daemon</strong></span> and
                  activate a power profile.
                </p>
                <p>
                  The activated power profile is automatically stored in
                  <code class=3D"filename">/var/lib/power-profiles-daemon/s=
tate.ini</code>
                  and <span class=3D"command"><strong>power-profiles-daemon=
</strong></span>
                  will read it out and activate it again on the next boot i=
f
                  the <span class=3D"phrase">bootscript is installed</span>=
 as
                  above.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
