                  <colgroup>
                    <col align=3D"left" valign=3D"top">
                    <col>
                  </colgroup>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"which-prog" name=3D"which-prog"></a><spa=
n class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>which</strong></span></spa=
n>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          shows the full path of (shell) commands installed
                          in your <code class=3D"envar">PATH</code>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                The 'which' Script
              </h3>
              <p>
                The second option (for those who don't want to install the
                package) is to create a simple script (execute as the
                <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user):
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /usr/bin/=
which &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">#!/bin/bash
type -pa "$@" | head -n 1 ; exit ${PIPESTATUS[0]}</code>
EOF
chmod -v 755 /usr/bin/which
chown -v root:root /usr/bin/which</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This should work OK and is probably the easiest solution fo=
r
                most cases, but is not the most comprehensive implementatio=
n.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
