            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Doxygen
              </h3>
              <p>
                First, fix up some python scripts:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">grep -rl '^#!=
.*python$' | xargs sed -i '1s/python/&amp;3/'</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Doxygen</span> by runni=
ng
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -v buil=
d &amp;&amp;
cd       build &amp;&amp;

cmake -G "Unix Makefiles"          \
      -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease  \
      -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=3D/usr \
      -D build_wizard=3DON           \
      -D force_qt=3DQt6              \
      -W no-dev .. &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make tests</strong></span>. One test,
                012_cite.dox, is known to fail if <a class=3D"xref" href=3D=
"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv=
-nochunks.html#texlive" title=3D"texlive-20240312-source">texlive-20240312<=
/a> or <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/down=
loads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#tl-installer" title=3D"insta=
ll-tl-unx">install-tl-unx</a> is not installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                If you wish to generate the package documentation, you must
                have <span class=3D"application">Python</span>, <span class=
=3D"application">TeX Live</span> (for HTML docs) and
                <span class=3D"application">Ghostscript</span> (for PDF doc=
s)
                installed, then issue the following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cmake  -D bui=
ld_doc=3DON \
       -D DOC_INSTALL_DIR=3Dshare/doc/doxygen-1.12.0 \
       .. &amp;&amp;
make docs</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install &amp;=
&amp;
install -vm644 ../doc/*.1 /usr/share/man/man1</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have generated the package documentation, then the m=
an
                pages are automatically installed, and you do not need to r=
un
                the last <span class=3D"command"><strong>install
                ...</strong></span> command.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D build_wizard=3DOFF</code>: Use th=
is
                switch if <span class=3D"application">Qt6</span> is not
                installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D build_search=3DON</code>: Use thi=
s
                switch if <span class=3D"application">xapian</span> is
                installed and you wish to build external search tools
                (<span class=3D"command"><strong>doxysearch.cgi</strong></s=
pan>
                and <span class=3D"command"><strong>doxyindexer)</strong></=
span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D force_qt6=3DON</code>: Use this s=
witch
                to build <span class=3D"command"><strong>doxywizard</strong=
></span> with Qt6 even if
                Qt5 is installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D use_libclang=3DON</code>: Use thi=
s
                switch if <span class=3D"application">llvm</span> with
                <span class=3D"application">clang</span> are installed, to =
add
