              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470517588752" name=3D"idm140470517588752"></=
a>Dtc
                Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470517588064" name=3D"idm140470517588064"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libyaml" title=3D"l=
ibyaml-0.2.5">libyaml-0.2.5</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linu=
xfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#sw=
ig" title=3D"SWIG-4.2.1">SWIG-4.2.1</a>, and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"http=
s://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-noch=
unks.html#texlive" title=3D"texlive-20240312-source">texlive-20240312</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Dtc
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">dtc</span> by running t=
he
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup --prefix=3D/usr         \
            --buildtype=3Drelease   \
            -D python=3Ddisabled .. &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>meson test -v</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
              <p>
                Still as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user,
                remove the useless static library:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">rm /usr/lib/libfdt=
.a</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#texlive=
" title=3D"texlive-20240312-source">texlive-20240312</a> installed, you
                can build the PDF format of the documentation by issuing th=
e
                following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">pushd ../Docu=
mentation
  latexmk -bibtex --pdf dtc-paper &amp;&amp;
  latexmk -bibtex --pdf dtc-paper -c
popd</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To install the documentation, as the <code class=3D"systemi=
tem">root</code> user issue the following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cp -R ../Documenta=
tion -T /usr/share/doc/dtc-1.7.1</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have installed <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www=
.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.ht=
ml#swig" title=3D"SWIG-4.2.1">SWIG-4.2.1</a> and you wish to install the
                Python 3 binding of this package, build the Python 3 module=
:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">pip3 wheel -w=
 dist --no-build-isolation --no-deps --no-cache-dir ..</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                As the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user, install=
 the
                Python 3 module:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">pip3 install =
--no-index --find-links=3Ddist --no-cache-dir --no-user libfdt</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D python=3Ddisabled</code></=
em>:
                This switch prevents building the Python 3 binding with the
                deprecated method (running <span class=3D"command"><strong>=
setup.py</strong></span> directly). We will
                build the Python 3 binding with the <span class=3D"command"=
><strong>pip3 wheel</strong></span> command
                separately if wanted.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">convert-dtsv0, dtc, dtdiff,
                    fdtdump, fdtget, fdtoverlay, and fdtput</span>
