          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"gdb" name=3D"gdb"></a>GDB-15.1
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to GDB
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"application">GDB</span>, the GNU Project
                debugger, allows you to see what is going on <span class=3D=
"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D"quote">inside</span>=E2=80=9D</span> anothe=
r
                program while it executes -- or what another program was
                doing at the moment it crashed. Note that <span class=3D"ap=
plication">GDB</span> is most effective when tracing
                programs and libraries that were built with debugging symbo=
ls
                and not stripped.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470517332496" name=3D"idm140470517332496"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://f=
tp.gnu.org/gnu/gdb/gdb-15.1.tar.xz">https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gdb/gdb-15.1.ta=
r.xz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 494e3beaac44e66367c3e443a4414529
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 23 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 806 MB (add 1.0 GB for
                      docs; add 720 MB for tests)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.9 SBU (add 0.4 SBU for docs;
                      see below for tests; all using parallelism=3D8)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470517324848" name=3D"idm140470517324848"></=
a>GDB
                Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470517323696" name=3D"idm140470517323696"></=
a>Recommended Runtime Dependency
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#six" title=3D"six-1=
.16.0">six-1.16.0</a>
                (Python 3 module, required at run-time to use GDB scripts
                from various LFS/BLFS packages with Python 3 installed in
                LFS)
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470517321456" name=3D"idm140470517321456"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#doxygen" title=3D"D=
oxygen-1.12.0">Doxygen-1.12.0</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
gcc" title=3D"GCC-14.2.0">GCC-14.2.0</a> (ada, gfortran, and
                go are used for tests), <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://w=
ww.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.=
html#guile" title=3D"Guile-3.0.10">Guile-3.0.10</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#rust" title=3D"Rustc-1.80.1">rustc-1.80.1</a> (used for s=
ome tests),
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#valgrind" title=3D"=
Valgrind-3.23.0">Valgrind-3.23.0</a>, and <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https:=
//sourceware.org/systemtap/">SystemTap</a>
                (run-time, used for tests)
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of GDB
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">GDB</span> by running t=
he
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

../configure --prefix=3D/usr          \
             --with-system-readline \
             --with-python=3D/usr/bin/python3 &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Optionally, to build the API documentation using <a class=
=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BL=
FS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#doxygen" title=3D"Doxygen-1.12.0">Doxygen-1=
.12.0</a>, run:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make -C gdb/d=
oc doxy</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Running the tests is not recommended. The results vary a lo=
t
                depending on the system architecture and what optional
                dependencies are installed and what version of gcc is being
                used. On one system tested, there were 140 unexpected
                failures (out of over 108,000 tests) and on another system
                there were "only" 32 unexpected failures. The time to run t=
he
                tests varies from approximately 6 SBU to over 15 SBU when
                using -j8. This depends on number of tests that time out as
                will as other factors.
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon tip">
                <h3>
                  Tip
                </h3>
                <p>
                  With a plain <span class=3D"command"><strong>make
                  check</strong></span>, there are many warning messages
                  about a missing global configuration file. These can be
                  avoided by running <span class=3D"command"><strong>touch
                  global.exp</strong></span> and prepending the <span class=
=3D"command"><strong>make check</strong></span> command with
                  <span class=3D"command"><strong>DEJAGNU=3D$PWD/global.exp=
</strong></span>.
                  In addition the tests can be speeded up considerably by
                  using the <span class=3D"command"><strong>make</strong></=
span> option "-j&lt;N&gt;"
                  where &lt;N&gt; is the number of cores on your system.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                To test the results anyway, issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">pushd gdb/tes=
tsuite &amp;&amp;
make  site.exp      &amp;&amp;
echo  "set gdb_test_timeout 30" &gt;&gt; site.exp &amp;&amp;
make check 2&gt;1 | tee gdb-check.log
popd</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                See <span class=3D"emphasis"><em>gdb/testsuite/README</em><=
/span> and <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://sourceware.org/gdb/wiki/Testi=
ngGDB">TestingGDB</a>.
                There are many additional problems with the test suite:
              </p>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Clean directories are needed if re-running the tests.
                      For that reason, make a copy of the compiled source
                      code directory before the tests in case you need to r=
un
                      the tests again.
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Results depend on installed compilers.
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      On some AMD-based systems, over 200 additional tests
                      may fail due to a difference in the threading
                      implementation on those CPUs.
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make -C gdb instal=
l &amp;&amp;
make -C gdbserver install</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have built the API documentation, it is now in
                gdb/doc/doxy. You can install it (as the <code class=3D"sys=
temitem">root</code> user):
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -d /usr/sh=
are/doc/gdb-15.1 &amp;&amp;
rm -rf gdb/doc/doxy/xml &amp;&amp;
cp -Rv gdb/doc/doxy /usr/share/doc/gdb-15.1</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-system-readline</code>=
</em>: This
                switch forces <span class=3D"application">GDB</span> to use=
 the
                copy of <span class=3D"application">Readline</span> install=
ed
                in LFS.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-python=3D/usr/bin/pyth=
on3</code></em>:
                This switch forces <span class=3D"application">GDB</span> t=
o
                use Python 3.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">gcore, gdb, gdbserver, and
