            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Git
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Git</span> by running t=
he
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr \
            --with-gitconfig=3D/etc/gitconfig \
            --with-python=3Dpython3 &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                You can build the man pages and/or html docs, or use
                downloaded ones. If you choose to build them, use the next
                two instructions.
              </p>
              <p>
                If you have installed <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www=
.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.ht=
ml#asciidoc" title=3D"Asciidoc-10.2.1">asciidoc-10.2.1</a> you can create t=
he html
                version of the man pages and other docs:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make html</kb=
d></pre>
              <p>
                If you have installed <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www=
.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.ht=
ml#asciidoc" title=3D"Asciidoc-10.2.1">asciidoc-10.2.1</a> and <a class=3D"=
xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-B=
OOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#xmlto" title=3D"xmlto-0.0.29">xmlto-0.0.29</a> =
you can
                create the man pages:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make man</kbd=
></pre>
              <p>
                The test suite can be run in parallel mode. To run the test
                suite, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong>make test -k
                |&amp; tee test.log</strong></span>. If some test fails, th=
e
                list of failed tests can be shown via <span class=3D"comman=
d"><strong>grep '^not ok' test.log | grep -v
                TODO</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make perllibdir=3D=
/usr/lib/perl5/5.40/site_perl install</kbd></pre>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470517180512" name=3D"idm140470517180512"></=
a>If
                you created the man pages and/or html docs
              </h4>
              <p>
                Install the man pages as the <code class=3D"systemitem">roo=
t</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-man</=
kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install the html docs as the <code class=3D"systemitem">roo=
t</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make htmldir=3D/us=
r/share/doc/git-2.46.0 install-html</kbd></pre>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470517173344" name=3D"idm140470517173344"></=
a>If
                you downloaded the man pages and/or html docs
              </h4>
              <p>
                If you downloaded the man pages untar them as the
                <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">tar -xf ../git-man=
pages-2.46.0.tar.xz \
    -C /usr/share/man --no-same-owner --no-overwrite-dir</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you downloaded the html docs untar them as the
                <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -vp   /usr/s=
hare/doc/git-2.46.0 &amp;&amp;
tar   -xf   ../git-htmldocs-2.46.0.tar.xz \
      -C    /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0 --no-same-owner --no-overwrite-dir &a=
mp;&amp;

find        /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0 -type d -exec chmod 755 {} \; &amp;&a=
mp;
find        /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0 -type f -exec chmod 644 {} \;</kbd></=
pre>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470517166192" name=3D"idm140470517166192"></=
a>Reorganize text and html in the
                html-docs (both methods)
              </h4>
              <p>
                For both methods, the html-docs include a lot of plain text
                files. Reorganize the files as the <code class=3D"systemite=
m">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -vp /usr/sha=
re/doc/git-2.46.0/man-pages/{html,text}         &amp;&amp;
mv        /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0/{git*.txt,man-pages/text}     &amp;&amp=
;
mv        /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0/{git*.,index.,man-pages/}html &amp;&amp=
;

mkdir -vp /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0/technical/{html,text}         &amp;&amp=
;
mv        /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0/technical/{*.txt,text}        &amp;&amp=
;
mv        /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0/technical/{*.,}html           &amp;&amp=
;

mkdir -vp /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0/howto/{html,text}             &amp;&amp=
;
mv        /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0/howto/{*.txt,text}            &amp;&amp=
;
mv        /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0/howto/{*.,}html               &amp;&amp=
;

sed -i '/^&lt;a href=3D/s|howto/|&amp;html/|' /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0/how=
to-index.html &amp;&amp;
sed -i '/^\* link:/s|howto/|&amp;html/|' /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.0/howto-in=
dex.txt</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-gitconfig=3D/etc/gitco=
nfig</code></em>:
                This sets <code class=3D"filename">/etc/gitconfig</code> as=
 the
                file that stores the default, system wide, <span class=3D"a=
pplication">Git</span> settings.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-python=3Dpython3</code=
></em>: Use this
                switch to use <span class=3D"application">Python 3</span>,
                instead of the EOL'ed <span class=3D"application">Python
                2</span>. Python is used for the <span class=3D"command"><s=
trong>git p4</strong></span> interface to
                Perforce repositories, and also used in some tests.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-libpcre2</code>: Use this swi=
tch
                if <span class=3D"application">PCRE2</span> is installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>tar -xf
                ../git-manpages-2.46.0.tar.gz -C /usr/share/man
                --no-same-owner</strong></span>: This untars <code class=3D=
"filename">git-manpages-2.46.0.tar.gz</code>. The
                <code class=3D"option">-C</code> option makes tar change
                directory to <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/man</code>
                before it starts to decompress the docs. The <code class=3D=
"option">--no-same-owner</code> option stops tar from
                preserving the user and group details of the files. This is
                useful as that user or group may not exist on your system;
                this could (potentially) be a security risk.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>mv /usr/share/doc/git-2.46.=
0
                ...</strong></span>: These commands move some of the files
                into subfolders to make it easier to sort through the docs
                and find what you're looking for.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>find ... chmod
                ...</strong></span>: These commands correct the permissions
                in the shipped documentation tar file.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Git
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"git-config" name=3D"git-config"></a>Config=
 Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">~/.gitconfig</code> and <code cl=
ass=3D"filename">/etc/gitconfig</code>
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">git, git-receive-pack,
