            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of LLVM
              </h3>
              <p>
                Two additional tarballs <code class=3D"filename">llvm-cmake=
-18.src.tar.xz</code> and <code class=3D"filename">llvm-third-party-18.src.=
tar.xz</code> are needed
                by LLVM building system. The upstream expects them extracte=
d
                at the same level as the <code class=3D"filename">llvm-18.1=
.7.src.tar.xz</code> tarball, and the
                extracted directories renamed to <code class=3D"filename">c=
make</code> and <code class=3D"filename">third-party</code>. Extract them a=
nd modify the
                build system to avoid creating ambiguously-named directorie=
s
                outside the <code class=3D"filename">llvm-18.1.7.src</code>
                hierarchy:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">tar -xf ../ll=
vm-cmake-18.src.tar.xz                                   &amp;&amp;
tar -xf ../llvm-third-party-18.src.tar.xz                             &amp;=
&amp;
sed '/LLVM_COMMON_CMAKE_UTILS/s@../cmake@llvm-cmake-18.src@'          \
    -i CMakeLists.txt                                                 &amp;=
&amp;
sed '/LLVM_THIRD_PARTY_DIR/s@../third-party@llvm-third-party-18.src@' \
    -i cmake/modules/HandleLLVMOptions.cmake</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">clang</span> into the
                source tree by running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">tar -xf ../cl=
ang-18.1.7.src.tar.xz -C tools &amp;&amp;
mv tools/clang-18.1.7.src tools/clang</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have downloaded <span class=3D"application">compiler=
-rt</span>, install it into the source
                tree by running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">tar -xf ../co=
mpiler-rt-18.1.7.src.tar.xz -C projects    &amp;&amp;
mv projects/compiler-rt-18.1.7.src projects/compiler-rt</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                There are many Python scripts in this package which use
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>/usr/bin/env
                python</strong></span> to access the system Python which on
                LFS is <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscrat=
ch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#python3" tit=
le=3D"Python-3.12.5">Python-3.12.5</a>. Use the following command
                to fix these scripts:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">grep -rl '#!.=
*python' | xargs sed -i '1s/python$/python3/'</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Ensure installing the <span class=3D"command"><strong>FileC=
heck</strong></span> program which is
                needed by the test suite of some packages (for example
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#rust" title=3D"Rust=
c-1.80.1">rustc-1.80.1</a>):
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed 's/utilit=
y/tool/' -i utils/FileCheck/CMakeLists.txt</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">LLVM</span> by running =
the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -v buil=
d &amp;&amp;
cd       build &amp;&amp;

CC=3Dgcc CXX=3Dg++                               \
cmake -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=3D/usr           \
      -D CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RPATH=3DON         \
      -D LLVM_ENABLE_FFI=3DON                  \
      -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease            \
      -D LLVM_BUILD_LLVM_DYLIB=3DON            \
      -D LLVM_LINK_LLVM_DYLIB=3DON             \
      -D LLVM_ENABLE_RTTI=3DON                 \
      -D LLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD=3D"host;AMDGPU" \
      -D LLVM_BINUTILS_INCDIR=3D/usr/include   \
      -D LLVM_INCLUDE_BENCHMARKS=3DOFF         \
      -D CLANG_DEFAULT_PIE_ON_LINUX=3DON       \
      -D CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_DIR=3D/etc/clang \
      -W no-dev -G Ninja ..                  &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you wish to run the tests, remove a test case known to
                hang indefinitely on some systems:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">rm -f ../proj=
ects/compiler-rt/test/tsan/getline_nohang.cpp</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                LLVM test suite can produce many core dump files. They will
                occupy a large amount of disk space, and the core dump
                process can significantly slow down the testing. To test th=
e
                results with core dump disabled, issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sh -c 'ulimit=
 -c 0 &amp;&amp; ninja check-all'</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If <code class=3D"option">-jN</code> (N replaced with a num=
ber)
                is passed to <span class=3D"command"><strong>ninja</strong>=
</span>, the tests will be
                built with N logical cores, but run using all available
                logical cores. Run the test command in a cgroup ( read
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#build-in-cgroup" ti=
tle=3D"Use Linux Control Group to Limit the Resource Usage">the
                section called =E2=80=9CUse Linux Control Group to Limit th=
e Resource
                Usage=E2=80=9D</a> for details) to limit the number of logi=
cal cores
                for running the tests. Two tests related to <code class=3D"=
filename">TestCases/Linux/printf-fortify-5.c</code> are
                known to fail with Glibc-2.40 or newer. One test named
                <code class=3D"filename">Linux/clone_setns.cpp</code> will =
fail
                if <code class=3D"option">CONFIG_USER_NS</code> is not enab=
led
                in kernel configuration.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RPATH=3DON</code></em>: This switch make=
s
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>cmake</strong></span> remov=
e
                hardcoded library search paths (rpath) when installing a
                binary executable file or a shared library. This package do=
es
                not need rpath once it's installed into the standard
                location, and rpath may sometimes cause unwanted effects or
                even security issues.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                LLVM_ENABLE_FFI=3DON</code></em>: This switch allows
                <span class=3D"application">LLVM</span> to use <span class=
=3D"application">libffi</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                LLVM_BUILD_LLVM_DYLIB=3DON</code></em>: This switch builds =
the
                libraries as static and links all of them into an unique
                shared one. This is the recommended way of building a share=
d
                library.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease</code></em>: This switch enables
                compiler optimizations in order to speed up the code and
                reduce its size. It also disables some compile checks which
                are not necessary on a production system.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                LLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD=3D"host;AMDGPU"</code></em>: This swi=
tch
                enables building for the same target as the host, and also
                for the r600 AMD GPU used by the Mesa r600 and radeonsi
                drivers. The default is all of the targets. You can use a
                semicolon separated list. Valid targets are: host, AArch64,
                AMDGPU, ARM, AVR, BPF, Hexagon, Lanai, LoongArch, Mips,
                MSP430, NVPTX, PowerPC, RISCV, Sparc, SystemZ, SystemZ, VE,
                WebAssembly, X86, XCore, or all.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                LLVM_LINK_LLVM_DYLIB=3DON</code></em>: Used in conjunction =
with
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                LLVM_BUILD_LLVM_DYLIB=3DON</code></em>, this switch enables
                linking the tools against the shared library instead of the
                static ones. It slightly reduces their size and also ensure=
s
                that llvm-config will correctly use libLLVM-18.so.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                LLVM_ENABLE_RTTI=3DON</code></em>: This switch is used to b=
uild
                LLVM with run-time type information. This is required for
                building <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscr=
atch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#mesa" titl=
e=3D"Mesa-24.1.5">Mesa-24.1.5</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                LLVM_BINUTILS_INCDIR=3D/usr/include</code></em>: This switc=
h is
                used to tell the build system the location of binutils
                headers, which were installed in LFS. This allows the
                building of <code class=3D"filename">LLVMgold.so</code>, wh=
ich
                is needed for building programs with <span class=3D"command=
"><strong>clang</strong></span> and Link Time
                Optimization (LTO).
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                LLVM_INCLUDE_BENCHMARKS=3DOFF</code></em>: is used to disab=
le
                generation build targets for the LLVM benchmarks. This opti=
on
                requires additional code that is not currently available.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                CLANG_DEFAULT_PIE_ON_LINUX=3DON</code></em>: makes <code cl=
ass=3D"option">-fpie</code> option the default when compiling
                programs. Together with the <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https=
://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochu=
nks.html#gASLR" title=3D"ASLR"><acronym class=3D"acronym">ASLR</acronym></a=
>
                feature enabled in the kernel, this defeats some kind of
                attacks based on known memory layouts.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_DIR=3D/etc/clang</code></em>: make=
s
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>clang</strong></span> and
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>clang++</strong></span> sea=
rch
                <code class=3D"filename">/etc/clang</code> for configuratio=
n
                files.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=3DON</code>: if=
 used
                instead of <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                LLVM_BUILD_LLVM_DYLIB=3DON</code></em> and <em class=3D"par=
ameter"><code>-D LLVM_LINK_LLVM_DYLIB=3DON</code></em>,
                builds all the <span class=3D"application">LLVM</span>
                libraries (about 60) as shared libraries instead of static.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D LLVM_ENABLE_DOXYGEN</code>: Enabl=
es
                the generation of browsable HTML documentation if you have
                installed <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromsc=
ratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#doxygen" =
title=3D"Doxygen-1.12.0">Doxygen-1.12.0</a>. You should run
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>make
                doxygen-html</strong></span> afterwards, and install the
                generated documentation manually.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring LLVM
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"llvm-config-info" name=3D"llvm-config-info=
"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  If you've built Clang, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">=
root</code> user create two configuration
                  files to make <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linux=
fromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gSS=
P" title=3D"SSP"><acronym class=3D"acronym">SSP</acronym></a> enabled by
                  default for <span class=3D"command"><strong>clang</strong=
></span> and <span class=3D"command"><strong>clang++</strong></span>, so th=
e default
                  configuration of their SSP feature will be consistent wit=
h
                  <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.or=
g/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gcc" title=3D"GCC=
-14.2.0">GCC-14.2.0</a>:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -pv /etc/c=
lang &amp;&amp;
for i in clang clang++; do
  echo -fstack-protector-strong &gt; /etc/clang/$i.cfg
done</kbd></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
