            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Lua 5.2
              </h3>
              <p>
                Some packages check for the <span class=3D"application">pkg=
-config</span> file for <span class=3D"application">Lua</span>, which is cr=
eated with:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; lua.=
pc &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">V=3D5.2
R=3D5.2.4

prefix=3D/usr
INSTALL_BIN=3D${prefix}/bin
INSTALL_INC=3D${prefix}/include/lua5.2
INSTALL_LIB=3D${prefix}/lib
INSTALL_MAN=3D${prefix}/share/man/man1
INSTALL_LMOD=3D${prefix}/share/lua/${V}
INSTALL_CMOD=3D${prefix}/lib/lua/${V}
exec_prefix=3D${prefix}
libdir=3D${exec_prefix}/lib
includedir=3D${prefix}/include/lua5.2

Name: Lua
Description: An Extensible Extension Language
Version: ${R}
Requires:
Libs: -L${libdir} -llua5.2 -lm -ldl
Cflags: -I${includedir}</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Lua</span> by running t=
he
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">patch -Np1 -i=
 ../lua-5.2.4-shared_library-1.patch &amp;&amp;

sed -i '/#define LUA_ROOT/s:/usr/local/:/usr/:' src/luaconf.h &amp;&amp;

sed -r -e '/^LUA_(SO|A|T)=3D/ s/lua/lua5.2/' \
       -e '/^LUAC_T=3D/ s/luac/luac5.2/'     \
       -i src/Makefile &amp;&amp;

make MYCFLAGS=3D"-fPIC" linux</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                The installation of this package is complex, so we will use
                the DESTDIR method of installation:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make TO_BIN=
=3D'lua5.2 luac5.2'                     \
     TO_LIB=3D"liblua5.2.so liblua5.2.so.5.2 liblua5.2.so.5.2.4" \
     INSTALL_DATA=3D"cp -d"                        \
     INSTALL_TOP=3D$PWD/install/usr                \
     INSTALL_INC=3D$PWD/install/usr/include/lua5.2 \
     INSTALL_MAN=3D$PWD/install/usr/share/man/man1 \
     install &amp;&amp;

install -Dm644 lua.pc install/usr/lib/pkgconfig/lua52.pc &amp;&amp;

mkdir -pv install/usr/share/doc/lua-5.2.4 &amp;&amp;
cp -v doc/*.{html,css,gif,png} install/usr/share/doc/lua-5.2.4 &amp;&amp;

ln -s liblua5.2.so install/usr/lib/liblua.so.5.2   &amp;&amp;
ln -s liblua5.2.so install/usr/lib/liblua.so.5.2.4 &amp;&amp;

mv install/usr/share/man/man1/{lua.1,lua5.2.1} &amp;&amp;
mv install/usr/share/man/man1/{luac.1,luac5.2.1}</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">chown -R root:root=
 install  &amp;&amp;
cp -a install/* /</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sed -i ...
                src/luaconf.h</strong></span>: This command changes the
                <span class=3D"application">Lua</span> search path to match=
 the
                install path.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sed -i ...
                src/Makefile</strong></span>: This command deconflicts this
                installation with the latest version of lua.
              </p>
