            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Python 3
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Python 3</span> by runn=
ing
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">CXX=3D"/usr/b=
in/g++"               \
./configure --prefix=3D/usr        \
            --enable-shared      \
            --with-system-expat  \
            --enable-optimizations &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Some tests are known to occasionally hang indefinitely. So =
to
                test the results, run the test suite but set a 2-minute tim=
e
                limit for each test case:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make test TES=
TOPTS=3D"--timeout 120"</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                For a relatively slow system you may need to increase the
                time limit and 1 SBU (measured when building Binutils pass =
1
                with one CPU core) should be enough. Some tests are flaky, =
so
                the test suite will automatically re-run failed tests. If a
                test failed but then passed when re-run, it should be
                considered as passed.
              </p>
              <p>
                Of over 42,000 tests, the following are known to fail:
                test__xxsubinterpreters, test_import, test_interpreters, an=
d
                test_threading.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
              <p>
                If upgrading and the documentation has been downloaded,
                optionally install it as the <code class=3D"systemitem">roo=
t</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -dm755 =
/usr/share/doc/python-3.12.5/html

tar --strip-components=3D1  \
    --no-same-owner       \
    --no-same-permissions \
    -C /usr/share/doc/python-3.12.5/html \
    -xvf ../python-3.12.5-docs-html.tar.bz2</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>CXX=3D"/usr/bin/g++" ./conf=
igure
                ...</strong></span>: Avoid an annoying message during
                configuration.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-system-expat</code></e=
m>:
                This switch enables linking against the system version of
                <span class=3D"application">Expat</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-optimizations</code>=
</em>: This
                switch enables stable, but expensive, optimizations.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-lto</code>: This optional swi=
tch
                enables thick Link Time Optimization. Unusually, it creates=
 a
                much larger <code class=3D"filename">/usr/lib/python3.12/co=
nfig-3.12-&lt;arch&gt;-linux-gnu/libpython3.12.a</code>
                with a small increase in the time to compile <span class=3D=
"application">Python</span>. Run-time results do not appear
                to show any benefit from doing this.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Python 3
              </h3>
              <p>
                In order for <span class=3D"command"><strong>python3</stron=
g></span> to find the
                installed documentation, create the following version
                independent symlink:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ln -svfn python-3.=
12.5 /usr/share/doc/python-3</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                and add the following environment variable to the individua=
l
                user's or system's profile:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">export PYTHONDOCS=
=3D/usr/share/doc/python-3/html</kbd></pre>
            </div>
