                <a id=3D"idm140470512873712" name=3D"idm140470512873712"></=
a>Python 3.11 Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470512873008" name=3D"idm140470512873008"></=
a>Recommended
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#sqlite" title=3D"SQ=
Lite-3.46.1">SQLite-3.46.1</a> (required if building
                firefox or thunderbird)
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Python 3.11
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Python 3.11</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">CXX=3D"/usr/b=
in/g++"                     \
./configure --prefix=3D/opt/python3.11   \
            --disable-shared           \
            --with-system-expat        &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Since this package is only used in very limited situations,
                tests are not recommended.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>CXX=3D"/usr/bin/g++" ./conf=
igure
                ...</strong></span>: Avoid an annoying message during
                configuration.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--prefix=3D/opt/python3.11</c=
ode></em>: This
                installs python 3.11 into /opt in order to avoid conflicts
                with the system version of python, and allows for easy
                removal/isolation once programs update to python3.12 or
                later.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-shared</code></em>:
                This switch disables building shared libraries. Since all t=
he
                packages that need python-3.11 have built in modules and
                don't directly link to python, it is safe to turn off share=
d
                library support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-system-expat</code></e=
m>:
                This switch enables linking against the system version of
                <span class=3D"application">Expat</span>.
              </p>
            </div>
