            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Subversion
              </h3>
              <p>
                First, adapt some Python scripts to use python3:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">grep -rl '^#!=
.*python$' | xargs sed -i '1s/python/&amp;3/'</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Next, fix building this package with GCC 14:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">patch -Np1 -i=
 ../subversion-1.14.3-upstream_fixes-1.patch</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                After modifying the SWIG bindings like we did with the patc=
h,
                the build system must be regenerated so the bindings pick u=
p
                the changes:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">touch build/g=
enerator/swig/*.py &amp;&amp;
mv -v build-outputs.mk{,.old}   &amp;&amp;
./autogen.sh --release</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Subversion</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">PYTHON=3Dpyth=
on3                        \
./configure --prefix=3D/usr             \
            --disable-static          \
            --with-apache-libexecdir  \
            --with-utf8proc=3Dinternal &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#doxygen=
" title=3D"Doxygen-1.12.0">Doxygen-1.12.0</a> installed and you wish to
                build the API documentation, issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">doxygen doc/d=
oxygen.conf</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you wish to build the Java bindings pass the <code class=
=3D"option">--enable-javahl</code> parameter to the <span class=3D"command"=
><strong>configure</strong></span> command. In
                addition, if you want to run the Java test suite, you have =
to
                specify the location of the <span class=3D"application">JUn=
it</span> file by adding <code class=3D"option">--with-junit=3D&lt;path to =
junit jar&gt;</code> (for
                instance <code class=3D"option">--with-junit=3D/usr/local/j=
ava/lib/junit-4.13.jar</code>)
                to <span class=3D"command"><strong>configure</strong></span=
>.
                The JUnit jar file is no longer included in <a class=3D"xre=
f" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK=
-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#apache-ant" title=3D"apache-ant-1.10.14">apache-an=
t-1.10.14</a> and must be
                downloaded separately. To build the Java bindings, issue th=
e
                following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"command"><strong>make -j=
1 javahl</strong></span></pre>
              <p>
                If you want to compile <span class=3D"application">Perl</sp=
an>,
                <span class=3D"application">Python</span>, or <span class=
=3D"application">Ruby</span> bindings, issue any of the
                following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"command"><strong>make sw=
ig-pl</strong></span> # for <span class=3D"application">Perl</span>
<span class=3D"command"><strong>make swig-py \
     swig_pydir=3D/usr/lib/python3.12/site-packages/libsvn \
     swig_pydir_extra=3D/usr/lib/python3.12/site-packages/svn</strong></spa=
n> # for <span class=3D"application">Python</span>
<span class=3D"command"><strong>make swig-rb</strong></span> # for <span cl=
ass=3D"application">Ruby</span></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make check</strong></span>. Four tests in
                the <code class=3D"filename">commit_tests.py</code>,
                <code class=3D"filename">prop_tests.py</code>, and <code cl=
ass=3D"filename">update_tests.py</code> suites are known to fail.
                Due to changes in Python-3.12, you can expect to see around
                200 Syntax Warnings during the test suite due to invalid
                escape sequences.
              </p>
              <p>
                To test the results of any of the <span class=3D"applicatio=
n">SWIG</span> bindings, you can use any of the
                following commands: <span class=3D"command"><strong>make
                check-swig-pl</strong></span>, <span class=3D"command"><str=
ong>make check-swig-py</strong></span>, or
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>make
                check-swig-rb</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install &amp;=
&amp;

install -v -m755 -d /usr/share/doc/subversion-1.14.3 &amp;&amp;
cp      -v -R doc/* /usr/share/doc/subversion-1.14.3</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you built the Java bindings, issue the following command
                as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user to insta=
ll
                them:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"command"><strong>make in=
stall-javahl</strong></span></pre>
              <p>
                If you built the <span class=3D"application">Perl</span>,
                <span class=3D"application">Python</span>, or <span class=
=3D"application">Ruby</span> bindings, issue any of the
                following commands as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</=
code> user to install them:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"command"><strong>make in=
stall-swig-pl</strong></span>
<span class=3D"command"><strong>make install-swig-py \
      swig_pydir=3D/usr/lib/python3.12/site-packages/libsvn \
      swig_pydir_extra=3D/usr/lib/python3.12/site-packages/svn</strong></sp=
an>
<span class=3D"command"><strong>make install-swig-rb</strong></span></pre>
              <p>
                The java bindings need to be installed in order for the tes=
ts
                to run, since the tests attempt to look for them in
                CLASSPATH. To test the results of the Java bindings build,
                issue <span class=3D"command"><strong>LANG=3DC make
                check-javahl</strong></span>.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-static</code></em>:
                This switch prevents installation of static versions of the
                libraries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-apache-libexecdir</cod=
e></em>: If
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#apache" title=3D"Ap=
ache-2.4.62">Apache-2.4.62</a> is installed, the shared
                <span class=3D"application">Apache</span> modules are built=
.
                This switch allows to have those modules installed to
                <span class=3D"application">Apache</span>'s configured modu=
le
                dir instead of <code class=3D"filename">/usr/libexec</code>=
. It
                has no effect if <span class=3D"application">Apache</span> =
is
                not installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-utf8proc=3Dinternal</c=
ode></em>:
                Remove these switches if you have installed the optional
                dependencies.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-javahl</code>: enables
                compilation of Java high level bindings. Running <span clas=
s=3D"command"><strong>make javahl</strong></span> is necessary to
                do the compilation.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-junit=3D&lt;location of the j=
unit
                jar file&gt;</code>: gives the location of the junit jar,
                otherwise the javahl tests cannot be run.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--disable-gmock</code>: Do not use t=
he
                Googlemock testing framework.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Subversion
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"subversion-config" name=3D"subversion-conf=
ig"></a>Config Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">~/.subversion/config</code> and
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/subversion/config</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470508703728" name=3D"idm14047050870=
3728"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/subversion/config</code> is=
 the
                  <span class=3D"application">Subversion</span> system-wide
                  configuration file. This file is used to specify defaults
                  for different <span class=3D"command"><strong>svn</strong=
></span> commands.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">~/.subversion/config</code> is t=
he
                  user's personal configuration file. It is used to overrid=
e
                  the system-wide defaults set in <code class=3D"filename">=
/etc/subversion/config</code>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
