blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#DocBook" title=3D"d=
ocbook-xml-4.5">docbook-xml-4.5</a> (for tests), <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"=
https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-=
nochunks.html#gdb" title=3D"GDB-15.1">GDB-15.1</a> (for tests),
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#llvm" title=3D"LLVM=
-18.1.7">LLVM-18.1.7</a> (with Clang), and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https:=
//www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochun=
ks.html#which" title=3D"Which-2.21 and Alternatives">Which-2.21</a> (for te=
sts)
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Valgrind
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Valgrind</span> by runn=
ing
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -i 's|/do=
c/valgrind||' docs/Makefile.in &amp;&amp;

./configure --prefix=3D/usr \
            --datadir=3D/usr/share/doc/valgrind-3.23.0 &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make regtest</strong></span>. The tests may
                hang forever if <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linux=
fromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gdb=
" title=3D"GDB-15.1">GDB-15.1</a> is not installed. Some tests are
                known to hang also, depending on the version of glibc. A fe=
w
                tests can fail in various suites. Problematic tests can be
                disabled by changing the <strong class=3D"userinput"><code>=
prereq:</code></strong> line in the
                corresponding <code class=3D"filename">.vgtest</code> file =
to
                <strong class=3D"userinput"><code>prereq:
                false</code></strong>. For example:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -e 's@pre=
req:.*@prereq: false@' \
    -i {helgrind,drd}/tests/pth_cond_destroy_busy.vgtest</kbd></pre>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  The <span class=3D"application">OpenMP</span> tests are
                  skipped if libgomp has been compiled with <code class=3D"=
option">--enable-linux-futex</code> (the default). If
                  needed, just recompile the libgomp library from the gcc
                  build tree, passing <code class=3D"option">--disable-linu=
x-futex</code> to configure, storing
                  the library to some place and changing the link from
                  <code class=3D"filename">/usr/lib/libgomp.so.1</code> to
                  point to the new library.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
