              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of the Java BinaryJDK
              </h3>
              <p>
                Begin by extracting the appropriate binary tarball for your
                architecture and changing to the extracted directory. Insta=
ll
                the binary <span class=3D"application">OpenJDK</span> with =
the
                following commands as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</=
code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -vdm755 /o=
pt/OpenJDK-22.0.2-bin &amp;&amp;
mv -v * /opt/OpenJDK-22.0.2-bin         &amp;&amp;
chown -R root:root /opt/OpenJDK-22.0.2-bin</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                The binary version is now installed. You may create a symli=
nk
                to that version by issuing, as the <code class=3D"systemite=
m">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ln -sfn OpenJDK-22=
.0.2-bin /opt/jdk</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                You may now proceed to <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.h=
tml#ojdk-conf" title=3D"Configuring the Java environment">Configuring the J=
ava
                environment</a>, where the instructions assume that the abo=
ve
                link exists.
              </p>
