          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Apache Ant
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">Apache Ant</span> package i=
s a
                <span class=3D"application">Java</span>-based build tool. I=
n
                theory, it is like the <span class=3D"command"><strong>make=
</strong></span> command, but without
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>make</strong></span>'s
                wrinkles. <span class=3D"application">Ant</span> is differe=
nt.
                Instead of a model that is extended with shell-based
                commands, <span class=3D"application">Ant</span> is extende=
d
                using <span class=3D"application">Java</span> classes. Inst=
ead
                of writing shell commands, the configuration files are
                XML-based, calling out a target tree that executes various
                tasks. Each task is run by an object that implements a
                particular task interface.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470507804000" name=3D"idm140470507804000"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://a=
rchive.apache.org/dist/ant/source/apache-ant-1.10.14-src.tar.xz">
                      https://archive.apache.org/dist/ant/source/apache-ant=
-1.10.14-src.tar.xz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 055843219f487edb3a6db554ad1355ef
                    </p>
                  </li>
