            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Apache Ant
              </h3>
              <p>
                Build a limited bootstrap version of <span class=3D"applica=
tion">Apache Ant</span> using the following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./bootstrap.s=
h</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Download the runtime dependencies using the <code class=3D"=
filename">fetch.xml</code> ant build script:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">bootstrap/bin=
/ant -f fetch.xml -Ddest=3Doptional</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Build <span class=3D"application">Apache Ant</span> by runn=
ing
                the following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./build.sh -D=
dist.dir=3D$PWD/ant-1.10.14 dist</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user=
:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cp -rv ant-1.10.14=
 /opt/            &amp;&amp;
chown -R root:root /opt/ant-1.10.14 &amp;&amp;
ln -sfv ant-1.10.14 /opt/ant</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>bootstrap/bin/ant -f fetch.=
xml
                -D dest=3Doptional</strong></span>: Downloads the missing
                dependencies to the user's home directory, and copies them
                into the source tree (in the <code class=3D"filename">lib/o=
ptional</code> directory, where <span class=3D"command"><strong>ant</strong=
></span> picks them up at build
                time).
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>./build.sh -D
                dist.dir=3D$PWD/ant-1.10.14 dist</strong></span>: This comm=
and
                builds, tests, then installs the package into a temporary
                directory.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Apache Ant
              </h3>
