          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"ncftp" name=3D"ncftp"></a>NcFTP-3.2.7
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to NcFTP
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">NcFTP</span> package contai=
ns a
                powerful and flexible interface to the Internet standard Fi=
le
                Transfer Protocol. It is intended to replace or supplement
                the stock <span class=3D"command"><strong>ftp</strong></spa=
n>
                program.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470507414848" name=3D"idm140470507414848"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://w=
ww.ncftp.com/downloads/ncftp/ncftp-3.2.7-src.tar.xz">
                      https://www.ncftp.com/downloads/ncftp/ncftp-3.2.7-src=
.tar.xz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: bbcb048d2412f4d62bc798818e703680
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 416 KB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 6.9 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.2 SBU
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of NcFTP
              </h3>
              <p>
                There are two ways to build <span class=3D"application">NcF=
TP</span>. The first (and optimal) way
                builds most of the functionality as a shared library and th=
en
                builds and installs the program linked against this library=
.
                The second method simply links all of the functionality int=
o
                the binary statically. This doesn't make the dynamic librar=
y
                available for linking by other applications. You need to
                choose which method best suits you. Note that the second
                method does <span class=3D"emphasis"><em>not</em></span> cr=
eate
                an entirely statically linked binary; only the <code class=
=3D"filename">libncftp</code> parts are statically linked in, in
                this case. Be aware that building and using the shared
                library is covered by the Clarified Artistic License;
                however, developing applications that utilize the shared
                library is subject to a different license.
              </p>
              <p>
                First, fix an issue with the configure script introduced by
                gcc-14:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -i 's/def=
 HAVE_STDLIB_H/ 1/;s/extern select/extern int select/' configure</kbd></pre=
>
              <p>
                To install <span class=3D"application">NcFTP</span> using t=
he
                first (and optimal) method, run the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">CC=3D/usr/bin=
/gcc \
./configure --prefix=3D/usr --sysconfdir=3D/etc &amp;&amp;
make -C libncftp shared &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make -C libncftp s=
oinstall &amp;&amp;
make install</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To install <span class=3D"application">NcFTP</span> using t=
he
                second method (with the <code class=3D"filename">libncftp</=
code> functionality linked in
                statically) run the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr --sysconfdir=3D/etc &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make install<=
/kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"envar">CC=3D/usr/bin/gcc</code>. This enviro=
nment
                variable ensures that <span class=3D"command"><strong>gcc</=
strong></span> is used if <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromsc=
ratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#llvm" tit=
le=3D"LLVM-18.1.7">LLVM-18.1.7</a> is
                installed. The build procedure is broken if <span class=3D"=
command"><strong>gcc</strong></span> is not used.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>make -C ... &amp;&amp; make=
 -C
                ...</strong></span>: These commands make and install the
                dynamic library <code class=3D"filename">libncftp</code> wh=
ich
                is then used to link against when compiling the main progra=
m.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring NcFTP
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"ncftp-config" name=3D"ncftp-config"></a>Co=
nfig
                        Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/ncftp.*</code> and <code cl=
ass=3D"filename">~/.ncftp/*</code>; especially <code class=3D"filename">/et=
c/ncftp.prefs_v3</code> and <code class=3D"filename">~/.ncftp/prefs_v3</cod=
e>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470507372544" name=3D"idm14047050737=
2544"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Most <span class=3D"application">NcFTP</span> configurati=
on
                  is done while in the program, and the configuration files
                  are dealt with automatically. One exception to this is
                  <code class=3D"filename">~/.ncftp/prefs_v3</code>. There =
are
                  various options to alter in there, including:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"screen"><code class=3D"literal">yes-i-know-ab=
out-NcFTPd=3Dyes</code></pre>
                <p>
                  This disables the splash screen advertising the
                  <span class=3D"application">NcFTPd</span> server.
                </p>
                <p>
                  There are other options in the <code class=3D"filename">p=
refs_v3</code> file. Most of these are
                  self-explanatory. Global defaults can be set in
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/ncftp.prefs_v3</code>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
