              <p>
                For security reasons, running the <span class=3D"applicatio=
n">rsync</span> server as an unprivileged user and
                group is encouraged. If you intend to run <span class=3D"co=
mmand"><strong>rsync</strong></span> as a daemon, create
                the <code class=3D"systemitem">rsyncd</code> user and group
                with the following commands issued by the <code class=3D"sy=
stemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -g 48 rsy=
ncd &amp;&amp;
useradd -c "rsyncd Daemon" -m -d /home/rsync -g rsyncd \
    -s /bin/false -u 48 rsyncd</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">rsync</span> by running=
 the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr    \
            --disable-xxhash \
            --without-included-zlib &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#doxygen=
" title=3D"Doxygen-1.12.0">Doxygen-1.12.0</a> installed and wish to
                build HTML API documentation, issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">doxygen</kbd>=
</pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
              <p>
                If you built the documentation, install it using the
                following commands as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</=
code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -m755 -=
d          /usr/share/doc/rsync-3.3.0/api &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644 dox/html/*  /usr/share/doc/rsync-3.3.0/api</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-xxhash</code></em>:
                This switch disables advanced xxhash checksum support. Remo=
ve
                this switch if you have installed <a class=3D"ulink" href=
=3D"https://cyan4973.github.io/xxHash/">xxhash</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--without-included-zlib</code=
></em>: This
                switch enables compilation with the system-installed zlib
                library.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring rsync
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"rsync-config" name=3D"rsync-config"></a>Co=
nfig
                        Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/rsyncd.conf</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470506774128" name=3D"idm14047050677=
4128"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  For client access to remote files, you may need to instal=
l
                  the <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratc=
h.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#openssh" titl=
e=3D"OpenSSH-9.8p1">OpenSSH-9.8p1</a> package to connect to the
                  remote server.
                </p>
                <p>
                  This is a simple download-only configuration to set up
                  running <span class=3D"command"><strong>rsync</strong></s=
pan>
                  as a server. See the <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://m=
an.archlinux.org/man/rsyncd.conf.5">rsyncd.conf(5)</a>
                  man-page for additional options (i.e., user
                  authentication).
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/rs=
yncd.conf &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal"># This is a basic rsync configuration file
# It exports a single module without user authentication.

motd file =3D /home/rsync/welcome.msg
use chroot =3D yes

[localhost]
    path =3D /home/rsync
    comment =3D Default rsync module
    read only =3D yes
    list =3D yes
    uid =3D rsyncd
    gid =3D rsyncd
</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  You can find additional configuration information and
                  general documentation about <span class=3D"command"><stro=
ng>rsync</strong></span> at <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://rsync.samba.=
org/documentation.html">https://rsync.samba.org/documentation.html</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"rsync-init" name=3D"rsync-init"></a><span =
class=3D"phrase">Boot Script</span>
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Note that you only need to start the <span class=3D"appli=
cation">rsync</span> server if you want to provide an
                  <span class=3D"application">rsync</span> archive on your
                  local machine. You don't need this <span class=3D"phrase"=
>script</span> to run the <span class=3D"application">rsync</span> client.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Install the <span class=3D"phrase"><code class=3D"filenam=
e">/etc/rc.d/init.d/rsyncd</code> init
                  script</span> included in the <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"h=
ttps://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-n=
ochunks.html#bootscripts" title=3D"BLFS Boot Scripts">blfs-bootscripts-2024=
0416</a> package.
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-rsy=
ncd</kbd></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Program:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">rsync and rsync-ssl</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Libraries:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">None</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Directories:</stro=
ng>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">Optionally,
                    /usr/share/doc/rsync-3.3.0</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"variablelist">
                <h4>
                  <a id=3D"idm140470506751776" name=3D"idm140470506751776">=
</a>Short Descriptions
                </h4>
                <table border=3D"0" class=3D"variablelist">
                  <colgroup>
                    <col align=3D"left" valign=3D"top">
                    <col>
                  </colgroup>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"rsync-prog" name=3D"rsync-prog"></a><spa=
n class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>rsync</strong></span></spa=
n>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a replacement for <span class=3D"command"><str=
ong>rcp</strong></span> (and
                          <span class=3D"command"><strong>scp</strong></spa=
n>)
                          that has many more features. It uses the
                          <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D"quo=
te">rsync
                          algorithm</span>=E2=80=9D</span> which provides a=
 very fast
                          method of syncing remote files. It does this by
                          sending just the differences in the files across
                          the link, without requiring that both sets of fil=
es
                          are present at one end of the link beforehand
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"rsync-ssl" name=3D"rsync-ssl"></a><span =
class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>rsync-ssl</strong></span></s=
pan>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a helper script used when connecting to an rsy=
nc
                          daemon that has SSL support built in
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"samba" name=3D"samba"></a>Samba-4.20.4
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Samba
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">Samba</span> package provid=
es
                file and print services to SMB/CIFS clients and Windows
                networking to Linux clients. <span class=3D"application">Sa=
mba</span> can also be configured as a
                Windows Domain Controller replacement, a file/print server
                acting as a member of a Windows Active Directory domain and=
 a
                NetBIOS (RFC1001/1002) nameserver (which among other things
                provides LAN browsing support).
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
