                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: less than 0.1 SBU
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470506148832" name=3D"idm140470506148832"></=
a>Additional Downloads
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Required patch: <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/wireless_tools-29-fix_iwlist_scann=
ing-1.patch">
                      https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/wi=
reless_tools-29-fix_iwlist_scanning-1.patch</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470506146064" name=3D"idm140470506146064"></=
a>Wireless Tools Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470506145360" name=3D"idm140470506145360"></=
a>Required (Runtime)
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"nodump">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#wireless-kernel" ti=
tle=3D"Configuring the Linux Kernel for Wireless">Configuring the
                Linux Kernel for Wireless</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"wireless-tools-kernel" name=3D"wireless-tools-kern=
el"></a>Kernel Configuration
              </h3>
              <p>
                To use <span class=3D"application">Wireless Tools</span>, t=
he
                kernel must have the appropriate drivers and other support
                available. Besides the configurations mentioned by <a class=
=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BL=
FS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#wireless-kernel" title=3D"Configuring the L=
inux Kernel for Wireless">Configuring the
                Linux Kernel for Wireless</a>, it's also needed to enable t=
he
                following options in the kernel configuration:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen">[*] N<span class=3D"blue">e</span>twork=
ing support ---&gt;                                                [NET]
  [*] <span class=3D"blue">W</span>ireless ---&gt;                         =
                          [WIRELESS]
    &lt;*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">c</span>fg80211 - wireless configurati=
on API                       [CFG80211]
    [*]     <span class=3D"blue">c</span>fg80211 wireless extensions compat=
ibility           [CFG80211_WEXT]</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Wireless Tools
              </h3>
              <p>
                First, apply a patch that fixes a problem when numerous
                networks are available:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">patch -Np1 -i=
 ../wireless_tools-29-fix_iwlist_scanning-1.patch</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To install <span class=3D"application">Wireless Tools</span=
>,
                use the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make</kbd></p=
re>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make PREFIX=3D/usr=
 INSTALL_MAN=3D/usr/share/man install</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>INSTALL_MAN=3D/usr/share/ma=
n</strong></span>:
                Install manual pages in <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share=
/man</code> instead of <code class=3D"filename">/usr/man</code>.
              </p>
            </div>
