          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"wpa_supplicant" name=3D"wpa_supplicant"></a>wpa_=
supplicant-2.11
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to WPA Supplicant
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"application">WPA Supplicant</span> is a Wi-F=
i
                Protected Access (WPA) client and IEEE 802.1X supplicant. I=
t
                implements WPA key negotiation with a WPA Authenticator and
                Extensible Authentication Protocol (EAP) authentication wit=
h
                an Authentication Server. In addition, it controls the
                roaming and IEEE 802.11 authentication/association of the
                wireless LAN driver. This is useful for connecting to a
                password protected wireless access point.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470506073424" name=3D"idm140470506073424"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://w=
1.fi/releases/wpa_supplicant-2.11.tar.gz">https://w1.fi/releases/wpa_suppli=
cant-2.11.tar.gz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 72a4a00eddb7a499a58113c3361ab094
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 3.7 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 35 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.3 SBU (without optional gui)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470506065840" name=3D"idm140470506065840"></=
a>WPA
                Supplicant Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470506064656" name=3D"idm140470506064656"></=
a>Required (Runtime)
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"nodump">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#wireless-kernel" ti=
tle=3D"Configuring the Linux Kernel for Wireless">Configuring the
                Linux Kernel for Wireless</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470506062672" name=3D"idm140470506062672"></=
a>Recommended
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#desktop-file-utils"=
 title=3D"desktop-file-utils-0.27">desktop-file-utils-0.27</a> (for
                running <span class=3D"command"><strong>update-desktop-data=
base</strong></span>)
                and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.=
org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libnl" title=3D=
"libnl-3.10.0">libnl-3.10.0</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470506059296" name=3D"idm140470506059296"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <span class=3D"phrase"><a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.h=
tml#dbus" title=3D"dbus-1.14.10">dbus-1.14.10</a>,</span> <a class=3D"xref"=
 href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-1=
2.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libxml2" title=3D"libxml2-2.13.3">libxml2-2.13.3</a>=
, and
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#qt5-components" tit=
le=3D"qt5-components-5.15.14">qt5-components-5.15.14</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"wpa_supplicant-kernel" name=3D"wpa_supplicant-kern=
el"></a>Kernel Configuration
              </h3>
              <p>
                To use <span class=3D"application">wpa_supplicant</span>, t=
he
                kernel must have the appropriate drivers and other support
                available. Read <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linux=
fromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#wir=
eless-kernel" title=3D"Configuring the Linux Kernel for Wireless">Configuri=
ng
                the Linux Kernel for Wireless</a> for details.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of WPA Supplicant
              </h3>
              <p>
                First you will need to create an initial configuration file
                for the build process. You can read <code class=3D"filename=
">wpa_supplicant/README</code> and <code class=3D"filename">wpa_supplicant/=
defconfig</code> for the
                explanation of the following options as well as other optio=
ns
                that can be used. Create a build configuration file that
                should work for standard WiFi setups by running the followi=
ng
                command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; wpa_=
supplicant/.config &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">CONFIG_BACKEND=3Dfile
CONFIG_CTRL_IFACE=3Dy
CONFIG_DEBUG_FILE=3Dy
CONFIG_DEBUG_SYSLOG=3Dy
CONFIG_DEBUG_SYSLOG_FACILITY=3DLOG_DAEMON
CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211=3Dy
CONFIG_DRIVER_WEXT=3Dy
CONFIG_DRIVER_WIRED=3Dy
CONFIG_EAP_GTC=3Dy
CONFIG_EAP_LEAP=3Dy
CONFIG_EAP_MD5=3Dy
CONFIG_EAP_MSCHAPV2=3Dy
CONFIG_EAP_OTP=3Dy
CONFIG_EAP_PEAP=3Dy
CONFIG_EAP_TLS=3Dy
CONFIG_EAP_TTLS=3Dy
CONFIG_IEEE8021X_EAPOL=3Dy
CONFIG_IPV6=3Dy
CONFIG_LIBNL32=3Dy
CONFIG_PEERKEY=3Dy
CONFIG_PKCS12=3Dy
CONFIG_READLINE=3Dy
CONFIG_SMARTCARD=3Dy
CONFIG_WPS=3Dy
CFLAGS +=3D -I/usr/include/libnl3</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you wish to use <span class=3D"application">WPA
                Supplicant</span> with <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.h=
tml#NetworkManager" title=3D"NetworkManager-1.48.8">NetworkManager-1.48.8</=
a>, make
                sure that you have installed <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"http=
s://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-noch=
unks.html#dbus" title=3D"dbus-1.14.10">dbus-1.14.10</a> and <a class=3D"xre=
f" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK=
-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libxml2" title=3D"libxml2-2.13.3">libxml2-2.13.3</=
a>,
                then add the following options to the <span class=3D"applic=
ation">WPA Supplicant</span> build configuration file
                by running the following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt;&gt; =
wpa_supplicant/.config &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">CONFIG_CTRL_IFACE_DBUS=3Dy
CONFIG_CTRL_IFACE_DBUS_NEW=3Dy
CONFIG_CTRL_IFACE_DBUS_INTRO=3Dy</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">WPA Supplicant</span> b=
y
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cd wpa_suppli=
cant &amp;&amp;
make BINDIR=3D/usr/sbin LIBDIR=3D/usr/lib</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have installed <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www=
.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.ht=
ml#qt5-components" title=3D"qt5-components-5.15.14">qt5-components-5.15.14<=
/a> and
                wish to build the <span class=3D"application">WPA
                Supplicant</span> GUI program, run the following commands:
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  The following directory name is labelled qt4, but is
                  compatible with <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.lin=
uxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#q=
t5-components" title=3D"qt5-components-5.15.14">qt5-components-5.15.14</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">pushd wpa_gui=
-qt4 &amp;&amp;
qmake wpa_gui.pro &amp;&amp;
make &amp;&amp;
popd</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -m755 w=
pa_{cli,passphrase,supplicant} /usr/sbin/ &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644 doc/docbook/wpa_supplicant.conf.5 /usr/share/man/man5/ &am=
p;&amp;
install -v -m644 doc/docbook/wpa_{cli,passphrase,supplicant}.8 /usr/share/m=
an/man8/</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have built <span class=3D"application">WPA
                Supplicant</span> with <span class=3D"application">D-Bus</s=
pan>
                support, you will need to install <span class=3D"applicatio=
n">D-Bus</span> configuration files. Install them
                by running the following commands as the <code class=3D"sys=
temitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -m644 d=
bus/fi.w1.wpa_supplicant1.service \
                 /usr/share/dbus-1/system-services/ &amp;&amp;
install -v -d -m755 /etc/dbus-1/system.d &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644 dbus/dbus-wpa_supplicant.conf \
                 /etc/dbus-1/system.d/wpa_supplicant.conf</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have built the <span class=3D"application">WPA
                Supplicant</span> GUI program, install it by running the
                following commands as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</=
code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -m755 w=
pa_gui-qt4/wpa_gui /usr/bin/ &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644 doc/docbook/wpa_gui.8 /usr/share/man/man8/ &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644 wpa_gui-qt4/wpa_gui.desktop /usr/share/applications/ &amp;=
&amp;
install -v -m644 wpa_gui-qt4/icons/wpa_gui.svg /usr/share/pixmaps/</kbd></p=
re>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  You will need to restart the system <span class=3D"applic=
ation">D-Bus</span> daemon before you can use the
                  <span class=3D"application">WPA Supplicant</span>
                  <span class=3D"application">D-Bus</span> interface.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  This package installs desktop files into the <code class=
=3D"filename">/usr/share/applications</code> hierarchy and you
                  can improve system performance and memory usage by updati=
ng
                  <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/applications/mimeinfo=
.cache</code>.
                  To perform the update you must have <a class=3D"xref" hre=
f=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-=
sysv-nochunks.html#desktop-file-utils" title=3D"desktop-file-utils-0.27">de=
sktop-file-utils-0.27</a>
                  installed and issue the following command as the
                  <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">update-desktop-d=
atabase -q</kbd></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring wpa_supplicant
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"admon important">
                <h3>
                  Important
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If you are using WPA Supplicant with <a class=3D"xref" hr=
ef=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2=
-sysv-nochunks.html#NetworkManager" title=3D"NetworkManager-1.48.8">Network=
Manager-1.48.8</a> (or
                  anything communicating with WPA Supplicant via D-Bus), th=
is
                  section should be skipped. Running a D-Bus connected WPA
                  Supplicant instance and another WPA supplicant instance
                  configured following this section simultaneously can caus=
e
                  subtle issues.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"wpa_supplicant-config" name=3D"wpa_supplic=
ant-config"></a>Config File
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/sysconfig/wpa_supplicant-*.=
conf</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470506000944" name=3D"idm14047050600=
0944"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  To connect to an access point that uses a password, you
                  need to put the pre-shared key in <span class=3D"phrase">=
<code class=3D"filename">/etc/sysconfig/wpa_supplicant-<em class=3D"replace=
able"><code>wifi0</code></em>.conf</code>.</span>
                  SSID is the string that the access point/router transmits
                  to identify itself. Run the following command as the
                  <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">wpa_passphr=
ase <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>SSID</code></em> <em class=3D"replaceab=
le"><code>SECRET_PASSWORD</code></em> &gt; /etc/sysconfig/wpa_supplicant-<e=
m class=3D"replaceable"><code>wifi0</code></em>.conf</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  <span class=3D"phrase"><code class=3D"filename">/etc/sysc=
onfig/wpa_supplicant-<em class=3D"replaceable"><code>wifi0</code></em>.conf=
</code></span>
                  can hold the details of several access points. When
                  <span class=3D"command"><strong>wpa_supplicant</strong></=
span> is
                  started, it will scan for the SSIDs it can see and choose
                  the appropriate password to connect.
                </p>
                <p>
                  If you want to connect to an access point that isn't
                  password protected, put an entry like this in <span class=
=3D"phrase"><code class=3D"filename">/etc/sysconfig/wpa_supplicant-<em clas=
s=3D"replaceable"><code>wifi0</code></em>.conf</code>.</span>
                  Replace "Some-SSID" with the SSID of the access
                  point/router.
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"screen">network=3D{
  ssid=3D"<em class=3D"replaceable"><code>Some-SSID</code></em>"
  key_mgmt=3DNONE
}</pre>
                <p>
                  Connecting to a new access point that is not in the
                  configuration file can be accomplished manually via the
                  command line or GUI, but it must be done via a privileged
                  user. To do that, add the following to the configuration
                  file:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"screen">ctrl_interface=3DDIR=3D/run/wpa_suppl=
icant GROUP=3D&lt;privileged group&gt;
update_config=3D1</pre>
                <p>
                  Replace the &lt;privileged group&gt; above with a system
                  group where members have the ability to connect to a
                  wireless access point.
                </p>
                <p>
                  There are many options that you could use to tweak how yo=
u
                  connect to each access point. They are described in some
                  detail in the <code class=3D"filename">wpa_supplicant/wpa=
_supplicant.conf</code> file
                  in the source tree.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470505983408" name=3D"idm14047050598=
3408"></a>Connecting to an Access
                        Point
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <a id=3D"wpa-service" name=3D"wpa-service"></a> If you wa=
nt to
                  configure network interfaces at boot using <span class=3D=
"command"><strong>wpa_supplicant</strong></span>, you need
                  to install the <code class=3D"filename">/lib/services/wpa=
</code> script included in
                  <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.or=
g/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#bootscripts" titl=
e=3D"BLFS Boot Scripts">blfs-bootscripts-20240416</a> package:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-ser=
vice-wpa</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  If your router/access point uses DHCP to allocate IP
                  addresses, you can install <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"http=
s://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-noch=
unks.html#dhcpcd" title=3D"dhcpcd-10.0.8">dhcpcd-10.0.8</a> and use it to
                  automatically obtain network addresses. Create the
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/sysconfig/ifconfig-<em clas=
s=3D"replaceable"><code>wifi0</code></em></code> by running the
                  following command as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root<=
/code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/sy=
sconfig/ifconfig.<em class=3D"replaceable"><code>wifi0</code></em> &lt;&lt;=
 "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">ONBOOT=3D"yes"
IFACE=3D"<em class=3D"replaceable"><code>wlan0</code></em>"
SERVICE=3D"wpa"

# Additional arguments to wpa_supplicant
WPA_ARGS=3D""

WPA_SERVICE=3D"dhcpcd"
DHCP_START=3D"-b -q <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;insert appropriate =
start options here&gt;</code></em>"
DHCP_STOP=3D"-k <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;insert additional stop =
options here&gt;</code></em>"</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Alternatively, if you use static addresses on your local
                  network, then create the <code class=3D"filename">/etc/sy=
sconfig/ifconfig-<em class=3D"replaceable"><code>wifi0</code></em></code> b=
y running the
                  following command as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root<=
/code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/sy=
sconfig/ifconfig.<em class=3D"replaceable"><code>wifi0</code></em> &lt;&lt;=
 "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">ONBOOT=3D"yes"
IFACE=3D"<em class=3D"replaceable"><code>wlan0</code></em>"
SERVICE=3D"wpa"

# Additional arguments to wpa_supplicant
WPA_ARGS=3D""

WPA_SERVICE=3D"ipv4-static"
IP=3D"192.168.1.1"
GATEWAY=3D"192.168.1.2"
PREFIX=3D"24"
BROADCAST=3D"192.168.1.255"</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  You can connect to the wireless access point by running t=
he
                  following command as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root<=
/code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ifup <em class=
=3D"replaceable"><code>wifi0</code></em></kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Replace <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>wlan0</code></em>
                  with the correct wireless interface and <em class=3D"repl=
aceable"><code>wifi0</code></em> with desired name for
                  the configuration file. Please note that <code class=3D"f=
ilename">wpa_supplicant-*.conf</code> and <code class=3D"filename">ifconfig=
.*</code> configuration files need to
                  have identical names, ie both contain <em class=3D"replac=
eable"><code>wifi0</code></em> in their name.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">wpa_gui, wpa_supplicant,
                    wpa_passphrase and wpa_cli</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Libraries:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">None</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Directories:</stro=
ng>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">None</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"variablelist">
                <h4>
                  <a id=3D"idm140470505948752" name=3D"idm140470505948752">=
</a>Short Descriptions
                </h4>
                <table border=3D"0" class=3D"variablelist">
                  <colgroup>
                    <col align=3D"left" valign=3D"top">
                    <col>
                  </colgroup>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"wpa_gui" name=3D"wpa_gui"></a><span clas=
s=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>wpa_gui</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a graphical frontend program for interacting
                          with <span class=3D"application">wpa_supplicant</=
span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"wpa_supplicant-prog" name=3D"wpa_supplic=
ant-prog"></a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>wpa_supp=
licant</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a daemon that can connect to a password
                          protected wireless access point
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"wpa_passphrase" name=3D"wpa_passphrase">=
</a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>wpa_passphrase</st=
rong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          takes an SSID and a password and generates a simp=
le
                          configuration that <span class=3D"command"><stron=
g>wpa_supplicant</strong></span>
                          can understand
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"wpa_cli" name=3D"wpa_cli"></a><span clas=
s=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>wpa_cli</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a command line interface used to control a
                          running <span class=3D"command"><strong>wpa_suppl=
icant</strong></span>
                          daemon
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"titlepage">
          <div>
            <div>
              <h2 class=3D"title">
                <a id=3D"netutils" name=3D"netutils"></a>Chapter&nbsp;16.&n=
bsp;Networking Utilities
              </h2>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"chapter" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
          <p>
            This chapter contains some tools that come in handy when the
            network needs investigating.
          </p>
          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"avahi" name=3D"avahi"></a>Avahi-0.8
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Avahi
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">Avahi</span> package is a
                system which facilitates service discovery on a local
                network.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470505918432" name=3D"idm140470505918432"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://g=
ithub.com/lathiat/avahi/releases/download/v0.8/avahi-0.8.tar.gz">
                      https://github.com/lathiat/avahi/releases/download/v0=
.8/avahi-0.8.tar.gz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 229c6aa30674fc43c202b22c5f8c2be7
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 1.5 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 32 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.3 SBU
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470505911008" name=3D"idm140470505911008"></=
a>Additional Downloads
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Required patch: <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/avahi-0.8-ipv6_race_condition_fix-=
1.patch">
                      https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/av=
ahi-0.8-ipv6_race_condition_fix-1.patch</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470505908240" name=3D"idm140470505908240"></=
a>Avahi Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470505907552" name=3D"idm140470505907552"></=
a>Required
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#glib2" title=3D"GLi=
b-2.80.4">GLib-2.80.4</a> (GObject Introspection
                recommended)
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470505905504" name=3D"idm140470505905504"></=
a>Recommended
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gtk3" title=3D"GTK+=
-3.24.43">GTK+-3.24.43</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libdaem=
on" title=3D"libdaemon-0.14">libdaemon-0.14</a>, and
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#qt5-components" tit=
le=3D"qt5-components-5.15.14">qt5-components-5.15.14</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470505902176" name=3D"idm140470505902176"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#dbus-python" title=
=3D"D-Bus Python-1.3.2">D-Bus Python-1.3.2</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"h=
ttps://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-n=
ochunks.html#libevent" title=3D"libevent-2.1.12">libevent-2.1.12</a>,
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#doxygen" title=3D"D=
oxygen-1.12.0">Doxygen-1.12.0</a>, <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://downl=
oad.gnome.org/sources/gtk+/2.24/">GTK+-2</a>
                (deprecated), and <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://source=
forge.net/projects/xmltoman/">xmltoman</a>
                (for generating documentation)
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Avahi
              </h3>
              <p>
                There should be a dedicated user and group to take control =
of
                the <span class=3D"command"><strong>avahi-daemon</strong></=
span> daemon after
                it is started. Issue the following commands as the
                <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -fg 84 av=
ahi &amp;&amp;
useradd -c "Avahi Daemon Owner" -d /run/avahi-daemon -u 84 \
        -g avahi -s /bin/false avahi</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                There should also be a dedicated privileged access group fo=
r
                <span class=3D"application">Avahi</span> clients. Issue the
                following command as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</c=
ode>
                user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -fg 86 ne=
tdev</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Fix a regression that results in a race condition when IPv6
                is in use and multiple network adapters are present on the
                system:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">patch -Np1 -i=
 ../avahi-0.8-ipv6_race_condition_fix-1.patch</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Fix a security vulnerability in <span class=3D"command"><st=
rong>avahi-daemon</strong></span>:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -i '426a =
if (events &amp; AVAHI_WATCH_HUP) { \
client_free(c); \
return; \
}' avahi-daemon/simple-protocol.c</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Avahi</span> by running=
 the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure \
    --prefix=3D/usr                  \
    --sysconfdir=3D/etc              \
    --localstatedir=3D/var           \
    --disable-static               \
    --disable-libevent             \
    --disable-mono                 \
    --disable-monodoc              \
    --disable-python               \
    --disable-qt3                  \
    --disable-qt4                  \
    --enable-core-docs             \
    --with-distro=3Dnone             \
    --with-systemdsystemunitdir=3Dno \
    --with-dbus-system-address=3D'unix:path=3D/run/dbus/system_bus_socket' =
&amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-static</code></em>:
                This switch prevents installation of static versions of the
                libraries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-libevent</code></em=
>:
                This parameter disables the use of <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#libevent" title=3D"libevent-2.1.12">libevent-2.1.12</a>.
                Remove if you have it installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-mono</code></em>: T=
his
                parameter disables the <span class=3D"application">Mono</sp=
an>
                bindings.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-monodoc</code></em>=
:
                This parameter disables documentation for the <span class=
=3D"application">Mono</span> bindings.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-python</code></em>:
                This parameter disables the scripts that depend on
                <span class=3D"application">Python</span>. It also allows a
                regular install to complete successfully.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-qt3</code></em>: Th=
is
                parameter disables the attempt to build the obsolete
                <span class=3D"application">Qt3</span> portions of the pack=
age.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-qt4</code></em>: Th=
is
                parameter disables the attempt to build the obsolete
                <span class=3D"application">Qt4Core</span> portions of the
                package.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-core-docs</code></em=
>:
                This parameter enables the building of documentation.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-distro=3Dnone</code></=
em>:
                There is an obsolete boot script in the distribution for LF=
S.
                This option disables it.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-systemdsystemunitdir=
=3Dno</code></em>:
                Without it, the daemon fails to start in BLFS, which does n=
ot
                support <span class=3D"application">systemd</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-dbus-system-address=3D=
</code></em>:
                This option prevents the package from referring to the
                deprecated <code class=3D"filename">/var/run</code> directo=
ry.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--disable-dbus</code>: This paramete=
r
                disables the use of <span class=3D"application">D-Bus</span=
>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--disable-gtk</code>: This parameter
                disables the use of <span class=3D"application">GTK+2</span=
>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--disable-gtk3</code>: This paramete=
r
                disables the use of <span class=3D"application">GTK+3</span=
>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--disable-qt5</code>: This parameter
                disables the use of <span class=3D"application">Qt5</span>,=
 and
                allows building without it.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--disable-libdaemon</code>: This
                parameter disables the use of <span class=3D"application">l=
ibdaemon</span>. If you use this option,
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>avahi-daemon</strong></span=
>
                won't be built.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-tests</code>: This option
                enables the building of tests and examples.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-compat-howl</code>: This op=
tion
                enables the compatibility layer for <span class=3D"applicat=
ion">HOWL</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-compat-libdns_sd</code>: Th=
is
