            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of NetworkManager
              </h3>
              <p>
                If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#qt5-components" =
title=3D"qt5-components-5.15.14">qt5-components-5.15.14</a> is
                installed and the Qt based examples are desired, fix two
                meson.build files:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -e 's/-qt=
4/-qt5/'              \
    -e 's/moc_location/host_bins/' \
    -i examples/C/qt/meson.build   &amp;&amp;

sed -e 's/Qt/&amp;5/'                  \
    -i meson.build</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Fix the python scripts so that they use <span class=3D"appl=
ication">Python 3</span>:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">grep -rl '^#!=
.*python$' | xargs sed -i '1s/python/&amp;3/'</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">NetworkManager</span> b=
y
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

CXXFLAGS+=3D"-O2 -fPIC"             \
meson setup ..                    \
      --prefix=3D/usr               \
      --buildtype=3Drelease         \
      -D libaudit=3Dno              \
      -D nmtui=3Dtrue               \
      -D ovs=3Dfalse                \
      -D ppp=3Dfalse                \
      -D selinux=3Dfalse            \
      -D session_tracking=3Delogind \
      -D modem_manager=3Dfalse      \
      -D systemdsystemunitdir=3Dno  \
      -D systemd_journal=3Dfalse    \
      -D qt=3Dfalse                 &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                An already active graphical session with a bus address is
                necessary to run the tests. To test the results, issue
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>ninja test</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                A few tests may fail, depending on enabled kernel options.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install &amp=
;&amp;
mv -v /usr/share/doc/NetworkManager{,-1.48.8}</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have not passed the <code class=3D"option">-D
                docs=3Dtrue</code> option to <span class=3D"command"><stron=
g>meson</strong></span>, you can install the
                pregenerated manual pages with (as the <code class=3D"syste=
mitem">root</code> user):
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">for file in $(echo=
 ../man/*.[1578]); do
    section=3D${file##*.} &amp;&amp;
    install -vdm 755 /usr/share/man/man$section
    install -vm 644 $file /usr/share/man/man$section/
done</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have not used <code class=3D"option">-D
                docs=3Dtrue</code>, the pregenerated HTML documentation can
                also be installed with (as the <code class=3D"systemitem">r=
oot</code> user):
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cp -Rv ../docs/{ap=
i,libnm} /usr/share/doc/NetworkManager-1.48.8</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"envar">CXXFLAGS=3D"-O2 -fPIC"</code>: These
                compiler options are necessary to build the Qt5 based
                examples.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D docs=3Dtrue</code>: Use this swit=
ch to
                enable building man pages and documentation if <a class=3D"=
xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-B=
OOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gtk-doc" title=3D"GTK-Doc-1.34.0">GTK-Doc-1.34.=
0</a> is installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D nmtui=3Dtrue</code></em>: =
This
                switch enables building <span class=3D"command"><strong>nmt=
ui</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                systemdsystemunitdir=3Dno</code></em> and <em class=3D"para=
meter"><code>-D systemd_journal=3Dfalse</code></em>:
                systemd is not used for sysv init systems, so prevent
                installing units and using the systemd journal.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D ovs=3Dfalse</code></em>: T=
his
                switch disable the Open vSwitch integration because it need=
s
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#jansson" title=3D"J=
ansson-2.14">jansson-2.14</a>. Remove it if you have
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#jansson" title=3D"J=
ansson-2.14">jansson-2.14</a> installed on your system.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                modem_manager=3Dfalse</code></em>: This switch is required =
if
                <span class=3D"application">ModemManager</span> is not
                installed. Omit this switch if you have built <span class=
=3D"application">ModemManager</span> and <span class=3D"application">mobile=
-broadband-provider-info</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                session_tracking=3Delogind</code></em>: This switch is used=
 to
                set <span class=3D"command"><strong>elogind</strong></span>=
 as
                the default program for session tracking.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D ppp=3Dfalse</code></em>: T=
his
                switch disables <span class=3D"application">PPP</span> supp=
ort
                in <span class=3D"application">NetworkManager</span> since =
the
                programs necessary for it are not installed. Remove this
                switch if you need PPP support and have <span class=3D"appl=
ication">PPP</span> installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D libaudit=3Dno</code></em> =
and
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D selinux=3Dfalse</code></em=
>:
                This switch disables support for libaudit and SELinux since
                they are not used in BLFS.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D qt=3Dfalse</code></em>: Th=
is
                switch disables the <span class=3D"application">Qt</span>
                examples. Omit if you have <span class=3D"application">Qt</=
span> available and wish to install the
                examples.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D crypto=3Dgnutls</code>: Use this =
switch
                if you have GnuTLS installed and want to use it for
                certificate and key operations in NetworkManager, instead o=
f
                using NSS (the default).
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D crypto=3Dnull</code>: Use this sw=
itch
                if neither NSS nor GnuTLS is installed but you want to buil=
d
                NetworkManager anyway. This switch will make NetworkManager
                lack some features (for example 802.1X).
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D suspend_resume=3Dupower</code>: U=
se
                this switch if you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://w=
ww.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.=
html#upower" title=3D"UPower-1.90.4">UPower-1.90.4</a> installed and want t=
o use
                it (instead of <span class=3D"phrase"><a class=3D"xref" hre=
f=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-=
sysv-nochunks.html#elogind" title=3D"elogind-255.5">elogind-255.5</a></span=
> )
                for suspend and resume support.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring NetworkManager
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"NetworkManager-config" name=3D"NetworkMana=
ger-config"></a>Config Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/NetworkManager/NetworkManag=
er.conf</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470505568608" name=3D"idm14047050556=
8608"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  For <span class=3D"application">NetworkManager</span> to
                  work, at least a minimal configuration file must be
                  present. Such a file is not installed with <span class=3D=
"command"><strong>make install</strong></span>. Issue the
                  following command as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root<=
/code> user to create a minimal
                  <code class=3D"filename">NetworkManager.conf</code> file:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt;&gt; /et=
c/NetworkManager/NetworkManager.conf &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">[main]
plugins=3Dkeyfile</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  This file should not be modified directly by users of the
                  system. Instead, system specific changes should be made
                  using configuration files in the <code class=3D"filename"=
>/etc/NetworkManager/conf.d</code> directory.
                </p>
                <p>
                  To allow polkit to manage authorizations, add the followi=
ng
                  configuration file:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/Ne=
tworkManager/conf.d/polkit.conf &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">[main]
auth-polkit=3Dtrue</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  To use something other than the built-in dhcp client
                  (recommended if using only <span class=3D"command"><stron=
g>nmcli</strong></span>), use the following
                  configuration (valid values include either dhcpcd or
                  internal):
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /e=
tc/NetworkManager/conf.d/dhcp.conf &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">[main]
dhcp=3D</code><em class=3D"replaceable"><code>dhcpcd</code></em>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  To prevent <span class=3D"application">NetworkManager</sp=
an>
                  from updating the <code class=3D"filename">/etc/resolv.co=
nf</code> file, add the following
                  configuration file:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /e=
tc/NetworkManager/conf.d/no-dns-update.conf &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">[main]
dns=3Dnone</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  For additional configuration options, see <span class=3D"=
command"><strong>man 5
                  NetworkManager.conf</strong></span>.
                </p>
                <p>
                  To allow regular users to configure network connections,
                  you should add them to the <code class=3D"systemitem">net=
dev</code> group, and create a <span class=3D"application">polkit</span> ru=
le that grants access. Run
                  the following commands as the <code class=3D"systemitem">=
root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -fg 86 =
netdev &amp;&amp;
/usr/sbin/usermod -a -G netdev <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;username=
&gt;</code></em>

