              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of NetworkManager Applet
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">NetworkManager
                Applet</span> by running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup ..            \
      --prefix=3D/usr       \
      --buildtype=3Drelease \
      -D appindicator=3Dno  \
      -D selinux=3Dfalse    &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>ninja test</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D appindicator=3Dno</code></=
em>:
                This switch disables AppIndicator support in
                network-manager-applet because it requires libindicator,
                which is not in BLFS. The build will fail without this
                option.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D selinux=3Dfalse</code></em=
>:
                This switch forcibly disables <span class=3D"application">S=
ELinux</span> support since it is not
                currently in BLFS and the build will fail without it.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D wwan=3Dfalse</code>: This switch
                disables WWAN support. Use this if you do not have <a class=
=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BL=
FS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#ModemManager" title=3D"ModemManager-1.18.12=
">ModemManager-1.18.12</a> installed.
              </p>
            </div>
