            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of cURL
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">cURL</span> by running =
the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr                           \
            --disable-static                        \
            --with-openssl                          \
            --enable-threaded-resolver              \
            --with-ca-path=3D/etc/ssl/certs &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To run the test suite, issue: <span class=3D"command"><stro=
ng>make test</strong></span>. Some tests are
                flaky, so if some tests have failed it's possible to run a
                test again with: <span class=3D"command"><strong>(cd tests;
                ./runtests.pl <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;test
                ID&gt;</code></em>)</strong></span> (the ID of failed tests
                are shown in the <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=
=3D"quote"><code class=3D"computeroutput">These test cases
                failed:</code></span>=E2=80=9D</span> message). If you run =
the tests
                after the package has been installed, some tests may fail
                because the man pages were deleted by the 'find' command in
                the installation instructions below.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install &amp;=
&amp;

rm -rf docs/examples/.deps &amp;&amp;

find docs \( -name Makefile\* -o  \
             -name \*.1       -o  \
             -name \*.3       -o  \
             -name CMakeLists.txt \) -delete &amp;&amp;

cp -v -R docs -T /usr/share/doc/curl-8.9.1</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To run some simple verification tests on the newly installe=
d
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>curl</strong></span>, issue=
 the
                following commands: <span class=3D"command"><strong>curl
                --trace-ascii debugdump.txt
                https://www.example.com/</strong></span> and <span class=3D=
"command"><strong>curl --trace-ascii d.txt --trace-time
                https://example.com/</strong></span>. Inspect the locally
                created trace files <code class=3D"filename">debugdump.txt<=
/code> and <code class=3D"filename">d.txt</code>, which contains version in=
formation,
                downloaded files information, etc. One file has the time fo=
r
                each action logged.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-static</code></em>:
                This switch prevents installation of static versions of the
                libraries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-threaded-resolver</c=
ode></em>:
                This switch enables <span class=3D"application">cURL</span>=
's
                builtin threaded DNS resolver.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-ca-path=3D/etc/ssl/cer=
ts</code></em>:
                This switch sets the location of the BLFS Certificate
                Authority store.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-openssl</code></em>: T=
his
                parameter chooses <span class=3D"application">OpenSSL</span=
> as
                SSL/TLS implementation. This seems mandatory now.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-gssapi</code>: This parameter
                adds <span class=3D"application">Kerberos 5</span> support =
to
                <code class=3D"filename">libcurl</code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--without-ssl --with-gnutls</code>: =
Use
                this switch to build with <span class=3D"application">GnuTL=
S</span> support instead of <span class=3D"application">OpenSSL</span> for =
SSL/TLS.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-ca-bundle=3D/etc/pki/tls/cert=
s/ca-bundle.crt</code>:
                Use this switch instead of <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--=
with-ca-path</code></em> if building with
                <span class=3D"application">GnuTLS</span> support instead o=
f
                <span class=3D"application">OpenSSL</span> for SSL/TLS.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-libssh2</code>: This paramete=
r
                adds <span class=3D"application">SSH</span> support to cURL=
.
                This is disabled by default.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-ares</code>: This parameter
                adds support for DNS resolution through the c-ares library.
                It overrides <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-threade=
d-resolver</code></em> and
                is not widely tested by the editors.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>find docs ... -exec rm {}
                \;</strong></span>: This command removes <code class=3D"fil=
ename">Makefiles</code> and man files from the
                documentation directory that would otherwise be installed b=
y
                the commands that follow.
              </p>
