            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of libnma
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">libnma</span> by runnin=
g
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup ..                                \
      --prefix=3D/usr                           \
      --buildtype=3Drelease                     \
      -D gtk_doc=3Dfalse                        \
      -D libnma_gtk4=3Dtrue                     \
      -D mobile_broadband_provider_info=3Dfalse &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>ninja test</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D gtk_doc=3Dfalse</code></em=
>:
                This parameter disables generating API documentation using
                gtk-doc. If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.=
linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.htm=
l#gtk-doc" title=3D"GTK-Doc-1.34.0">GTK-Doc-1.34.0</a> installed and wish t=
o
                generate the API documentation, omit this switch.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D libnma_gtk4=3Dtrue</code><=
/em>:
                This parameter builds the GTK-4 version of libnma. It is
                needed by <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromsc=
ratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gnome-con=
trol-center" title=3D"gnome-control-center-46.4">gnome-control-center-46.4<=
/a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                mobile_broadband_provider_info=3Dfalse</code></em>: This sw=
itch
                disables WWAN support because mobile-broadband-provider-inf=
o
                is not in BLFS. Omit this switch if you have it installed a=
nd
                wish to enable WWAN support.
              </p>
            </div>
