                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Lynx
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"application">Lynx</span> is a text based web
                browser.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470503798688" name=3D"idm140470503798688"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://i=
nvisible-mirror.net/archives/lynx/tarballs/lynx2.9.2.tar.bz2">
                      https://invisible-mirror.net/archives/lynx/tarballs/l=
ynx2.9.2.tar.bz2</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 3ce01505e82626ca4d7291d7e649c4c9
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 2.7 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 25 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.4 SBU
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470503791280" name=3D"idm140470503791280"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gnutls" title=3D"Gn=
uTLS-3.8.7.1">GnuTLS-3.8.7.1</a> (experimental, to replace
                openssl), <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromsc=
ratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#zip" titl=
e=3D"Zip-3.0">Zip-3.0</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfroms=
cratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#unzip" t=
itle=3D"UnZip-6.0">UnZip-6.0</a>, an <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.=
linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.htm=
l#server-mail" title=3D"Chapter&nbsp;21.&nbsp;Mail Server Software">MTA</a>=
 (that
                provides a <span class=3D"command"><strong>sendmail</strong=
></span> command), and
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#sharutils" title=3D=
"Sharutils-4.15.2">Sharutils-4.15.2</a> (for the <span class=3D"command"><s=
trong>uudecode</strong></span> program)
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Lynx
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Lynx</span> by running =
the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr           \
            --sysconfdir=3D/etc/lynx  \
            --with-zlib             \
            --with-bzlib            \
            --with-ssl              \
            --with-screen=3Dncursesw  \
            --enable-locale-charset \
            --datadir=3D/usr/share/doc/lynx-2.9.2 &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-full
chgrp -v -R root /usr/share/doc/lynx-2.9.2/lynx_doc</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--sysconfdir=3D/etc/lynx</cod=
e></em>: This
                parameter is used so that the configuration files are locat=
ed
                in <code class=3D"filename">/etc/lynx</code> instead of
                <code class=3D"filename">/usr/etc</code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--datadir=3D/usr/share/doc/ly=
nx-2.9.2</code></em>:
                This parameter is used so that the documentation files are
                installed into <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/doc/lynx=
-2.9.2</code> instead of
                <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/lynx_{doc,help}</code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-zlib</code></em>: This
                enables support for linking <code class=3D"filename">libz</=
code> into <span class=3D"application">Lynx</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-bzlib</code></em>: Thi=
s
                enables support for linking <code class=3D"filename">libbz2=
</code> into <span class=3D"application">Lynx</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-ssl</code></em>: This
                enables support for linking SSL into <span class=3D"applica=
tion">Lynx</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-screen=3Dncursesw</cod=
e></em>: This
                switch enables the use of advanced wide-character support
                present in the system <span class=3D"application">NCurses</=
span> library. This is needed for
                proper display of characters and line wrapping in multibyte
                locales.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-locale-charset</code=
></em>: This
                switch allows <span class=3D"application">Lynx</span> to de=
duce
                the proper character encoding for terminal output from the
                current locale. A configuration step is still needed (see
                below), but unlike the situation without this switch, the
                configuration step becomes the same for all users (without
                the switch one must specify the display character set
                explicitly). This is important for environments such as a
                LiveCD, where the amount of system-specific configuration
                steps has to be reduced to the minimum.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-ipv6</code>: This switch al=
lows
                <span class=3D"application">Lynx</span> to use IPv6, along =
with
                IPv4. Use it if your ISP provides an IPv6 configuration.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-nls</code>: This switch all=
ows
                <span class=3D"application">Lynx</span> to print translated
                messages (such as questions about cookies and SSL
                certificates).
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-gnutls</code>: This enables
                experimental support for linking <span class=3D"application=
">GnuTLS</span> into <span class=3D"application">Lynx</span>. Remove the <e=
m class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-ssl</code></em> switch if you want
                to use gnutls.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>make
                install-full</strong></span>: In addition to the standard
                installation, this target installs the documentation and he=
lp
                files.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>chgrp -v -R root
                /usr/share/doc/lynx-2.9.2/lynx_doc</strong></span> : This
                command corrects the improper group ownership of installed
                documentation files.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Lynx
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"lynx-config" name=3D"lynx-config"></a>Conf=
ig
                        Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/lynx/lynx.cfg</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470503743440" name=3D"idm14047050374=
3440"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  The proper way to get the display character set is to
                  examine the current locale. However, <span class=3D"appli=
cation">Lynx</span> does not do this by default. As
                  the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user, change t=
his
                  setting:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -e '/#LOCALE=
/     a LOCALE_CHARSET:TRUE'     \
    -i /etc/lynx/lynx.cfg</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  The built-in editor in <span class=3D"application">Lynx</=
span> <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downl=
oads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#locale-wrong-multibyte-charac=
ters" title=3D"The Program Breaks Multibyte Characters or Doesn't Count Cha=
racter Cells Correctly">
                  Breaks Multibyte Characters</a>. This issue manifests
                  itself in multibyte locales, e.g., as the Backspace key n=
ot
                  erasing non-ASCII characters properly, and as incorrect
                  data being sent to the network when one edits the content=
s
                  of text areas. The only solution to this problem is to
                  configure <span class=3D"application">Lynx</span> to use =
an
                  external editor (bound to the <span class=3D"quote">=E2=
=80=9C<span class=3D"quote">Ctrl+X e</span>=E2=80=9D</span> key
                  combination by default). Still as the <code class=3D"syst=
emitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -e '/#DEFAUL=
T_ED/ a DEFAULT_EDITOR:vi'       \
    -i /etc/lynx/lynx.cfg</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  <span class=3D"application">Lynx</span> handles the follo=
wing
                  values of the DEFAULT_EDITOR option specially by adding
                  cursor-positioning arguments: <code class=3D"literal">ema=
cs</code>, <code class=3D"literal">jed</code>,
                  <code class=3D"literal">jmacs</code>, <code class=3D"lite=
ral">joe</code>, <code class=3D"literal">jove</code>,
                  <code class=3D"literal">jpico</code>, <code class=3D"lite=
ral">jstar</code>, <code class=3D"literal">nano</code>,
                  <code class=3D"literal">pico</code>, <code class=3D"liter=
al">rjoe</code>, <code class=3D"literal">vi</code> (but
                  not <code class=3D"literal">vim</code>: in order to posit=
ion
                  the cursor in <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linux=
fromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#vim=
" title=3D"Vim-9.1.0660">Vim-9.1.0660</a>, set this option to
                  <code class=3D"literal">vi</code>).
                </p>
                <p>
                  By default, <span class=3D"application">Lynx</span> doesn=
't
                  save cookies between sessions. Again as the <code class=
=3D"systemitem">root</code> user, change this setting:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -e '/#PERSIS=
T/    a PERSISTENT_COOKIES:TRUE' \
    -i /etc/lynx/lynx.cfg</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Many other system-wide settings such as proxies can also =
be
                  set in the <code class=3D"filename">/etc/lynx/lynx.cfg</c=
ode>
                  file.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
