        <div class=3D"titlepage">
          <div>
            <div>
              <h2 class=3D"title">
                <a id=3D"basicnet-mailnews" name=3D"basicnet-mailnews"></a>=
Chapter&nbsp;19.&nbsp;Mail/News
                Clients
              </h2>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"chapter" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
          <p>
            Mail Clients help you retrieve (Fetchmail), sort (Procmail), re=
ad
            and compose responses (Heirloom mailx, Mutt, Pine, Kmail, Balsa=
,
            Evolution, SeaMonkey) to email.
          </p>
          <p>
            News clients also help you retrieve, sort, read and compose
            responses, but these messages travel through USENET (a worldwid=
e
            bulletin board system) using the Network News Transfer Protocol
            (NNTP).
          </p>
          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"fetchmail" name=3D"fetchmail"></a>Fetchmail-6.4.=
39
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Fetchmail
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">Fetchmail</span> package
                contains a mail retrieval program. It retrieves mail from
                remote mail servers and forwards it to the local (client)
                machine's delivery system, so it can then be read by normal
                mail user agents.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470503696304" name=3D"idm140470503696304"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://d=
ownloads.sourceforge.net/fetchmail/fetchmail-6.4.39.tar.xz">
                      https://downloads.sourceforge.net/fetchmail/fetchmail=
-6.4.39.tar.xz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 33a916a14b91ba932b970fe02d28f058
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 1.2 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 12 MB including tests
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.1 SBU including tests
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470503688960" name=3D"idm140470503688960"></=
a>Fetchmail Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470503688272" name=3D"idm140470503688272"></=
a>Recommended
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                a local MDA (<a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfro=
mscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#procma=
il" title=3D"Procmail-3.24">Procmail-3.24</a>)
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470503686048" name=3D"idm140470503686048"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#mitkrb" title=3D"MI=
T Kerberos V5-1.21.3">MIT Kerberos V5-1.21.3</a> and
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"http://www.citi.umich.edu/projec=
ts/nfsv4/linux/">libgssapi</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470503683312" name=3D"idm140470503683312"></=
a>Optional (for running fetchmailconf)
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#python3" title=3D"P=
ython-3.12.5">Python-3.12.5</a>, built after <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"http=
s://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-noch=
unks.html#tk" title=3D"Tk-8.6.14">Tk-8.6.14</a>, with the
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://python-future.org/">py-f=
uture</a> package
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Fetchmail
              </h3>
              <p>
                Create a dedicated user for the fetchmail program. Issue th=
e
                following commands as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</=
code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">useradd -c "Fetchm=
ail User" -d /dev/null -g nogroup \
        -s /bin/false -u 38 fetchmail</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Fetchmail</span> by run=
ning
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">PYTHON=3Dpyth=
on3 \
./configure --prefix=3D/usr \
            --enable-fallback=3Dprocmail &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install      =
                            &amp;&amp;
chown -v fetchmail:nogroup /usr/bin/fetchmail</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>PYTHON=3Dpython3</code></em>:=
 a
                version of Python is <span class=3D"emphasis"><em>required<=
/em></span>, but only used to install
                a module to allow fetchmailconf to be run. That module is
                unmaintained and should not be used.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-fallback=3Dprocmail<=
/code></em>:
                This tells <span class=3D"application">Fetchmail</span> to =
hand
                incoming mail to <span class=3D"application">Procmail</span=
>
                for delivery, if the port 25 mail server is not present or
                not responding.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Fetchmail
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"fetchmail-config" name=3D"fetchmail-config=
"></a>Config Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">~/.fetchmailrc</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470503658896" name=3D"idm14047050365=
8896"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class=3D"admon note">
                  <h3>
                    Note
                  </h3>
                  <p>
                    If you are connecting to a mailserver that supports
                    SSL/TLS-wrapped or "implicit" mode on a dedicated port
                    (default 993) you should use <span class=3D"command"><s=
trong>fetchmail --ssl</strong></span> or add
                    the option 'ssl' in an rcfile.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; ~/=
.fetchmailrc &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">
# The logfile needs to exist when fetchmail is invoked, otherwise it will
# dump the details to the screen. As with all logs, you will need to rotate
# or clear it from time to time.
set logfile fetchmail.log
set no bouncemail
# You probably want to set your local username as the postmaster
set postmaster <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;username&gt;</code></em>

poll SERVERNAME :
    user <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;isp_username&gt;</code></em> p=
ass <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;password&gt;</code></em>;
    mda "/usr/bin/procmail -f %F -d %T";</code>
EOF

touch ~/fetchmail.log       &amp;&amp;
chmod -v 0600 ~/.fetchmailrc</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  This is an example configuration that should suffice for
                  most people. You can add as many users and servers as you
                  need using the same syntax.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <span class=3D"command"><strong>man
                  fetchmail</strong></span>: Look for the section near the
                  bottom named <span class=3D"emphasis"><em>CONFIGURATION
                  EXAMPLES</em></span>. It gives some quick examples. There
                  are countless other configuration options once you get us=
ed
                  to it.
                </p>
                <p>
                  If you expect to receive very little mail you can invoke
                  fetchmail when you wish to receive any incoming mail. Mor=
e
                  commonly, it is either invoked in daemon mode with the
                  <code class=3D"literal">-d</code> option either on the
                  command line, or in <code class=3D"filename">.fetchmailrc=
</code> (see 'DAEMON MODE' in man
                  fetchmailconf), or alternatively it is invoked from a cro=
n
                  job.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">fetchmail and fetchmailconf</sp=
an>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Libraries:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">None</span>
                  </div>
