        <div class=3D"titlepage">
          <div>
            <div>
              <h2 class=3D"title">
                <a id=3D"server-mail" name=3D"server-mail"></a>Chapter&nbsp=
;21.&nbsp;Mail Server Software
              </h2>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"chapter" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
          <p>
            MTAs are the programs which transport mail from one machine to
            the other. The traditional MTA is <span class=3D"application">S=
endmail</span>, however there are several other
            choices.
          </p>
          <p>
            In addition to the SMTP servers, there is also a POP/IMAP serve=
r
            (Dovecot).
          </p>
          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"dovecot" name=3D"dovecot"></a>Dovecot-2.3.21.1
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Dovecot
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"application">Dovecot</span> is an Internet
                Message Access Protocol (IMAP) and Post Office Protocol (PO=
P)
                server, written primarily with security in mind. <span clas=
s=3D"application">Dovecot</span> aims to be lightweight, fast and
                easy to set up as well as highly configurable and easily
                extensible with plugins.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470502548656" name=3D"idm140470502548656"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
