            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Dovecot
              </h3>
              <p>
                There should be dedicated users and groups for unprivileged
                Dovecot processes and for processing users' logins. Issue t=
he
                following commands as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</=
code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -g 42 dov=
ecot &amp;&amp;
useradd -c "Dovecot unprivileged user" -d /dev/null -u 42 \
        -g dovecot -s /bin/false dovecot &amp;&amp;
groupadd -g 43 dovenull &amp;&amp;
useradd -c "Dovecot login user" -d /dev/null -u 43 \
        -g dovenull -s /bin/false dovenull</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                First, apply a patch to fix problems with OpenSSL-3:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">patch -Np1 -i=
 ../dovecot-2.3.21.1-openssl3_fixes-1.patch</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Next, apply a patch to fix a security vulnerability:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">patch -Np1 -i=
 ../dovecot-2.3.21.1-security_fix-1.patch</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Dovecot</span> by runni=
ng
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">CPPFLAGS=3D"-=
I/usr/include/tirpc" \
LDFLAGS+=3D" -ltirpc" \
./configure --prefix=3D/usr                          \
            --sysconfdir=3D/etc                      \
            --localstatedir=3D/var                   \
            --with-systemd=3Dno                      \
            --docdir=3D/usr/share/doc/dovecot-2.3.21.1 \
            --disable-static &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue <span class=3D"command"><strong>=
make
                -k check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>CPPFLAGS=3D...
                LDFLAGS+=3D...</strong></span>: build with libtirpc instead=
 of
                the recently removed RPC code provided by GlibC.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-static</code></em>:
                This switch prevents installation of static versions of the
                libraries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-ldap</code>: This switch enab=
les
                <span class=3D"application">OpenLDAP</span> authentication
                support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-pgsql</code>: This switch ena=
bles
                <span class=3D"application">PostgreSQL</span> database supp=
ort.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-mysql</code>: This switch ena=
bles
                <span class=3D"application">MySQL</span> database support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-sqlite</code>: This switch
                enables <span class=3D"application">SQLite</span> database
                support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-lucene</code>: This switch
                enables <span class=3D"application">CLucene</span> full tex=
t
                search support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-lua</code>: This switch enabl=
es
                <span class=3D"application">Lua</span> plugin support. This
                includes a mail and push notification plugin.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Dovecot
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"dovecot-config" name=3D"dovecot-config"></=
a>Config Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/dovecot/dovecot.conf</code>=
,
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/dovecot/conf.d/*</code>, an=
d
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/dovecot/local.conf</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470502481712" name=3D"idm14047050248=
1712"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Copy an example configuration, which you can use as a
                  starting point:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cp -rv /usr/shar=
e/doc/dovecot-2.3.21.1/example-config/* /etc/dovecot</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  The following configuration is a simple proof of concept
                  with IMAP service using local users for authentication an=
d
                  mailbox location. Reading files from the <code class=3D"f=
ilename">conf.d</code> directory is commented out since
                  the included example configuration requires <span class=
=3D"application">OpenSSL</span> and <span class=3D"application">Linux PAM</=
span>.
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -i '/^\!incl=
ude / s/^/#/' /etc/dovecot/dovecot.conf &amp;&amp;
chmod -v 1777 /var/mail &amp;&amp;
cat &gt; /etc/dovecot/local.conf &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">protocols =3D imap
ssl =3D no
# The next line is only needed if you have no IPv6 network interfaces
listen =3D *
mail_location =3D mbox:~/Mail:INBOX=3D/var/mail/%u
userdb {
  driver =3D passwd
}
passdb {
  driver =3D shadow
}</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  You will definitely want to read the official documentati=
on
                  at <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://wiki2.dovecot.org/"=
>https://wiki2.dovecot.org/</a>
                  if you plan to use <span class=3D"application">Dovecot</s=
pan>
                  in a production environment.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"dovecot-init" name=3D"dovecot-init"></a><s=
pan class=3D"phrase">Boot
                        Script</span>
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  If you want the <span class=3D"application">Dovecot</span=
>
                  server to start automatically when the system is booted,
                  install the <code class=3D"filename">/etc/rc.d/init.d/dov=
ecot</code> init script
                  included in the <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.lin=
uxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#b=
ootscripts" title=3D"BLFS Boot Scripts">blfs-bootscripts-20240416</a> packa=
ge.
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-dov=
ecot</kbd></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
