            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Exim
              </h3>
              <p>
                Before building <span class=3D"application">Exim</span>, as=
 the
                <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user you should crea=
te
                the group and user <code class=3D"systemitem">exim</code> w=
hich
                will run the <span class=3D"command"><strong>exim</strong><=
/span> daemon:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -g 31 exi=
m &amp;&amp;
useradd -d /dev/null -c "Exim Daemon" -g exim -s /bin/false -u 31 exim</kbd=
></pre>
              <p>
                Configure <span class=3D"application">Exim</span> with the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -e 's,^BI=
N_DIR.*$,BIN_DIRECTORY=3D/usr/sbin,'    \
    -e 's,^CONF.*$,CONFIGURE_FILE=3D/etc/exim.conf,' \
    -e 's,^EXIM_USER.*$,EXIM_USER=3Dexim,'           \
    -e '/# USE_OPENSSL/s,^#,,' src/EDITME &gt; Local/Makefile &amp;&amp;

printf "USE_GDBM =3D yes\nDBMLIB =3D -lgdbm\n" &gt;&gt; Local/Makefile
</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you want to add <span class=3D"application">Linux PAM</s=
pan>
                support, also run the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -i '/# SU=
PPORT_PAM=3Dyes/s,^#,,' Local/Makefile
echo "EXTRALIBS=3D-lpam" &gt;&gt; Local/Makefile
</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Build <span class=3D"application">Exim</span> with the
                following command:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make</kbd></p=
re>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install      =
                              &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644 doc/exim.8 /usr/share/man/man8 &amp;&amp;

install -vdm 755    /usr/share/doc/exim-4.98 &amp;&amp;
cp      -Rv doc/*   /usr/share/doc/exim-4.98 &amp;&amp;

ln -sfv exim /usr/sbin/sendmail                 &amp;&amp;
install -v -d -m750 -o exim -g exim /var/spool/exim</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sed -e ... &gt;
                Local/Makefile</strong></span>: Most of <span class=3D"appl=
ication">Exim</span>'s configuration options are defined
                in <code class=3D"filename">Local/Makefile</code>, which is
                created from the <code class=3D"filename">src/EDITME</code>
                file. This command specifies the minimum set of options.
                Descriptions for the options are listed below.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>printf ... &gt;
                Local/Makefile</strong></span>: Setting those variables
                allows to use GDBM instead of the default Berkeley DB. Remo=
ve
                this command if you have installed <a class=3D"ulink" href=
=3D"https://anduin.linuxfromscratch.org/BLFS/bdb/db-5.3.28.tar.gz">
                Berkeley DB</a> (deprecated).
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>BIN_DIRECTORY=3D/usr/sbin</co=
de></em>: This
                installs all of <span class=3D"application">Exim</span>'s
                binaries and scripts in <code class=3D"filename">/usr/sbin<=
/code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>CONFIGURE_FILE=3D/etc/exim.co=
nf</code></em>:
                This installs <span class=3D"application">Exim</span>'s mai=
n
                configuration file in <code class=3D"filename">/etc</code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>EXIM_USER=3Dexim</code></em>:=
 This
                tells <span class=3D"application">Exim</span> that after th=
e
                daemon no longer needs <code class=3D"systemitem">root</cod=
e>
                privileges, the process needs to hand off the daemon to the
                <code class=3D"systemitem">exim</code> user.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>USE_OPENSSL</code></em>:
                uncommenting <code class=3D"option">USE_OPENSSL=3Dyes</code=
> and
                <code class=3D"option">USE_OPNSSL_PC=3Dyes</code> tells the=
 build
                system to use <span class=3D"application">OpenSSL</span>, a=
nd
                to find the needed libraries with <span class=3D"applicatio=
n">pkg-config</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Uncomment <code class=3D"option">EXIM_MONITOR</code>: This
                allows building the <span class=3D"application">Exim</span>
                monitor program, which requires <span class=3D"application"=
>X
                Window System</span> support, and is commented out by
                default.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>ln -sfv exim
                /usr/sbin/sendmail</strong></span>: Creates a link to
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sendmail</strong></span> fo=
r
                applications which need it. <span class=3D"application">Exi=
m</span> will accept most <span class=3D"application">Sendmail</span> comma=
nd-line options.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>install -v -m750 -o exim -g
                exim /var/spool/exim</strong></span>: Since /var/spool is
                owned by root and this version of <span class=3D"command"><=
strong>exim</strong></span> drops <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> pr=
ivileges early, to run as user
                <code class=3D"systemitem">exim</code>, it cannot create th=
e
                <code class=3D"filename">/var/spool/exim</code> directory. =
As a
                work around, it is created manually.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Adding Additional Functionality
              </h3>
              <p>
                To utilize some or all of the dependency packages, you'll
                need to modify <code class=3D"filename">Local/Makefile</cod=
e>
                to include the appropriate directives and parameters to lin=
k
                additional libraries before you build <span class=3D"applic=
ation">Exim</span>. <code class=3D"filename">Local/Makefile</code> is heavi=
ly commented with
                instructions on how to do this. Listed below is additional
                information to help you link these dependency packages or a=
dd
                additional functionality.
              </p>
              <p>
                If you wish to build and install the <code class=3D"filenam=
e">.info</code> documentation, refer to <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://=
exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch04.html#SECTinsinfdoc">
                https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch04.htm=
l#SECTinsinfdoc</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                If you wish to build in Exim's interfaces for calling virus
                and spam scanning software directly from access control
                lists, uncomment the <code class=3D"option">WITH_CONTENT_SC=
AN=3Dyes</code> parameter and review
                the information found at <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https:/=
/exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch45.html">
                https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch45.htm=
l</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                To use a backend database other than <span class=3D"applica=
tion">GDBM</span> , see the instructions at <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"http=
s://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch04.html#SECTdb">
                https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch04.htm=
l#SECTdb</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                For SSL functionality, see the instructions at <a class=3D"=
ulink" href=3D"https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch04.html=
#SECTinctlsssl">
                https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch04.htm=
l#SECTinctlsssl</a>
                and <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://exim.org/exim-html-4=
.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch42.html">
                https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch42.htm=
l</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                For <span class=3D"application">tcpwrappers</span>
                functionality, see the instructions at <a class=3D"ulink" h=
ref=3D"https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch04.html#SECID27=
">
                https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch04.htm=
l#SECID27</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                For information about adding authentication mechanisms to t=
he
                build, see chapters 33=E2=80=9441 of <a class=3D"ulink" hre=
f=3D"https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/index.html">
                https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/index.ht=
ml</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                For information about linking <span class=3D"application">L=
inux-PAM</span>, refer to the instructions
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/=
doc/html/spec_html/ch11.html#SECTexpcond">
                https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch11.htm=
l#SECTexpcond</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                For information about linking database engine libraries use=
d
                for <span class=3D"application">Exim</span> name lookups, s=
ee
                the instructions at <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://exim=
.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch09.html">
                https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch09.htm=
l</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                If you wish to add <span class=3D"application">Readline</sp=
an>
                support to <span class=3D"application">Exim</span> when inv=
oked
                in <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D"quote">tes=
t
                expansion</span>=E2=80=9D</span> (<code class=3D"option">-b=
e</code>)
                mode, see the information in the <code class=3D"option">-be=
</code> section of <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://exim.org/exim-html-4.=
98/doc/html/spec_html/ch05.html#id2525974">
                https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch05.htm=
l#id2525974</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                You may wish to modify the default configuration and send l=
og
                files to syslog instead of the default <code class=3D"filen=
ame">/var/spool/exim/log</code> directory. See the
                information at <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://exim.org/=
exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch-log_files.html">
                https://exim.org/exim-html-4.98/doc/html/spec_html/ch-log_f=
iles.html</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                A wealth of information can be also found at the <a class=
=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://github.com/Exim/exim/wiki">Exim
                Wiki</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Exim
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"exim-config" name=3D"exim-config"></a>Conf=
ig
                        Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/exim.conf</code> and
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/aliases</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470502317968" name=3D"idm14047050231=
7968"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Review the file <code class=3D"filename">/etc/exim.conf</=
code>, and modify any settings
                  to suit your needs. Note that the default configuration
                  assumes that the <code class=3D"filename">/var/mail</code=
>
                  directory is world writable, but has the sticky bit set. =
If
                  you want to use the default configuration, issue as the
                  <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">chmod -v a+wt /v=
ar/mail</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  A default (nothing but comments) <code class=3D"filename"=
>/etc/aliases</code> file is installed during the
                  package installation if this file did not exist on your
                  system. Create the necessary aliases and start the
                  <span class=3D"application">Exim</span> daemon using the
                  following commands:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt;&gt; /et=
c/aliases &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">postmaster: root
MAILER-DAEMON: root</code>
EOF
/usr/sbin/exim -bd -q15m</kbd></pre>
                <div class=3D"admon note">
                  <h3>
                    Note
                  </h3>
                  <p>
                    To protect an existing <code class=3D"filename">/etc/al=
iases</code> file, the command above
                    appends these aliases to it. This file should be checke=
d
                    and duplicate aliases removed, if present.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <p>
                  The <span class=3D"command"><strong>/usr/sbin/exim -bd
                  -q15m</strong></span> command starts the <span class=3D"a=
pplication">Exim</span> daemon with a 15 minute interval
                  in processing the mail queue. Adjust this parameter to su=
it
                  your desires.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470502304560" name=3D"idm14047050230=
4560"></a>Linux PAM Configuration
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  If you have built <span class=3D"application">Exim</span>
                  with <span class=3D"application">Linux PAM</span> support=
,
                  you need to create a <span class=3D"application">PAM</spa=
n>
                  configuration file to get it working correctly with BLFS.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Issue the following command as the <code class=3D"systemi=
tem">root</code> user to create the configuration
                  file for <span class=3D"application">Linux PAM</span>:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/pa=
m.d/exim &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal"># Begin /etc/pam.d/exim

auth    include system-auth
account include system-account
session include system-session

# End /etc/pam.d/exim</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"exim-init" name=3D"exim-init"></a><span cl=
ass=3D"phrase">Boot Script</span>
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  To automatically start <span class=3D"command"><strong>ex=
im</strong></span> at boot, install the
                  <span class=3D"phrase"><code class=3D"filename">/etc/rc.d=
/init.d/exim</code> init script</span>
                  included in the <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.lin=
uxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#b=
ootscripts" title=3D"BLFS Boot Scripts">blfs-bootscripts-20240416</a> packa=
ge:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-exi=
m</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  The bootscript also starts the <span class=3D"application=
">Exim</span> daemon and dispatches a queue
                  runner process every 15 minutes. Modify the <code class=
=3D"option">-q<em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;time
                  interval&gt;</code></em></code> parameter in <code class=
=3D"filename">/etc/rc.d/init.d/exim</code>, if necessary for
                  your installation.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
