            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of MariaDB
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"admon warning">
                <h3>
                  Warning
                </h3>
                <p>
                  MariaDB and MySQL cannot be installed on the same system
                  without extensive changes to the build configuration of o=
ne
                  of the two applications.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                For security reasons, running the server as an unprivileged
                user and group is strongly encouraged. Issue the following
                (as <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code>) to create the u=
ser
                and group:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -g 40 mys=
ql &amp;&amp;
useradd -c "MySQL Server" -d /srv/mysql -g mysql -s /bin/false -u 40 mysql<=
/kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">MariaDB</span> by runni=
ng
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

cmake -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease                       \
      -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=3D/usr                      \
      -D GRN_LOG_PATH=3D/var/log/groonga.log              \
      -D INSTALL_DOCDIR=3Dshare/doc/mariadb-10.11.8       \
      -D INSTALL_DOCREADMEDIR=3Dshare/doc/mariadb-10.11.8 \
      -D INSTALL_MANDIR=3Dshare/man                       \
      -D INSTALL_MYSQLSHAREDIR=3Dshare/mysql              \
      -D INSTALL_MYSQLTESTDIR=3Dshare/mysql/test          \
      -D INSTALL_PAMDIR=3Dlib/security                    \
      -D INSTALL_PAMDATADIR=3D/etc/security               \
      -D INSTALL_PLUGINDIR=3Dlib/mysql/plugin             \
      -D INSTALL_SBINDIR=3Dsbin                           \
      -D INSTALL_SCRIPTDIR=3Dbin                          \
      -D INSTALL_SQLBENCHDIR=3Dshare/mysql/bench          \
      -D INSTALL_SUPPORTFILESDIR=3Dshare/mysql            \
      -D MYSQL_DATADIR=3D/srv/mysql                       \
      -D MYSQL_UNIX_ADDR=3D/run/mysqld/mysqld.sock        \
      -D WITH_EXTRA_CHARSETS=3Dcomplex                    \
      -D WITH_EMBEDDED_SERVER=3DON                        \
      -D SKIP_TESTS=3DON                                  \
      -D TOKUDB_OK=3D0                                    \
      .. &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make test</strong></span>. One test,
                test-connect, is known to fail.
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  A more extensive set of tests can be run with the
                  following:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">pushd mysql=
-test
./mtr --parallel <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;N&gt;</code></em> --me=
m --force
popd</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Where N is the number of tests to run in parallel. Over
                  5400 tests are run in about 24 SBU with N=3D4. A few test=
s
                  may fail, mainly due to character set issues.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
              <p>
                If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#linux-p=
am" title=3D"Linux-PAM-1.6.1">Linux-PAM-1.6.1</a> installed, move the PAM
                module and configuration file installed by this package as
                the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mv -v /usr/sh=
are/pam_use_map.so /lib/security &amp;&amp;
mv -v /usr/share/user_map.conf /etc/security</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                WITH_EMBEDDED_SERVER=3DON</code></em>: This switch enables
                compiling the embedded server library needed by certain
                applications, such as <span class=3D"application">Amarok</s=
pan>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                WITH_EXTRA_CHARSETS=3Dcomplex</code></em>: This switch enab=
les
                support for the complex character sets.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D SKIP_TESTS=3DON</code></em=
>:
                This switch disables tests for MariaDB Connector/C which ar=
e
                not supported without additional setup.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D WITHOUT_SERVER=3DON</code>: Use t=
his
                switch if you don't want the server and would like to build
                the client only.
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  There are numerous options available to <span class=3D"co=
mmand"><strong>cmake</strong></span>. Check the output
                  of the <span class=3D"command"><strong>cmake .
                  -LH</strong></span> for additional customization options.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring MySQL
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"mariadb-config" name=3D"mariadb-config"></=
a>Config Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/mysql/my.cnf</code> and
                  <code class=3D"filename">~/.my.cnf</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470501647072" name=3D"idm14047050164=
7072"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Create a basic <code class=3D"filename">/etc/mysql/my.cnf=
</code> file using the
                  following command as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root<=
/code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -dm 7=
55 /etc/mysql &amp;&amp;
cat &gt; /etc/mysql/my.cnf &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal"># Begin /etc/mysql/my.cnf

# The following options will be passed to all MySQL clients
[client]
#password       =3D your_password
port            =3D 3306
socket          =3D /run/mysqld/mysqld.sock

# The MySQL server
[mysqld]
port            =3D 3306
socket          =3D /run/mysqld/mysqld.sock
datadir         =3D /srv/mysql
skip-external-locking
key_buffer_size =3D 16M
max_allowed_packet =3D 1M
sort_buffer_size =3D 512K
net_buffer_length =3D 16K
myisam_sort_buffer_size =3D 8M

# Don't listen on a TCP/IP port at all.
skip-networking

# required unique id between 1 and 2^32 - 1
server-id       =3D 1

# Uncomment the following if you are using BDB tables
#bdb_cache_size =3D 4M
#bdb_max_lock =3D 10000

# InnoDB tables are now used by default
innodb_data_home_dir =3D /srv/mysql
innodb_log_group_home_dir =3D /srv/mysql
# All the innodb_xxx values below are the default ones:
innodb_data_file_path =3D ibdata1:12M:autoextend
# You can set .._buffer_pool_size up to 50 - 80 %
# of RAM but beware of setting memory usage too high
innodb_buffer_pool_size =3D 128M
innodb_log_file_size =3D 48M
innodb_log_buffer_size =3D 16M
innodb_flush_log_at_trx_commit =3D 1
innodb_lock_wait_timeout =3D 50

[mysqldump]
quick
max_allowed_packet =3D 16M

[mysql]
no-auto-rehash
# Remove the next comment character if you are not familiar with SQL
#safe-updates

[isamchk]
key_buffer =3D 20M
sort_buffer_size =3D 20M
read_buffer =3D 2M
write_buffer =3D 2M

[myisamchk]
key_buffer_size =3D 20M
sort_buffer_size =3D 20M
read_buffer =3D 2M
write_buffer =3D 2M

[mysqlhotcopy]
interactive-timeout

# End /etc/mysql/my.cnf</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  You can now install a database and change the ownership t=
o
                  the unprivileged user and group (perform as the
                  <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user):
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mysql_install_db=
 --basedir=3D/usr --datadir=3D/srv/mysql --user=3Dmysql &amp;&amp;
chown -R mysql:mysql /srv/mysql</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Further configuration requires that the <span class=3D"ap=
plication">MariaDB</span> server is running. Start the
                  server using the following commands as the <code class=3D=
"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -m755=
 -o mysql -g mysql -d /run/mysqld &amp;&amp;
mysqld_safe --user=3Dmysql 2&gt;&amp;1 &gt;/dev/null &amp;</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  A default installation does not set up a password for the
                  administrator, so use the following command as the
                  <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user to set one.
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mysqladmin -u ro=
ot password</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Configuration of the server is now finished. Shut the
                  server down using the following command as the <code clas=
s=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mysqladmin -p sh=
utdown</kbd></pre>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"mariadb-init" name=3D"mariadb-init"></a><s=
pan class=3D"phrase">Boot
                        Script</span>
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Install the <span class=3D"phrase"><code class=3D"filenam=
e">/etc/rc.d/init.d/mysql</code> init script</span>
                  included in the <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.lin=
uxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#b=
ootscripts" title=3D"BLFS Boot Scripts">blfs-bootscripts-20240416</a> packa=
ge
                  as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user to sta=
rt
                  the <span class=3D"application">MariaDB</span> server dur=
ing
                  system boot-up.
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-mys=
ql</kbd></pre>
                <div class=3D"admon note">
                  <h3>
                    Note
                  </h3>
                  <p>
                    If you have an existing database already and this
                    installation of binaries was just an upgrade to a newer
                    version, check the upstream documentation for upgrading=
.
                    It is recommended to run:
                  </p>
                  <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mariadb-u=
pgrade</kbd></pre>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">aria_chk, aria_dump_log,
                    aria_ftdump, aria_pack, aria_read_log, aria_s3_copy,
                    galera_new_cluster, galera_recovery, innochecksum,
                    mariabackup, mariadb, mariadbd, mariadb-access,
                    mariadb-admin, mariadb-backup, mariadb-binlog,
                    mariadb-check, mariadb-client-test,
                    mariadb-client-test-embedded, mariadb-conv,
                    mariadb-convert-table-format, mariadb-find-rows,
                    mariadbd-multi, mariadbd-safe, mariadbd-safe-helper,
                    mariadb-dump, mariadb-dumpslow, mariadb-embedded,
                    mariadb-fix-extensions, mariadb-hotcopy, mariadb-import=
,
                    mariadb-install-db, mariadb-ldb, mariadb-plugin,
                    mariadb-secure-installation, mariadb-setpermission,
                    mariadb-service-convert, mariadb-show, mariadb-slap,
                    mariadb-test, mariadb-test-embedded,
                    mariadb-tzinfo-to-sql, mariadb-upgrade, mariadb-waitpid=
,
                    mariadb_config, mbstream, msql2mysql, my_print_defaults=
,
                    myisamchk, myisam_ftdump, myisamlog, myisampack,
                    mysql_config, mytop, perror, replace, resolve_stack_dum=
p,
                    resolveip, sst_dump, wsrep_sst_common,
                    wsrep_sst_mariabackup, wsrep_sst_mysqldump, and
                    wsrep_sst_rsync</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Libraries:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">libmariadbclient.a, libmariadb.=
so,
                    libmariadbd.so, libmysqlclient.a, libmysqlclient_r.a
                    (symbolic links to libmariadbclient.a), libmysqld.{so,a=
},
                    libmysqlservices.a, and several under
                    /usr/lib/mysql/plugin/</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Directories:</stro=
ng>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">/etc/mysql,
                    /usr/{include,lib,share}/mysql,
                    /usr/share/groonga{-normalizer-mysql}, and
                    /usr/share/doc/mariadb-10.11.8</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470501609056" name=3D"idm140470501609056"></=
a>Short Descriptions
              </h4>
              <p>
                There are several symlinks from mysql* to their mariadb
                counterparts. These are maintained for compatibility.
              </p>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">Perl</span> DBI modules mus=
t be
                installed for some of the <span class=3D"application">Maria=
DB</span> support programs to function
                properly.
              </p>
              <div class=3D"variablelist">
                <h4>
                  <a id=3D"idm140470501604768" name=3D"idm140470501604768">=
</a>Short Descriptions
                </h4>
                <table border=3D"0" class=3D"variablelist">
                  <colgroup>
                    <col align=3D"left" valign=3D"top">
                    <col>
                  </colgroup>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"aria_chk-mariadb" name=3D"aria_chk-maria=
db"></a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>aria_chk</stro=
ng></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is used to check, repair, optimize, sort and get
                          information about Aria tables
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"aria_dump_log-mariadb" name=3D"aria_dump=
_log-mariadb"></a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>aria=
_dump_log</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a tool to dump the contents of Aria log pages
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"aria_ftdump-mariadb" name=3D"aria_ftdump=
-mariadb"></a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>aria_ftd=
ump</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          displays full-text index information
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"aria_pack-mariadb" name=3D"aria_pack-mar=
iadb"></a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>aria_pack</s=
trong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a tool to generate compressed, read-only Aria
                          tables
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"aria_read_log-mariadb" name=3D"aria_read=
_log-mariadb"></a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>aria=
_read_log</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          displays Aria log file contents
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"aria_s3_copy-mariadb" name=3D"aria_s3_co=
py-mariadb"></a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>aria_s=
3_copy</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          copies an aria table to and from AWS S3
                        </p>
                      </td>
