            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Unbound
              </h3>
              <p>
                There should be a dedicated user and group to take control =
of
                the <span class=3D"command"><strong>unbound</strong></span>
                daemon after it is started. Issue the following commands as
                the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -g 88 unb=
ound &amp;&amp;
useradd -c "Unbound DNS Resolver" -d /var/lib/unbound -u 88 \
        -g unbound -s /bin/false unbound</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Unbound</span> by runni=
ng
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr     \
            --sysconfdir=3D/etc \
            --disable-static  \
            --with-pidfile=3D/run/unbound.pid &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#doxygen=
" title=3D"Doxygen-1.12.0">Doxygen-1.12.0</a> package installed and
                want to build html documentation, run the following command=
:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make doc</kbd=
></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue <span class=3D"command"><strong>=
make
                check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install &amp;=
&amp;
mv -v /usr/sbin/unbound-host /usr/bin/</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you built the documentation, install it by running the
                following commands as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</=
code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -m755 -=
d /usr/share/doc/unbound-1.21.0 &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644 doc/html/* /usr/share/doc/unbound-1.21.0</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-static</code></em>:
                This switch prevents installation of static versions of the
                libraries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-libevent</code>: This option
                enables libevent support allowing use of large outgoing por=
t
                ranges.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--with-pyunbound</code>: This option
                enables building of the Python bindings.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Unbound
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"unbound-config" name=3D"unbound-config"></=
a>Config Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/unbound/unbound.conf</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470500652448" name=3D"idm14047050065=
2448"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  In the default configuration, <span class=3D"command"><st=
rong>unbound</strong></span> will bind to
                  localhost (127.0.0.1 IP address) and allow recursive
                  queries only from localhost clients. If you want to use
                  <span class=3D"command"><strong>unbound</strong></span> f=
or
                  local DNS resolution, run the following command as the
                  <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">echo "nameserver=
 127.0.0.1" &gt; /etc/resolv.conf</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  For advanced configuration see <code class=3D"filename">/=
etc/unbound/unbound.conf</code> file and the
                  documentation.
                </p>
                <p>
                  When <span class=3D"application">Unbound</span> is instal=
led,
                  some package builds fail if the file <code class=3D"filen=
ame">/etc/unbound/root.key</code> is not found. This
                  file is created by running the boot script (install
                  instructions below). Alternatively, it can be created by
                  running the following command as the <code class=3D"syste=
mitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">unbound-anc=
hor</kbd></pre>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"unbound-init" name=3D"unbound-init"></a><s=
pan class=3D"phrase">Boot
                        Script</span>
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  If you want the <span class=3D"application">Unbound</span=
>
                  server to start automatically when the system is booted,
                  install the <span class=3D"phrase"><code class=3D"filenam=
e">/etc/rc.d/init.d/unbound</code> init
                  script</span> included in the <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"h=
ttps://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-n=
ochunks.html#bootscripts" title=3D"BLFS Boot Scripts">blfs-bootscripts-2024=
0416</a> package:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-unb=
ound</kbd></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
