              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">xwayland</span> by runn=
ing
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -i '/inst=
all_man/,$d' meson.build &amp;&amp;

mkdir build &amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup ..                       \
      --prefix=3D$XORG_PREFIX          \
      --buildtype=3Drelease            \
      -D xkb_output_dir=3D/var/lib/xkb &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Building the test framework needs some work. First, <a clas=
s=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://wayland.pages.freedesktop.org/weston/">weston</=
a>
                brings in several dependencies, but the number can be reduc=
ed
                by disabling unneeded features. The <span class=3D"command"=
><strong>meson</strong></span> command for a
                stripped down build of <span class=3D"application">weston</=
span> is shown in <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://gitlab.freedesktop.org=
/xorg/xserver/-/blob/xwayland-22.1/.gitlab-ci/debian-install.sh">
                Upstream continuous integration build</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Running the tests involves downloading two other frameworks=
,
                in addition to the mentioned optional dependencies:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir tools &=
amp;&amp;
pushd tools &amp;&amp;

git clone https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/piglit.git --depth 1 &amp;&am=
p;
cat &gt; piglit/piglit.conf &lt;&lt; EOF                                   =
 &amp;&amp;
<code class=3D"literal">[xts]
path=3D$(pwd)/xts
EOF</code>

git clone https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/test/xts --depth 1   &amp;&am=
p;

export DISPLAY=3D:22           &amp;&amp;
../hw/vfb/Xvfb $DISPLAY &amp;
VFB_PID=3D$!                   &amp;&amp;
cd xts                       &amp;&amp;
CFLAGS=3D-fcommon ./autogen.sh &amp;&amp;
make                         &amp;&amp;
kill $VFB_PID                &amp;&amp;
unset DISPLAY VFB_PID        &amp;&amp;
popd</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Then the tests can be run with:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">XTEST_DIR=3D$=
(pwd)/tools/xts PIGLIT_DIR=3D$(pwd)/tools/piglit ninja test</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install &amp=
;&amp;
cat &gt;&gt; /etc/sysconfig/createfiles &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">/tmp/.X11-unix dir 1777 root root</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#xorg-server" tit=
le=3D"Xorg-Server-21.1.13">Xorg-Server-21.1.13</a> is not
                installed and you do not plan to install it later, you can
                install <span class=3D"command"><strong>Xvfb</strong></span=
>
                from this package. As the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</=
code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">install -vm75=
5 hw/vfb/Xvfb /usr/bin</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sed -i '/install_man/,$d'
                meson.build</strong></span>: Prevents installing a manual
                page for <span class=3D"command"><strong>Xserver</strong></=
span>, which is also
                provided by <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#xorg-se=
rver" title=3D"Xorg-Server-21.1.13">Xorg-Server-21.1.13</a>. Remove this
                command if <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfroms=
cratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#xorg-ser=
ver" title=3D"Xorg-Server-21.1.13">Xorg-Server-21.1.13</a> is not
                installed and you don't plan to install it later.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>cat &gt;&gt;
                /etc/sysconfig/createfiles...</strong></span>: This command
                creates the <code class=3D"filename">/tmp/.X11-unix</code>
                directory at startup, and ensures that the permissions and
                ownership are correct as required by applications using
                Xwayland.
              </p>
            </div>
