</a>Kernel Configuration
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Enable the following options in the kernel configuration
                  and recompile the kernel if necessary:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"blue">D</span>evice Dr=
ivers ---&gt;
  <span class=3D"blue">I</span>nput device support ---&gt;
    -*-   <span class=3D"blue">G</span>eneric input layer (needed for keybo=
ard, mouse, ...)          [INPUT]
    &lt;*/M&gt;   <span class=3D"blue">E</span>vent interface              =
                          [INPUT_EVDEV]</pre>
                <p>
                  If you want to test this package with full coverage, the
                  following options are needed as well:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"blue">D</span>evice Dr=
ivers ---&gt;
  <span class=3D"blue">I</span>nput device support ---&gt;
    -*- <span class=3D"blue">G</span>eneric input layer (needed for keyboar=
d, mouse, ...)            [INPUT]
    [*]   M<span class=3D"blue">i</span>scellaneous devices ---&gt;        =
                        [INPUT_MISC]
      &lt;*/M&gt;   <span class=3D"blue">U</span>ser level driver support  =
                         [INPUT_UINPUT]</pre>
                <p>
                  If you build this as a module, it needs to be inserted
                  before the test suite runs.
                </p>
              </div>
