                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470498874752" name=3D"idm14047049887=
4752"></a>Installation of libevdev
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Install <span class=3D"application">libevdev</span> by
                  running the following commands:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build=
 &amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup ..                  \
      --prefix=3D$XORG_PREFIX     \
      --buildtype=3Drelease       \
      -D documentation=3Ddisabled &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  The regression tests can be run as the <code class=3D"sys=
temitem">root</code> user with <span class=3D"command"><strong>ninja test</=
strong></span>, in a
                  graphical session. You need to have enabled the
                  CONFIG_INPUT_UINPUT setting in the kernel for full test
                  coverage. If it is enabled as a module, the module is nam=
ed
                  <span class=3D"command"><strong>uinput</strong></span> an=
d
                  needs to be loaded before running the tests. Note that on
                  some systems, the tests may cause a hard lockup and requi=
re
                  a reboot. On laptops, the system will go into Sleep and
                  need to be woken up to finish the test suites.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</k=
bd></pre>
              </div>
