                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"libinput-kernel" name=3D"libinput-kernel">=
</a>Kernel Configuration for
                        Running the Libinput Test Suite
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Although libinput works with the same kernel configuratio=
n
                  used by <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromsc=
ratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libevdev"=
 title=3D"libevdev 1.13.2">libevdev-1.13.2</a>, its extensive test
                  suite requires the presence of <code class=3D"filename">/=
dev/uinput</code> (as well as both <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
valgrind" title=3D"Valgrind-3.23.0">Valgrind-3.23.0</a> and <a class=3D"xre=
f" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK=
-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libunwind" title=3D"libunwind-1.6.2">libunwind-1.6=
.2</a>).
                </p>
                <p>
                  If you wish to run the full tests, enable the following
                  option in the kernel configuration and recompile the kern=
el
                  if necessary:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"blue">D</span>evice Dr=
ivers ---&gt;
  <span class=3D"blue">I</span>nput device support ---&gt;
    -*- <span class=3D"blue">G</span>eneric input layer (needed for keyboar=
d, mouse, ...)            [INPUT]
    [*]   M<span class=3D"blue">i</span>scellaneous devices ---&gt;        =
                        [INPUT_MISC]
      &lt;*/M&gt;   <span class=3D"blue">U</span>ser level driver support  =
                         [INPUT_UINPUT]</pre>
                <p>
                  If you build this as a module, it needs to be inserted
                  before the test suite runs.
                </p>
                <p>
                  On an Xorg system you will also need to prevent the event=
s
                  generated during the test suite from interfering with you=
r
                  desktop. Copy the file <code class=3D"filename">test/50-l=
itest.conf</code> into <code class=3D"filename">${XORG_PREFIX}/share/X11/xo=
rg.conf.d</code> and
                  restart X. For further information see <a class=3D"ulink"=
 href=3D"https://wayland.freedesktop.org/libinput/doc/1.26.1/test-suite.htm=
l">
                  libinput test suite</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470498765568" name=3D"idm14047049876=
5568"></a>Installation of Libinput
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Install <span class=3D"application">libinput</span> by
                  running the following commands:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build=
 &amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup ..                  \
      --prefix=3D$XORG_PREFIX     \
      --buildtype=3Drelease       \
      -D debug-gui=3Dfalse        \
      -D tests=3Dfalse            \
      -D libwacom=3Dfalse         \
      -D udev-dir=3D/usr/lib/udev &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
                <div class=3D"admon note">
                  <h3>
                    Note
                  </h3>
                  <p>
                    If you want to run the full tests, remove -D tests from
                    the <span class=3D"command"><strong>meson</strong></spa=
n>
                    command above. Please read "kernel configuration for
                    running the libinput test suite" (above).
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    If you have enabled the full tests, you can run the mai=
n
                    tests <span class=3D"emphasis"><em>as the root
                    user</em></span> by executing: <span class=3D"command">=
<strong>ninja test</strong></span>. A very
                    large number of tests will be run. One test fails on
                    wayland.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</k=
bd></pre>
                <p>
                  If you have passed <code class=3D"option">-D
                  documentation=3Dtrue</code> to <span class=3D"command"><s=
trong>meson</strong></span>, you can install
                  the generated documentation by running the following
                  commands as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> us=
er:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -dm75=
5      /usr/share/doc/libinput-1.26.1/html &amp;&amp;
cp -rv Documentation/* /usr/share/doc/libinput-1.26.1/html</kbd></pre>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470498750672" name=3D"idm14047049875=
0672"></a>Command Explanations
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code=
></em>: Specify
                  a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the package, =
as
                  the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D debug-gui=3Dfalse</code>=
</em>:
                  This switch disables creation of a visual debug helper fo=
r
                  libinput. Remove if you want it, and you have <a class=3D=
"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-=
BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gtk3" title=3D"GTK+-3.24.43">GTK+-3.24.43</a>
                  installed.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D tests=3Dfalse</code></em=
>:
                  This switch disables compilation of the main tests. Even
                  with the tests defined as false, you can still run the
                  first four minor tests, as a regular user, but one will b=
e
                  skipped if <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfro=
mscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#pypars=
ing" title=3D"pyparsing-3.1.2">pyparsing-3.1.2</a> is not installed.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D libwacom=3Dfalse</code><=
/em>:
                  Remove this option if you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"=
https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-=
nochunks.html#libwacom" title=3D"libwacom-2.12.2">libwacom-2.12.2</a>
                  installed, or if you are installing GNOME.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                  udev-dir=3D/usr/lib/udev</code></em>: In case that the va=
lue
                  of <code class=3D"envar">XORG_PREFIX</code> is not set to
                  <code class=3D"filename">/usr</code>, this option prevent=
s
                  the package from installing Udev rules and helpers into
                  <code class=3D"filename">$XORG_PREFIX/lib/udev</code> whi=
ch
                  is not searched by Udev daemon. This option is not needed
                  for systems with <code class=3D"envar">XORG_PREFIX</code>=
 set
                  to <code class=3D"filename">/usr</code>, but does no harm=
.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"option">-D documentation=3Dtrue</code>: Th=
is
                  switch enables generation of the documentation. Add it if
                  you want to generate the documentation. You must have
                  <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.or=
g/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#doxygen" title=3D=
"Doxygen-1.12.0">Doxygen-1.12.0</a> and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://w=
ww.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.=
html#graphviz" title=3D"Graphviz-12.1.0">Graphviz-12.1.0</a> installed.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470498735024" name=3D"idm14047049873=
