              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#emacs" title=3D"Ema=
cs-29.4">Emacs-29.4</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscr=
atch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#pcre2" tit=
le=3D"PCRE2-10.44">pcre2-10.44</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.l=
inuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html=
#valgrind" title=3D"Valgrind-3.23.0">Valgrind-3.23.0</a> and
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://www.nongnu.org/man2html/=
">man2html</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of xterm
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">xterm</span> by running=
 the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -i '/v0/{=
n;s/new:/new:kb=3D^?:/}' termcap &amp;&amp;
printf '\tkbs=3D\\177,\n' &gt;&gt; terminfo &amp;&amp;

TERMINFO=3D/usr/share/terminfo \
./configure $XORG_CONFIG     \
    --with-app-defaults=3D/etc/X11/app-defaults &amp;&amp;

make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install &amp;=
&amp;

mkdir -pv /usr/share/applications &amp;&amp;
cp -v *.desktop /usr/share/applications/</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sed -i ...
                termcap</strong></span>, <span class=3D"command"><strong>pr=
intf
                ... &gt;&gt; terminfo</strong></span>: These commands modif=
y
                the terminal description so that the Backspace key is
                expected to send the character with ASCII code 127. This is
                done for consistency with the Linux console.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"envar">TERMINFO=3D/usr/share/terminfo</code>=
: This
                ensures that the <span class=3D"command"><strong>xterm</str=
ong></span> terminfo files are
                installed to the system terminfo database.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-app-defaults=3D...</co=
de></em>: Sets
                the location for the <code class=3D"filename">app-defaults<=
/code> directory.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring xterm
              </h3>
              <p>
                There are two ways to configure xterm. You can add the X
                resource definitions to the user's <code class=3D"filename"=
>~/.Xresources</code> file, or add them to the
                system-wide <code class=3D"filename">$XORG_PREFIX/share/X11=
/app-defaults/Xterm</code>
                file.
              </p>
              <p>
                In order for xterm to follow the locale settings in the
                environment, use TrueType fonts, and follow the Linux
                convention about the code sent by the Backspace key, add th=
e
                following definitions as the <code class=3D"systemitem">roo=
t</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt;&gt; /etc/=
X11/app-defaults/XTerm &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">*VT100*locale: true
*VT100*faceName: Monospace
*VT100*faceSize: 10
*backarrowKeyIsErase: true
*ptyInitialErase: true</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
