              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
              <p>
                One test named <code class=3D"filename">check-cursor-names<=
/code> is known to fail if
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#adwaita-icon-theme"=
 title=3D"adwaita-icon-theme-46.2">adwaita-icon-theme-46.2</a> is not
                installed.
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If you installed the package on to your system using a
                  <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D"quote">DEST=
DIR</span>=E2=80=9D</span> method, an important file
                  was not installed and must be copied and/or generated.
                  Generate it using the following command as the <code clas=
s=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">gtk-query-immodu=
les-3.0 --update-cache</kbd></pre>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If you installed the package to your system using a
                  <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D"quote">DEST=
DIR</span>=E2=80=9D</span> method, <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/glib=
-2.0/schemas/gschemas.compiled</code>
                  was not updated/created. Create (or update) the file usin=
g
                  the following command as the <code class=3D"systemitem">r=
oot</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">glib-compile-sch=
emas /usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas</kbd></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                broadway_backend=3Dtrue</code></em>: This switch enables th=
e
                HTML5 GTK backend.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D man=3Dtrue</code></em>: Th=
is
                switch allows generating manual pages.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D gtk_doc=3Dtrue</code>: This switc=
h
                enables building documentation. It requires <a class=3D"xre=
f" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK=
-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gtk-doc" title=3D"GTK-Doc-1.34.0">GTK-Doc-1.34.0</=
a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D tracker3=3Dtrue</code>: This swit=
ch
                enables the search function based on Tracker 3 in the GTK+-=
3
                file chooser dialog. It requires <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"=
https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-=
nochunks.html#tracker3" title=3D"Tracker-3.7.3">Tracker-3.7.3</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D cloudproviders=3Dtrue</code>: Use=
 this
                switch if you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
libcloudproviders" title=3D"libcloudproviders-0.3.6">libcloudproviders-0.3.=
6</a>
                installed and wish to enable support for cloud providers in=
 a
                file chooser window.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring GTK+ 3
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"gtk3-config" name=3D"gtk3-config"></a>Conf=
ig
                        Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">~/.config/gtk-3.0/settings.ini</=
code> and
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/gtk-3.0/settings.ini</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470496822608" name=3D"idm14047049682=
2608"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <span class=3D"application">GTK+ 3</span> themes change t=
he
                  way a <span class=3D"application">GTK+ 3</span> applicati=
on
                  looks. An icon theme can be used to change the icons that
                  appear on the application's toolbar. If you have installe=
d
                  a <span class=3D"application">GTK+ 3</span> theme (e.g. t=
he
                  Adwaita theme built in <span class=3D"application">GTK+
                  3</span>), an icon theme (such as <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#oxygen-icons" title=3D"oxygen-icons-6.0.0">oxygen-icons-6=
.0.0</a>) and/or a font
                  (<a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#dejavu-fonts" ti=
tle=3D"DejaVu fonts">Dejavu fonts</a>), you can set your
                  preferences in <code class=3D"filename">~/.config/gtk-3.0=
/settings.ini</code>, or the
                  default system wide configuration file (as the <code clas=
s=3D"systemitem">root</code> user), in <code class=3D"filename">/etc/gtk-3.=
0/settings.ini</code>. For the local
                  user an example is:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -vp ~=
/.config/gtk-3.0
cat &gt; ~/.config/gtk-3.0/settings.ini &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">[Settings]
gtk-theme-name =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>Adwaita</code></em>
gtk-icon-theme-name =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>oxygen</code></em>
gtk-font-name =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>DejaVu Sans 12</code></em=
>
gtk-cursor-theme-size =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>18</code></em>
gtk-toolbar-style =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>GTK_TOOLBAR_BOTH_HORI=
Z</code></em>
gtk-xft-antialias =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>1</code></em>
gtk-xft-hinting =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>1</code></em>
gtk-xft-hintstyle =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>hintslight</code></em=
>
gtk-xft-rgba =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>rgb</code></em>
gtk-cursor-theme-name =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>Adwaita</code></e=
m></code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  There are many settings keys, some with default values. Y=
ou
                  can find them at <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://devel=
oper.gnome.org/gtk3/stable/GtkSettings.html">Settings:
                  GTK+ 3 Reference Manual</a>. There are many more themes
                  available at <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://www.gnome=
-look.org/browse/">https://www.gnome-look.org/browse/</a>
                  and other places.
                </p>
                <p>
                  As part of GTK+-3.0's redesign, the scroll bar buttons ar=
e
                  no longer visible on the scrollbar in many applications. =
If
                  this functionality is desired, modify the <code class=3D"=
filename">gtk.css</code> file and restore them using the
                  following command:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; ~/=
.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">*  {
   -GtkScrollbar-has-backward-stepper: 1;
   -GtkScrollbar-has-forward-stepper: 1;
}</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
