            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of GTK 4
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">GTK 4</span> by running=
 the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup --prefix=3D/usr            \
            --buildtype=3Drelease      \
            -D broadway-backend=3Dtrue \
            -D introspection=3Denabled \
            -D vulkan=3Ddisabled       \
            .. &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gi-docg=
en" title=3D"Gi-DocGen-2024.1">Gi-DocGen-2024.1</a> installed and wish to
                build the API documentation for this package, issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed "s@'doc'@=
&amp; / 'gtk-4.14.5'@" -i ../docs/reference/meson.build &amp;&amp;
meson configure -D documentation=3Dtrue                            &amp;&am=
p;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To run the tests, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong>db=
us-run-session meson test --setup
                x11</strong></span>. If you are in a Wayland session, repla=
ce
                x11 with wayland. Nine tests are known to fail if <a class=
=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/cantarell-fonts">Cantrell
                fonts</a> are not installed. Many tests will fail if
                <code class=3D"filename">~/.config/gtk-4.0/settings.ini</co=
de>
                exists and the gtk-modules line is not commented out. On
                systems with NVIDIA graphics cards, the tests may take
                significantly longer than the above test time.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                broadway-backend=3Dtrue</code></em>: This switch enables th=
e
                HTML5 GDK backend.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                introspection=3Denabled</code></em>: This switch enables us=
ing
                GObject Introspection to generate GIR bindings of this
                packages. These bindings are required by GNOME.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D cloudproviders=3Denabled</code>: =
Use
                this switch if you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://w=
ww.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.=
html#libcloudproviders" title=3D"libcloudproviders-0.3.6">libcloudproviders=
-0.3.6</a>
                installed and wish to enable support for cloud providers in=
 a
                file chooser window.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D tracker=3Denabled</code>: Use thi=
s
                switch if you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
tracker3" title=3D"Tracker-3.7.3">Tracker-3.7.3</a> installed and wish to u=
se
                search functionality when running a file chooser.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D colord=3Denabled</code>: Use this
                switch if you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
colord" title=3D"Colord-1.4.7">colord-1.4.7</a> installed and wish to use
                colord with the CUPS printing backend.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D man-pages=3Dtrue</code>: Use this
                switch if you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
docutils" title=3D"docutils-0.21.2">docutils-0.21.2</a> installed and wish =
to
                generate the man pages.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D sysprof=3Denabled</code>: Use thi=
s
                switch if you have <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://wiki.=
gnome.org/Apps/Sysprof">sysprof</a> installed
                and wish to enable tracing support for GTK4-based
                applications.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D vulkan=3Denabled</code>: Use this
                switch if you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
vulkan-loader" title=3D"Vulkan-Loader-1.3.294">Vulkan-Loader-1.3.294</a>
                installed and wish to build the experimental Vulkan backend=
.
                Note that you must have <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://=
github.com/google/shaderc/blob/main/downloads.md">glslc</a>
                installed if you decide to enable this option.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring GTK 4
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"gtk4-config" name=3D"gtk4-config"></a>Conf=
ig
                        Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">~/.config/gtk-4.0/settings.ini</=
code> and
                  <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/gtk-4.0/settings.ini<=
/code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470496646576" name=3D"idm14047049664=
6576"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <span class=3D"application">GTK 4</span> themes change th=
e
                  way a <span class=3D"application">GTK 4</span> applicatio=
n
                  looks. An icon theme can be used to change the icons that
                  appear on the application's toolbar. If you have installe=
d
                  a <span class=3D"application">GTK 4</span> theme (e.g. th=
e
                  Adwaita theme built in <span class=3D"application">GTK
                  4</span>), an icon theme (such as <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#oxygen-icons" title=3D"oxygen-icons-6.0.0">oxygen-icons-6=
.0.0</a>) and/or a font
                  (<a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.o=
rg/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#dejavu-fonts" ti=
tle=3D"DejaVu fonts">Dejavu fonts</a>), you can set your
                  preferences in <code class=3D"filename">~/.config/gtk-4.0=
/settings.ini</code>, or the
                  default system-wide configuration file (as the <code clas=
s=3D"systemitem">root</code> user), in <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/=
gtk-4.0/settings.ini</code>. For the
                  local user, an example is:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -pv ~=
/.config/gtk-4.0
cat &gt; ~/.config/gtk-4.0/settings.ini &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">[Settings]
gtk-theme-name =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>Adwaita</code></em>
gtk-icon-theme-name =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>oxygen</code></em>
gtk-font-name =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>DejaVu Sans 12</code></em=
>
gtk-cursor-theme-size =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>18</code></em>
gtk-xft-antialias =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>1</code></em>
gtk-xft-hinting =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>1</code></em>
gtk-xft-hintstyle =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>hintslight</code></em=
>
gtk-xft-rgba =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>rgb</code></em>
gtk-cursor-theme-name =3D <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>Adwaita</code></e=
m></code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  There are many settings keys, some with default values. Y=
ou
                  can find them at <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://devel=
oper.gnome.org/gtk4/stable/GtkSettings.html">Settings:
                  GTK 4 Reference Manual</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
