            <div class=3D"qt6-prefix" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Setting the installation prefix
              </h3>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470495025408" name=3D"idm140470495025408"></=
a>Installing in /opt/qt6
              </h4>
              <p>
                The BLFS editors recommend installing <span class=3D"applic=
ation">Qt6</span> in a directory other than
                <code class=3D"filename">/usr</code>, i.e. <code class=3D"f=
ilename">/opt/qt6</code>. This is needed to avoid conflicts
                with Qt5. To do this, set the following environment variabl=
e:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">export QT6PRE=
FIX=3D/opt/qt6</kbd></pre>
              <div class=3D"admon tip">
                <h3>
                  Tip
                </h3>
                <p>
                  Sometimes the installation paths are hardcoded into
                  installed files. This is the reason why <code class=3D"fi=
lename">/opt/qt6</code> is used as installation prefix
                  instead of <code class=3D"filename">/opt/qt-6.7.2</code>.=
 To
                  create a versioned <span class=3D"application">Qt6</span>
                  directory, you may rename the directory and create a
                  symlink:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -pv /opt/q=
t-6.7.2
ln -sfnv qt-6.7.2 /opt/qt6</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Later on, you may want to install other versions of
                  <span class=3D"application">Qt6</span>. To do that, just
                  remove the symlink, create the new versioned directory, a=
nd
                  recreate the <code class=3D"filename">/opt/qt6</code> sym=
link
                  again before building the new version. Which version of
                  <span class=3D"application">Qt6</span> you use depends on=
ly
                  on where the symlink points.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch=
.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#qca" title=3D"=
Qca-2.3.9">qca-2.3.9</a> has been installed and you are
                  reinstalling or updating this package, then <span class=
=3D"application">qca</span> will need to be reinstalled.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Qt6
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"admon warning">
                <h3>
                  Warning
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If <span class=3D"application">Qt6</span> is being
                  reinstalled into the same directory as an existing
                  instance, run the commands done by <code class=3D"systemi=
tem">root</code>, such as <span class=3D"command"><strong>make install</str=
ong></span>, from a
                  console or non-Qt6 based window manager. It overwrites
                  <span class=3D"application">Qt6</span> libraries that sho=
uld
                  not be in use during the install process.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"admon caution">
                <h3>
                  Caution
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If you did not install some of the recommended
                  dependencies, examine <span class=3D"command"><strong>./c=
onfigure --help</strong></span> output
                  to check how to disable them or use internal versions
                  bundled in the source tarball.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  The build time and space required for the full <span clas=
s=3D"application">Qt6</span> is quite long. The instructions
                  below do not build the tutorials and examples. Removing t=
he
                  <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-nomake</code></em> line wi=
ll
                  create additional resources..
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  The BLFS editors do not recommend installing <span class=
=3D"application">Qt6</span> into the /usr hierarchy because it
                  becomes difficult to find components and to update to a n=
ew
                  version. There are also some programs that conflict with
                  those installed by Qt5.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                Disable a conflicting declaration on i686 systems:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">if [ "$(uname=
 -m)" =3D=3D "i686" ]; then
    sed -e "/^#elif defined(Q_CC_GNU_ONLY)/s/.*/&amp; \&amp;\&amp; 0/" \
        -i qtbase/src/corelib/global/qtypes.h
fi</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Qt6</span> by running t=
he
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
prefix $QT6PREFIX      \
            -sysconfdir /etc/xdg    \
            -dbus-linked            \
            -openssl-linked         \
            -system-sqlite          \
            -nomake examples        \
            -no-rpath               \
            -syslog                 \
            -skip qt3d              \
            -skip qtquick3dphysics  \
            -skip qtwebengine       \
            -W no-dev               &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
              <p>
                Remove references to the build directory from installed
                library dependency (prl) files by running the following
                command as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">find $QT6PREFIX/ -=
name \*.prl \
   -exec sed -i -e '/^QMAKE_PRL_BUILD_DIR/d' {} \;</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install images and create the menu entries for installed
                applications. Again as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root<=
/code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">pushd qttools/src =
&amp;&amp;

install -v -Dm644 assistant/assistant/images/assistant-128.png       \
                  /usr/share/pixmaps/assistant-qt6.png               &amp;&=
amp;

install -v -Dm644 designer/src/designer/images/designer.png          \
                  /usr/share/pixmaps/designer-qt6.png                &amp;&=
amp;

install -v -Dm644 linguist/linguist/images/icons/linguist-128-32.png \
                  /usr/share/pixmaps/linguist-qt6.png                &amp;&=
amp;

install -v -Dm644 qdbus/qdbusviewer/images/qdbusviewer-128.png       \
                  /usr/share/pixmaps/qdbusviewer-qt6.png             &amp;&=
amp;
popd &amp;&amp;


cat &gt; /usr/share/applications/assistant-qt6.desktop &lt;&lt; EOF
<code class=3D"literal">[Desktop Entry]
Name=3DQt6 Assistant
Comment=3DShows Qt6 documentation and examples
Exec=3D$QT6PREFIX/bin/assistant
Icon=3Dassistant-qt6.png
Terminal=3Dfalse
Encoding=3DUTF-8
Type=3DApplication
Categories=3DQt;Development;Documentation;</code>
EOF

cat &gt; /usr/share/applications/designer-qt6.desktop &lt;&lt; EOF
<code class=3D"literal">[Desktop Entry]
Name=3DQt6 Designer
GenericName=3DInterface Designer
Comment=3DDesign GUIs for Qt6 applications
Exec=3D$QT6PREFIX/bin/designer
Icon=3Ddesigner-qt6.png
MimeType=3Dapplication/x-designer;
Terminal=3Dfalse
Encoding=3DUTF-8
Type=3DApplication
Categories=3DQt;Development;</code>
EOF

cat &gt; /usr/share/applications/linguist-qt6.desktop &lt;&lt; EOF
<code class=3D"literal">[Desktop Entry]
Name=3DQt6 Linguist
Comment=3DAdd translations to Qt6 applications
Exec=3D$QT6PREFIX/bin/linguist
Icon=3Dlinguist-qt6.png
MimeType=3Dtext/vnd.trolltech.linguist;application/x-linguist;
Terminal=3Dfalse
Encoding=3DUTF-8
Type=3DApplication
Categories=3DQt;Development;</code>
EOF

cat &gt; /usr/share/applications/qdbusviewer-qt6.desktop &lt;&lt; EOF
<code class=3D"literal">[Desktop Entry]
Name=3DQt6 QDbusViewer
GenericName=3DD-Bus Debugger
Comment=3DDebug D-Bus applications
Exec=3D$QT6PREFIX/bin/qdbusviewer
Icon=3Dqdbusviewer-qt6.png
Terminal=3Dfalse
Encoding=3DUTF-8
Type=3DApplication
Categories=3DQt;Development;Debugger;</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-nomake examples</code></em>:
                This switch disables building of the example programs
                included in the source tarball. Remove it if you want to
                build them.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-skip qt3d</code></em>: This
                switch disables building qt3d support. There is a problem
                building these files without an external library and no
                packages in BLFS use qt3d.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-system-sqlite</code></em>: T=
his
                switch enables use of the system version of <span class=3D"=
application">SQLite</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-dbus-linked</code></em>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-openssl-linked</code></em>:
                These switches enable explicit linking of the <span class=
=3D"application">D-Bus</span> and <span class=3D"application">OpenSSL</span=
> libraries into <span class=3D"application">Qt6</span> libraries instead o=
f <span class=3D"command"><strong>dlopen()</strong></span>-ing them.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-syslog</code></em>: This swi=
tch
                allows sending Qt messages to the <span class=3D"command"><=
strong>syslog</strong></span> logging system.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-skip qtwebengine</code></em>=
:
                This switch disables building the QtWebEngine. The BLFS
                editors have chosen to build <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"http=
s://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-noch=
unks.html#qtwebengine" title=3D"QtWebEngine-6.7.2">qtwebengine-6.7.2</a> se=
parately.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-skip
                qtquick3dphysics</code></em>: This switch disables building
                the Qt Quick 3D Physics submodule. On 32-bit systems, this
                will cause the build process to fail with an inlining error
                in Qt6's bundled copy of the PhysX SDK.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Qt6
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"qt6-config" name=3D"qt6-config"></a>Config=
uration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  If <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch=
.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#sudo" title=3D=
"Sudo-1.9.15p5">Sudo-1.9.15p5</a> is installed, QT6DIR
                  should be available to the super user as well. Execute th=
e
                  following commands as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root=
</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/su=
doers.d/qt &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">Defaults env_keep +=3D QT6DIR</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  You now need to update the following configuration files =
so
                  that <span class=3D"application">Qt6</span> is correctly
                  found by other packages and system processes.
                </p>
                <p>
                  As the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user, updat=
e
                  the <code class=3D"filename">/etc/ld.so.conf</code> file =
and
                  the dynamic linker's run-time cache file:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt;&gt; /et=
c/ld.so.conf &lt;&lt; EOF
<code class=3D"literal"># Begin Qt addition

/opt/qt6/lib

# End Qt addition</code>
EOF

ldconfig</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  As the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user, creat=
e
                  the <code class=3D"filename">/etc/profile.d/qt6.sh</code>
                  file:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/pr=
ofile.d/qt6.sh &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal"># Begin /etc/profile.d/qt6.sh

QT6DIR=3D/opt/qt6

pathappend $QT6DIR/bin           PATH
pathappend $QT6DIR/lib/pkgconfig PKG_CONFIG_PATH

export QT6DIR

# End /etc/profile.d/qt6.sh</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
