                  such as <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromsc=
ratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#balsa" ti=
tle=3D"Balsa-2.6.4">Balsa-2.6.4</a> or <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.h=
tml#evolution" title=3D"Evolution-3.52.4">Evolution-3.52.4</a>,
                  require the GTK-3 version. Both versions can be installed
                  side by side on the same system. We give build instructio=
ns
                  for both cases below, but the only difference is the
                  setting of <span class=3D"command"><strong>-D
                  USE_GTK4</strong></span>
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                First, fix a regression that occurs with some websites that
                use WebAssembly:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed '/returnL=
ocation.isStackArgument/,/returnLocation =3D canonicalLocation/d'\
    -i Source/JavaScriptCore/wasm/WasmBBQJIT.cpp</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you want to install the GTK+-3 version of <span class=3D=
"application">WebKitGTK</span>, run the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -vp bui=
ld &amp;&amp;
cd        build &amp;&amp;

cmake -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease     \
      -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=3D/usr    \
      -D CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RPATH=3DON  \
      -D PORT=3DGTK                     \
      -D LIB_INSTALL_DIR=3D/usr/lib     \
      -D USE_LIBBACKTRACE=3DOFF         \
      -D USE_LIBHYPHEN=3DOFF            \
      -D ENABLE_GAMEPAD=3DOFF           \
      -D ENABLE_MINIBROWSER=3DON        \
      -D ENABLE_DOCUMENTATION=3DOFF     \
      -D ENABLE_WEBDRIVER=3DOFF         \
      -D USE_WOFF2=3DOFF                \
      -D USE_GTK4=3DOFF                 \
      -D ENABLE_JOURNALD_LOG=3DOFF      \
      -D ENABLE_BUBBLEWRAP_SANDBOX=3DON \
      -W no-dev -G Ninja ..           &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not have a working test suite. However,
                there is a usable basic graphical web browser in the build
                directory, <span class=3D"application">build/bin/MiniBrowse=
r</span>. If launching it
                fails, there is a problem with the build.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
              <p>
                If you want to install the GTK4 version of <span class=3D"a=
pplication">WebKitGTK</span>, run the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">rm -rf * .[^.=
]* &amp;&amp;

cmake -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease     \
      -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=3D/usr    \
      -D CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RPATH=3DON  \
      -D PORT=3DGTK                     \
      -D LIB_INSTALL_DIR=3D/usr/lib     \
      -D USE_LIBBACKTRACE=3DOFF         \
      -D USE_LIBHYPHEN=3DOFF            \
      -D ENABLE_GAMEPAD=3DOFF           \
      -D ENABLE_MINIBROWSER=3DON        \
      -D ENABLE_DOCUMENTATION=3DOFF     \
      -D USE_WOFF2=3DOFF                \
      -D USE_GTK4=3DON                  \
      -D ENABLE_JOURNALD_LOG=3DOFF      \
      -D ENABLE_BUBBLEWRAP_SANDBOX=3DON \
      -W no-dev -G Ninja ..           &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
              <p>
                As the <code class=3D"option">-D
                ENABLE_DOCUMENTATION=3DOFF</code> option is used, the
                documentation is not rebuilt nor installed now. If you need
                the documentation, you can either install <a class=3D"xref"=
 href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-1=
2.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gi-docgen" title=3D"Gi-DocGen-2024.1">Gi-DocGen-2024=
.1</a> and remove this
                option from the <span class=3D"command"><strong>cmake</stro=
ng></span> command, or install
                the pre-built documentation (only for the GTK-4 version)
                instead:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -vdm755 /u=
sr/share/gtk-doc/html &amp;&amp;
cp -rv ../Documentation/* /usr/share/gtk-doc/html</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RPATH=3DON</code></em>: This switch make=
s
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>cmake</strong></span> remov=
e
                hardcoded library search paths (rpath) when installing a
                binary executable file or a shared library. This package do=
es
                not need rpath once it's installed into the standard
                location, and rpath may sometimes cause unwanted effects or
                even security issues.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                USE_LIBBACKTRACE=3DOFF</code></em>: This switch disables th=
e
                use of libbacktrace for dumping a stack trace when a crash
                happens. You need to install <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"htt=
ps://github.com/ianlancetaylor/libbacktrace">libbacktrace</a>
                if you wish to enable it (replacing OFF with ON or just
                removing the switch).
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D USE_LIBHYPHEN=3DOFF</code>=
</em>:
                This switch disables the default automatic hyphenation
                implementation. You need to install <a class=3D"ulink" href=
=3D"https://sourceforge.net/projects/hunspell/files/Hyphen/">Hyphen</a>
                if you wish to enable it (replacing OFF with ON or just
                removing the switch).
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                ENABLE_DOCUMENTATION=3DOFF</code></em>: This switch disable=
s
                regenerating the documentation. Remove this switch if you
                have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch=
.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gi-docgen" tit=
le=3D"Gi-DocGen-2024.1">Gi-DocGen-2024.1</a> installed and wish to
                regenerate the documentation.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                ENABLE_GAMEPAD=3DOFF</code></em>: This switch disables game=
pad
                support. Remove this switch if you have <a class=3D"ulink" =
href=3D"https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/libmanette/">libmanette</a>
                installed and wish to enable it.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                ENABLE_MINIBROWSER=3DON</code></em>: This switch enables
                compiling and installing the MiniBrowser.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                ENABLE_WEBDRIVER=3DOFF</code></em>: This switch disables
                compiling and installing <span class=3D"command"><strong>We=
bKitWebDriver</strong></span>. We use it
                for the GTK-3 build because the <span class=3D"command"><st=
rong>WebKitWebDriver</strong></span> from the
                GTK-3 build will be overwritten by the GTK-4 build anyway.
                Remove this option if you don't plan to build this package
                with GTK-4.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                ENABLE_BUBBLEWRAP_SANDBOX=3DON</code></em>: This switch ena=
bles
                the Bubblewrap sandbox, which helps mitigate the impact of
                most security vulnerabilities in this package. Change this
                switch to OFF if you do not want to install <a class=3D"xre=
f" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK=
-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#bubblewrap" title=3D"Bubblewrap-0.9.0">bubblewrap-=
0.9.0</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/=
downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libseccomp" title=3D"lib=
seccomp-2.5.5">libseccomp-2.5.5</a>, or <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://w=
ww.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.=
html#xdg-dbus-proxy" title=3D"xdg-dbus-proxy-0.1.5">xdg-dbus-proxy-0.1.5</a=
>, but note
                that this may put you at risk.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                ENABLE_JOURNALD_LOG=3DOFF</code></em>: This switch disables
                using the systemd journal for logging errors and debugging
                information since it is not available on SysV systems.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D USE_SYSTEM_MALLOC=3DON</code>: Th=
is
                switch enables building against the system installed
                <span class=3D"application">malloc</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D ENABLE_GEOLOCATION=3DOFF</code>: =
Use
                this switch if you don't want to install <a class=3D"xref" =
href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12=
.2-sysv-nochunks.html#geoclue2" title=3D"GeoClue-2.7.1">GeoClue-2.7.1</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D USE_AVIF=3DOFF</code>: Use this s=
witch
                if you don't want to install <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"http=
s://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-noch=
unks.html#libavif" title=3D"libavif-1.1.1">libavif-1.1.1</a>. Note that you=
 will
                not have support for AVIF images if you do this.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D USE_WOFF2=3DON</code>: Use this s=
witch
                if the optional package <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://w=
ww.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.=
html#woff2" title=3D"woff2-1.0.2">WOFF2-1.0.2</a> is installed. This adds
                additional support for fonts.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D USE_JPEGXL=3DOFF</code>: Use this
                switch if the recommended package <a class=3D"xref" href=3D=
"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv=
-nochunks.html#libjxl" title=3D"libjxl-0.10.3">libjxl-0.10.3</a> is not
                installed. Note that you will not have support for JPEG XL
                images if this option is passed.
              </p>
            </div>
