            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of GDM
              </h3>
              <p>
                It is recommended to have a dedicated user and group to tak=
e
                control of the <span class=3D"command"><strong>gdm</strong>=
</span> daemon after it is
                started. Issue the following commands as the <code class=3D=
"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -g 21 gdm=
 &amp;&amp;
useradd -c "GDM Daemon Owner" -d /var/lib/gdm -u 21 \
        -g gdm -s /bin/false gdm &amp;&amp;
passwd -ql gdm</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">GDM</span> by running t=
he
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -e 's@sys=
temd@elogind@'                                \
    -e '/elogind/isession  required       pam_loginuid.so' \
    -i data/pam-lfs/gdm-launch-environment.pam &amp;&amp;

mkdir build &amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup ..                   \
      --prefix=3D/usr              \
      --buildtype=3Drelease        \
      -D gdm-xsession=3Dtrue       \
      -D run-dir=3D/run/gdm        \
      -D logind-provider=3Delogind \
      -D systemd-journal=3Dfalse   \
      -D systemdsystemunitdir=3Dno \
      -D systemduserunitdir=3Dno   &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a usable test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
