            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Fluxbox
              </h3>
              <p>
                First, fix a build failure when building with gcc-11.1:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -i '/text=
_prop.value &gt; 0/s/&gt;/!=3D/' util/fluxbox-remote.cc</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Fluxbox</span> by runni=
ng
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not have a working test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Fluxbox
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"fluxbox-config" name=3D"fluxbox-config"></=
a>Config Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">~/.fluxbox/init</code>, <code cl=
ass=3D"filename">~/.fluxbox/keys</code>, and <code class=3D"filename">~/.fl=
uxbox/menu</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470493933328" name=3D"idm14047049393=
3328"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  If <span class=3D"application">Fluxbox</span> is the only
                  Window Manager you want to use, you can start it with an
                  <code class=3D"filename">.xinitrc</code> file in your hom=
e
                  folder. Be sure to backup your current <code class=3D"fil=
ename">.xinitrc</code> before proceeding.
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">echo startf=
luxbox &gt; ~/.xinitrc</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Or alternatively, if you use a login manager like <a clas=
s=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/B=
LFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gdm" title=3D"GDM-46.2">GDM-46.2</a> or
                  <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.or=
g/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#lightdm" title=3D=
"lightdm-1.32.0">lightdm-1.32.0</a>, and would like to be
                  able to choose <span class=3D"application">Fluxbox</span>=
 at
                  the login prompt, create a <code class=3D"filename">fluxb=
ox.desktop</code> file. As <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code>:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -pv /usr/s=
hare/xsessions &amp;&amp;
cat &gt; /usr/share/xsessions/fluxbox.desktop &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">[Desktop Entry]
Encoding=3DUTF-8
Name=3DFluxbox
Comment=3DThis session logs you into Fluxbox
Exec=3Dstartfluxbox
Type=3DApplication</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  If you didn't install <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://w=
ww.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.=
html#gdm" title=3D"GDM-46.2">GDM-46.2</a> or <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"http=
s://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-noch=
unks.html#lightdm" title=3D"lightdm-1.32.0">lightdm-1.32.0</a> in <code cla=
ss=3D"filename">/usr</code>, then change that command to fit the
                  prefix you chose.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Now create the <span class=3D"application">Fluxbox</span>
                  configuration files:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir -v ~/=
.fluxbox &amp;&amp;
cp -v /usr/share/fluxbox/init ~/.fluxbox/init &amp;&amp;
cp -v /usr/share/fluxbox/keys ~/.fluxbox/keys</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  To generate the application menu, first you may wish to r=
un
                  <span class=3D"command"><strong>fluxbox-generate_menu
                  -h</strong></span>, in order to choose any <em class=3D"r=
eplaceable"><code>&lt;user_options&gt;</code></em>, then
                  issue:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cd ~/.fluxb=
ox &amp;&amp;
fluxbox-generate_menu <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;user_options&gt;<=
/code></em></kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Alternately, copy a pregenerated menu:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cp -v /usr/=
share/fluxbox/menu ~/.fluxbox/menu</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Menu items are added by editing <code class=3D"filename">=
~/.fluxbox/menu</code>. The syntax is explained
                  on the <span class=3D"command"><strong>fluxbox</strong></=
span> man page.
                </p>
                <p>
                  If you want to use an image as your desktop background,
                  copy the theme you like into <code class=3D"filename">~/.=
fluxbox</code>. Then add a line to make it
                  use the correct image. In the following command, change
                  <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;theme&gt;</code></em>=
 for
                  the name of the theme you want and change <em class=3D"re=
placeable"><code>&lt;/path/to/nice/image.ext&gt;</code></em>
                  to point to the actual image you want to use, where
                  <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>ext</code></em> must be
                  <code class=3D"literal">xpm</code>, if <a class=3D"xref" =
href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12=
.2-sysv-nochunks.html#imlib2" title=3D"imlib2-1.12.3">imlib2-1.12.3</a> is =
not
                  installed to allow other image formats.
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cp -r /usr/=
share/fluxbox/styles/&lt;theme&gt; ~/.fluxbox/theme &amp;&amp;

sed -i 's,\(session.styleFile:\).*,\1 ~/.fluxbox/theme,' ~/.fluxbox/init &a=
mp;&amp;

[ -f ~/.fluxbox/theme ] &amp;&amp;
echo "background.pixmap: &lt;/path/to/nice/image.ext&gt;" &gt;&gt; ~/.fluxb=
ox/theme ||
[ -d ~/.fluxbox/theme ] &amp;&amp;
echo "background.pixmap: &lt;/path/to/nice/image.ext&gt;" &gt;&gt; ~/.fluxb=
ox/theme/theme.cfg</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  In some locales the font specified in the theme may not
                  contain the needed characters. This results in menus with
                  blank items. You can fix this by editing <code class=3D"f=
ilename">~/.fluxbox/theme</code> with a text editor and
                  altering it so that it names a suitable font.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
