3.&nbsp;GNOME Libraries and
                Desktop
              </h2>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"chapter" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
          <p>
            The objective of this section is to build a <span class=3D"appl=
ication">GNOME</span> desktop.
          </p>
          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"idm140470491955664" name=3D"idm140470491955664">=
</a>Libraries
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"dummy" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en"></div>
          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"gcr" name=3D"gcr"></a>Gcr-3.41.2
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to Gcr
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">Gcr</span> package contains
                libraries used for displaying certificates and accessing ke=
y
                stores. It also provides the viewer for crypto files on the
                <span class=3D"application">GNOME</span> Desktop.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470491947760" name=3D"idm140470491947760"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://d=
ownload.gnome.org/sources/gcr/3.41/gcr-3.41.2.tar.xz">
                      https://download.gnome.org/sources/gcr/3.41/gcr-3.41.=
2.tar.xz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 40a754ba44d5e95e4d07656d6302900c
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 1012 KB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 33 MB (with tests)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 0.2 SBU (with tests; both using
                      parallelism=3D4)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470491940304" name=3D"idm140470491940304"></=
a>Gcr
                Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470491939616" name=3D"idm140470491939616"></=
a>Required
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#glib2" title=3D"GLi=
b-2.80.4">GLib-2.80.4</a> (GObject Introspection
                recommended), <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfr=
omscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libgc=
rypt" title=3D"libgcrypt-1.11.0">libgcrypt-1.11.0</a>, and <a class=3D"xref=
" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-=
12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#p11-kit" title=3D"p11-kit-0.25.5">p11-kit-0.25.5</a=
>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470491936256" name=3D"idm140470491936256"></=
a>Recommended
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gnupg2" title=3D"Gn=
uPG-2.4.5">GnuPG-2.4.5</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gtk3" t=
itle=3D"GTK+-3.24.43">GTK+-3.24.43</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://w=
ww.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.=
html#libsecret" title=3D"libsecret-0.21.4">libsecret-0.21.4</a>,
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libxslt" title=3D"l=
ibxslt-1.1.42">libxslt-1.1.42</a>, and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.h=
tml#vala" title=3D"Vala-0.56.17">Vala-0.56.17</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470491931584" name=3D"idm140470491931584"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gi-docgen" title=3D=
"Gi-DocGen-2024.1">Gi-DocGen-2024.1</a> and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https=
://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochu=
nks.html#valgrind" title=3D"Valgrind-3.23.0">Valgrind-3.23.0</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Gcr
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Gcr</span> by running t=
he
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -i 's:"/d=
esktop:"/org:' schema/*.xml &amp;&amp;

mkdir build &amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup --prefix=3D/usr       \
            --buildtype=3Drelease \
            -D gtk_doc=3Dfalse    \
            -D ssh_agent=3Dfalse  \
            ..                  &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gi-docg=
en" title=3D"Gi-DocGen-2024.1">Gi-DocGen-2024.1</a> installed and wish to
                build the API documentation for this package, issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -e "/inst=
all_dir/s@,\$@ / 'gcr-3.41.2'&amp;@" \
    -i ../docs/*/meson.build                  &amp;&amp;
meson configure -D gtk_doc=3Dtrue               &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>ninja test</strong></span>. The tests must
                be run from an X Terminal or similar.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D ssh_agent=3Dfalse</code></=
em>:
                Prevent a conflict with <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://w=
ww.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.=
