e.org/Apps/Sysprof">sysprof</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Mutter
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Mutter</span> by runnin=
g
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup --prefix=3D/usr       \
            --buildtype=3Drelease \
            -D tests=3Dfalse      \
            -D profiler=3Dfalse   \
            ..                  &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                The test suite requires an external program called
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>xvfb-run</strong></span>. I=
f
                you wish to run the tests, you should download and install =
it
                before running <span class=3D"command"><strong>meson</stron=
g></span>. You can obtain it
                from <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://anduin.linuxfromscr=
atch.org/BLFS/mutter/xvfb-run">xvfb-run</a>,
                and install it with executable permissions in <code class=
=3D"filename">/usr/bin</code>. <span class=3D"command"><strong>xvfb-run</st=
rong></span> needs <span class=3D"command"><strong>Xvfb</strong></span> at =
runtime, and
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>Xvfb</strong></span> can be
                installed from either <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www=
.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.ht=
ml#xorg-server" title=3D"Xorg-Server-21.1.13">Xorg-Server-21.1.13</a> or
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#xwayland" title=3D"=
Xwayland-24.1.2">Xwayland-24.1.2</a>. You should also
                replace <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                tests=3Dfalse</code></em> in the <span class=3D"command"><s=
trong>meson</strong></span> command, with
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D tests=3Dtrue -D
                clutter_tests=3Dfalse</code></em>. The test suite requires =
the
                mutter schema to be installed on the system, so it is bette=
r
                to run the tests after installing the package.
              </p>
              <p>
                You can also test basic functions of <span class=3D"applica=
tion">Mutter</span> following <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfr=
omscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#mutte=
r-starting" title=3D"Starting Mutter">the section called
                =E2=80=9CStarting Mutter=E2=80=9D</a>, after installing it.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
              <p>
                If you wish to run the tests, remove the reference to
                <span class=3D"application">Zenity</span> which is not a pa=
rt
                of BLFS from one test:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"test"><kbd class=3D"command">sed 's/zenity --[a=
-z]*/gtk4-demo/' -i ../src/tests/x11-test.sh</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Now run the test suite:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"test"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja test</kbd></=
pre>
              <p>
                The tests require an active X or wayland session. Some test=
s
                are flaky (especially under a high system load) so if a tes=
t
                fails you can try to re-run it alone with the <span class=
=3D"command"><strong>meson test <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>&lt;test
                name&gt;</code></em></strong></span> command. A few tests m=
ay
                fail depending on some system configuration. Don't make any
                mouse or keyboard input while the test suite is running or
                some tests may fail.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D tests=3Dfalse</code></em>:
                Prevents building the tests, and removes a hard requirement
                on <span class=3D"command"><strong>xvfb-run</strong></span>=
.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D profiler=3Dfalse</code></e=
m>:
                Allows building this package without <span class=3D"applica=
tion">Sysprof</span>. Remove this option if you've
                installed <span class=3D"application">Sysprof</span> and wa=
nt
                to analyze the rendering performance of <span class=3D"appl=
ication">Mutter</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D tests=3Dtrue -D
                clutter_tests=3Dfalse</code>: This builds all of the tests
                except for the tests for the shipped <span class=3D"applica=
tion">Clutter</span> library. The <span class=3D"application">Clutter</span=
> tests are known to fail with
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"starting" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"mutter-starting" name=3D"mutter-starting"></a>Star=
ting
                Mutter
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"application">Mutter</span> is normally used =
as a
                component of <span class=3D"application">gnome-shell</span>=
,
                but it can be used as a standalone Wayland compositor too. =
To
                run <span class=3D"application">Mutter</span> as a Wayland
                compositor, in a virtual console, issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mutter --wayl=
and -- vte-2.91</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Replace <span class=3D"command"><strong>vte-2.91</strong></=
span> with the command
                line for the first application you want in the Wayland
                session. Note that once this application exits, the Wayland
                session will be terminated.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"application">Mutter</span> can also function=
 as
                a nested compositor in another Wayland session. In a termin=
al
                emulator, issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">MUTTER_DEBUG_=
DUMMY_MODE_SPECS=3D1920x1080 mutter --wayland --nested -- vte-2.91</kbd></p=
re>
              <p>
                Replace <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>1920x1080</code></e=
m>
                with the size you want for the nested Wayland session.
              </p>
            </div>
