            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Evince
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Evince</span> by runnin=
g
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

CPPFLAGS+=3D" -I/opt/texlive/2024/include" \
meson setup --prefix=3D/usr                \
            --buildtype=3Drelease          \
            -D gtk_doc=3Dfalse             \
            --wrap-mode=3Dnodownload       \
            -D systemduserunitdir=3Dno ..  &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gi-docg=
en" title=3D"Gi-DocGen-2024.1">Gi-DocGen-2024.1</a> installed and wish to
                build the API documentation for this package, issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed "/docs_di=
r/s@\$@ / 'evince-46.3.1'@" -i ../help/meson.build &amp;&amp;
meson configure -D gtk_doc=3Dtrue                                 &amp;&amp=
;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not have a working test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If you installed the package to your system using a
                  <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D"quote">DEST=
DIR</span>=E2=80=9D</span> method, <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/glib=
-2.0/schemas/gschemas.compiled</code>
                  was not updated/created. Create (or update) the file usin=
g
                  the following command as the <code class=3D"systemitem">r=
oot</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">glib-compile-sch=
emas /usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas</kbd></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>CPPFLAGS+=3D"
                -I/opt/texlive/2024/include"</code></em>: Make sure that
                meson can find libkpathsea headers from TeXLive if it is
                installed. This has no effect on systems without TeXLive
                installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--wrap-mode=3Dnodownload</cod=
e></em>: This
                switch disables fetching any dependency: the build system
                tries to fetch gi-docgen even if <em class=3D"parameter"><c=
ode>-D gtk_doc=3Dfalse</code></em> is passed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D gtk_doc=3Dfalse</code></em=
>:
                Allow building this package without <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#gi-docgen" title=3D"Gi-DocGen-2024.1">Gi-DocGen-2024.1</a=
>
                installed. If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.h=
tml#gi-docgen" title=3D"Gi-DocGen-2024.1">Gi-DocGen-2024.1</a> installed an=
d
                you wish to rebuild and install the API documentation, a
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>meson configure</strong></s=
pan>
                command will reset this option.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D gspell=3Dfalse</code>: This switc=
h
                turns off support for the spell checking plugin.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D introspection=3Dfalse</code>: Use=
 this
                option if you don't have built <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"ht=
tps://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-no=
chunks.html#glib2" title=3D"GLib-2.80.4">GLib-2.80.4</a> with GObject
                Introspection and don't wish to have introspection support
                built into Evince.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D nautilus=3Dfalse</code>: This swi=
tch
                disables building the <span class=3D"application">Nautilus<=
/span> Plugin. Use this switch if
                <span class=3D"application">Nautilus</span> is not installe=
d.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D keyring=3Dfalse</code>: This swit=
ch
                disables the use of <span class=3D"application">libsecret</=
span>. Use this switch if
                <span class=3D"application">libsecret</span> is not install=
ed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D ps=3Denabled</code>: Use this swi=
tch if
                <span class=3D"application">libspectre</span> is installed =
and
                you want to view PostScript files with <span class=3D"appli=
cation">Evince</span>.
              </p>
            </div>
