/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#polkit-gnome" titl=
e=3D"polkit-gnome-0.105">polkit-gnome-0.105</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470487451264" name=3D"idm140470487451264"></=
a>Required Runtime
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#xfdesktop" title=3D=
"Xfdesktop-4.18.1">Xfdesktop-4.18.1</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Xfce4 Session
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Xfce4 Session</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr \
            --sysconfdir=3D/etc \
            --disable-legacy-sm &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-legacy-sm</code></e=
m>:
                This switch disables legacy session management which isn't
                necessary on modern system.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Xfce4 Session
              </h3>
              <p>
                There are several optional run time dependencies for
                <span class=3D"application">Xfce4</span>: <a class=3D"xref"=
 href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-1=
2.2-sysv-nochunks.html#dbus" title=3D"dbus-1.14.10">dbus-1.14.10</a>, <a cl=
ass=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable=
/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gnupg2" title=3D"GnuPG-2.4.5">GnuPG-2.4.=
5</a>,
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#hicolor-icon-theme"=
 title=3D"hicolor-icon-theme-0.18">hicolor-icon-theme-0.18</a>,
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#openssh" title=3D"O=
penSSH-9.8p1">OpenSSH-9.8p1</a>, and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.=
linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.htm=
l#xinit" title=3D"xinit-1.4.2">xinit-1.4.2</a>
              </p>
              <p>
                When building an <span class=3D"application">Xfce4</span>
                package, some configuration files are installed in
                <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/applications</code>,
                <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/icons</code>, and
                <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/mime</code>. In order t=
o
                use those files in your <span class=3D"application">Xfce4</=
span> session, you need to update
                various databases. Do that by running, as the <code class=
=3D"systemitem">root</code> user (you need to have the
                recommended dependencies installed):
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">update-desktop-dat=
abase &amp;&amp;
update-mime-database /usr/share/mime</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"starting" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Starting Xfce4
              </h3>
              <p>
                You can start <span class=3D"application">Xfce4</span> from
                runlevel 3, using <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.lin=
uxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#x=
init" title=3D"xinit-1.4.2">xinit-1.4.2</a>, or from runlevel 5, using a
                Display Manager, such as <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://=
www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks=
.html#lightdm" title=3D"lightdm-1.32.0">lightdm-1.32.0</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                To start <span class=3D"application">Xfce4</span> using
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#xinit" title=3D"xin=
it-1.4.2">xinit-1.4.2</a>, run the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; ~/.x=
initrc &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">dbus-launch --exit-with-x11 startxfce4</code>
EOF

startx</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                The X session starts on the first unused virtual terminal,
                normally vt7. You can switch to another vt<span class=3D"em=
phasis"><em>n</em></span> simultaneously pressing the keys
                Ctrl-Alt-F<span class=3D"emphasis"><em>n</em></span>
                (<span class=3D"emphasis"><em>n</em></span>=3D1, 2, ...). T=
o
                switch back to the X session, normally started at vt7, use
                Ctrl-Alt-F7. The vt where the command <span class=3D"comman=
d"><strong>startx</strong></span> was executed will
                display many messages, including X starting messages,
                applications automatically started with the session, and
                eventually, some warning and error messages. You may prefer
                to redirect those messages to a log file, which not only wi=
ll
                keep the initial vt uncluttered, but can also be used for
                debugging purposes. This can be done starting X with:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">startx &amp;&=
gt; ~/.x-session-errors</kbd></pre>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  You may wish to drop dbus-launch, e.g., just using
                  startxfce4 in ~/.xinitrc. However some capabilities such =
as
                  mounting or umounting file systems from a file manager wi=
ll
                  not be possible, or the reboot option will be absent or
                  inoperative, among other problems.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                When shutting down or rebooting, the shutdown messages appe=
ar
                on the vt where X was running. If you wish to see those
                messages, simultaneously press keys Alt-F7 (assuming that X
                was running on vt7).
              </p>
            </div>
