            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of FreeRDP
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">FreeRDP</span> by runni=
ng
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

cmake -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=3D/usr   \
      -D CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RPATH=3DON \
      -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease    \
      -D WITH_CAIRO=3DON               \
      -D WITH_CLIENT_SDL=3DOFF         \
      -D WITH_DSP_FFMPEG=3DON          \
      -D WITH_FFMPEG=3DON              \
      -D WITH_PCSC=3DOFF               \
      -D WITH_SERVER=3DON              \
      -D WITH_SERVER_CHANNELS=3DON     \
      -D DOCBOOKXSL_DIR=3D/usr/share/xml/docbook/xsl-stylesheets-nons-1.79.=
2 \
      -W no-dev                      \
      -G Ninja ..                    &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RPATH=3DON</code></em>: This switch make=
s
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>cmake</strong></span> remov=
e
                hardcoded library search paths (rpath) when installing a
                binary executable file or a shared library. This package do=
es
                not need rpath once it's installed into the standard
                location, and rpath may sometimes cause unwanted effects or
                even security issues.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                DOCBOOKXSL_DIR=3D/usr/share/xml/docbook/xsl-stylesheets-non=
s-1.79.2</code></em>:
                This parameter points CMake to the location of the Docbook
                XSL stylesheets, and is needed because BLFS does not use
                namespaced versions of the stylesheets. This is needed to
                create man pages. If you do not want manpages, pass -D
                WITH_MANPAGES=3DOFF to CMake instead.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D WITH_CAIRO=3DON</code></em=
>:
                This parameter uses Cairo for HighDPI and window resizing
                support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                WITH_CLIENT_SDL=3DOFF</code></em>: This parameter disables
                using SDL to draw the window when using the FreeRDP client.
                This is disabled because it depends on <a class=3D"ulink" h=
ref=3D"https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL_ttf">SDL_ttf</a>. Remove
                this switch if you have the SDL_ttf package installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D WITH_FFMPEG=3DON</code></e=
m>:
                This parameter enables support for using ffmpeg for the H.2=
64
                graphics rendering mode, which is required when connecting
                via RDP to Windows Server 2012 (or Windows 8) or later host=
s.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                WITH_DSP_FFMPEG=3DON</code></em>: This parameter enables
                support for using ffmpeg for sound and microphone
                redirection.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D WITH_PCSC=3DOFF</code></em=
>:
                This parameter disables support for SmartCards since BLFS
                does not have the required dependency for it.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D WITH_SERVER=3DON</code></e=
m>:
                This parameter enables building the FreeRDP server
                components. Remove this parameter if you do not want to use
                the FreeRDP server.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                WITH_SERVER_CHANNELS=3DON</code></em>: This parameter build=
s
                additional plugins for the FreeRDP server.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D WITH_LAME=3DON</code>: Use this o=
ption
                if you wish to enable support for using LAME to provide MP3
                Audio Codec support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D WITH_FAAC=3DON</code>: Use this o=
ption
                if you wish to enable support for using FAAC to provide AAC
                Audio Codec support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D WITH_FAAD2=3DON</code>: Use this =
option
                if you wish to enable support for using FAAD2 to provide AA=
C
                Audio Codec support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D WITH_FDK_AAC=3DON</code>: Use thi=
s
                option if you wish to enable support for using fdk-aac to
                provide AAC Audio Codec support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D WITH_MBEDTLS=3DON</code>: Use thi=
s
                option if you have the optional dependency <a class=3D"ulin=
k" href=3D"https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls">mbedTLS</a>
                installed and wish to use it as an alternative to OpenSSL f=
or
                cryptography support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D WITH_OPENCL=3DON</code>: Use this
                option if you have the optional dependency <a class=3D"ulin=
k" href=3D"https://github.com/OCL-dev/ocl-icd">ocl-icd</a>
                installed and wish to use OpenCL support.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D WITH_OPENH264=3DON</code>: Use th=
is
                option if you have the optional dependency <a class=3D"ulin=
k" href=3D"https://www.openh264.org/">openh264</a> installed and
                wish to use it for H.264 support instead of ffmpeg.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D WITH_GSM=3DON</code>: Use this op=
tion
                if you have the optional dependency <a class=3D"ulink" href=
=3D"https://www.quut.com/gsm/">GSM</a> installed and wish to use
                GSM as an audio codec.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D WITH_SOXR=3DON</code>: Use this o=
ption
                if you have the optional dependency <a class=3D"ulink" href=
=3D"https://github.com/chirlu/soxr">soxr</a> installed and wish
                to use it instead of ffmpeg for multimedia redirection.
              </p>
            </div>
