              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470483986768" name=3D"idm140470483986768"></=
a>Gparted Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470483986080" name=3D"idm140470483986080"></=
a>Required
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gtkmm3" title=3D"Gt=
kmm-3.24.9">Gtkmm-3.24.9</a> and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linu=
xfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#pa=
rted" title=3D"parted-3.6">parted-3.6</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470483983008" name=3D"idm140470483983008"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#btrfs-progs" title=
=3D"btrfs-progs-6.10.1">btrfs-progs-6.10.1</a> (if using a btrfs
                filesystem), <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://github.com/=
exfatprogs/exfatprogs">exfatprogs</a>,
                and <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://github.com/pali/udft=
ools">udftools</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Gparted
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Gparted</span> by runni=
ng
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr    \
            --disable-doc    \
            --disable-static &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To run the tests, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong>ma=
ke
                check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-static</code></em>:
                This switch prevents installation of static versions of the
                libraries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-doc</code></em>: Th=
is
                switch disables building of the optional documentation.
                Remove it if you have installed <span class=3D"application"=
>GNOME Doc Utils</span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-xhost-root</code>: This swi=
tch
                provides an interim workaround to allow GParted to run unde=
r
                Wayland by using xhost to grant and revoke root access to t=
he
                X11 display.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"using" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Using Gparted
              </h3>
              <p>
                To manipulate file systems Gparted has a run time dependenc=
y
                on various file system tools (you only need to install the
                tools for file systems you actually use): <a class=3D"xref"=
 href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-1=
2.2-sysv-nochunks.html#hdparm" title=3D"Hdparm-9.65">Hdparm-9.65</a> (requi=
red
                for optionally displaying serial number device information)=
,
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#btrfs-progs" title=
=3D"btrfs-progs-6.10.1">btrfs-progs-6.10.1</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"h=
ttps://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-n=
ochunks.html#dosfstools" title=3D"dosfstools-4.2">dosfstools-4.2</a>,
                e2fsprogs (installed as part of LFS), <a class=3D"xref" hre=
f=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-=
sysv-nochunks.html#jfsutils" title=3D"jfsutils-1.1.15">jfsutils-1.1.15</a>,
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#xfsprogs" title=3D"=
xfsprogs-6.9.0">xfsprogs-6.9.0</a>, <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://ftp.=
gnu.org/pub/gnu/mtools/">mtools</a> (required to
                read and write FAT16/32 volume labels and UUIDs), <a class=
=3D"ulink" href=3D"ftp://ftp.mars.org/pub/hfs/">hfsutils</a>,
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://packages.debian.org/sid/=
hfsprogs">hfsprogs</a>,
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://nilfs.sourceforge.io/en/=
">nilfs-utils</a>, <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://reiser4.wiki.kernel.o=
rg/index.php/Reiser4progs">Reiser4progs</a>,
                and <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://mirrors.edge.kernel.=
org/pub/linux/kernel/people/jeffm/reiserfsprogs/">
                reiserfsprogs</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Root privileges are required to run Gparted. If you wish to
                run the application from the menu, further applications and
                configurations are necessary. Examples of applications that
                may be used: <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://people.debi=
an.org/~kov/gksu/">gksu</a>, <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://launchpad.n=
et/kdesudo">kdesudo</a>, or
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://github.com/tarakbumba/xd=
g-su">xdg-su</a>. Another
                simple solution is <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
ssh-askpass" title=3D"ssh-askpass-9.8p1">ssh-askpass-9.8p1</a>.
              </p>
              <div class=3D"ssh-askpass" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470483951136" name=3D"idm14047048395=
1136"></a>ssh-askpass
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  To optionally use <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.l=
inuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html=
#ssh-askpass" title=3D"ssh-askpass-9.8p1">ssh-askpass-9.8p1</a> if it is
                  installed in your system, run the following commands as t=
he
                  <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cp -v /usr/share=
/applications/gparted.desktop /usr/share/applications/gparted.desktop.back =
&amp;&amp;
sed -i 's/Exec=3D/Exec=3Dsudo -A /'               /usr/share/applications/g=
parted.desktop</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Now, clicking on the menu item for Gparted, a dialog
                  appears on the screen, asking for the administrator
                  password.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
