                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470483808448" name=3D"idm140470483808448"></=
a>rxvt-unicode Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470483807744" name=3D"idm140470483807744"></=
a>Required
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libptytty" title=3D=
"libptytty-2.0">libptytty-2.0</a> and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www=
.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.ht=
ml#x-window-system" title=3D"Chapter&nbsp;24.&nbsp;Graphical Environments">=
a graphical
                environment</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470483805088" name=3D"idm140470483805088"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gdk-pixbuf" title=
=3D"gdk-pixbuf-2.42.12">gdk-pixbuf-2.42.12</a> (for background
                images) and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#startup=
-notification" title=3D"startup-notification-0.12">startup-notification-0.1=
2</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of rxvt-unicode
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">rxvt-unicode</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr --enable-everything &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-everything</code></e=
m>:
                Add support for all non-multichoice options. Details about
                the different options can be found in the file <code class=
=3D"filename">README.configure</code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--disable-xft</code>: Remove support=
 for
                Xft fonts.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--disable-perl</code>: Disable the
                embedded <span class=3D"application">Perl</span> interprete=
r.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--disable-afterimage</code>: Remove
                support for libAfterImage.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring rxvt-unicode
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">rxvt-unicode</span> termina=
l
                emulator uses the resource class <code class=3D"classname">=
URxvt</code> and the resource name <code class=3D"classname">urxvt</code>. =
You can add X resource definitions
                to a user's <code class=3D"filename">~/.Xresources</code> o=
r
                <code class=3D"filename">~/.Xdefaults</code> files or to th=
e
                system-wide <code class=3D"filename">/etc/X11/app-defaults/=
URxvt</code> file. The
                following example will load the <code class=3D"classname">m=
atcher</code> <span class=3D"application">Perl</span> extension (assuming <=
span class=3D"application">Perl</span> support wasn't disabled), which
                enables a left button click to open an underlined URL in th=
e
                specified browser, sets a background and foreground color a=
nd
                loads an Xft font (as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</=
code> user):
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt;&gt; /etc/=
X11/app-defaults/URxvt &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">! Use the specified colour as the windows backgroun=
d colour [default white]
URxvt*background: black

! Use the specified colour as the windows foreground colour [default black]
URxvt*foreground: yellow

! Select the fonts to be used. This is a comma separated list of font names
URxvt*font: xft:Monospace:pixelsize=3D18

! Comma-separated list(s) of perl extension scripts (default: "default")
URxvt*perl-ext: matcher

! Specifies the program to be started with a URL argument. Used by
URxvt*url-launcher: firefox

! When clicked with the mouse button specified in the "matcher.button" reso=
urce
! (default 2, or middle), the program specified in the "matcher.launcher"
! resource (default, the "url-launcher" resource, "sensible-browser") will =
be
! started with the matched text as first argument.
! Below, default modified to mouse left button.
URxvt*matcher.button:     1</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                In order to view the defined X resources, issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">xrdb -query</=
kbd></pre>
              <p>
                In order to add the modifications of the new user
                configuration file, keeping previously X configurations (of
                course, unless you are changing any on previously define),
                issue:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">xrdb -merge ~=
/.Xresources</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">rxvt-unicode</span> applica=
tion
                can also run in a daemon mode, which makes it possible to
                open multiple terminal windows within the same process. The
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>urxvtc</strong></span> clie=
nt
                then connects to the <span class=3D"command"><strong>urxvtd=
</strong></span> daemon and requests
                a new terminal window. Use this option with caution. If the
                daemon crashes, all the running processes in the terminal
                windows are terminated.
              </p>
              <p>
                You can start the <span class=3D"command"><strong>urxvtd</s=
trong></span> daemon in the system
                or personal startup <span class=3D"command"><strong>X</stro=
ng></span> session script (e.g.,
                <code class=3D"filename">~/.xinitrc</code>) by adding the
                following lines near the top of the script:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command"><code class=
=3D"literal"># Start the urxvtd daemon
urxvtd -q -f -o &amp;</code></kbd></pre>
              <p>
                For more information, examine the <span class=3D"command"><=
strong>urxvt</strong></span>, <span class=3D"command"><strong>urxvtd</stron=
g></span>, <span class=3D"command"><strong>urxvtc</strong></span>, and <cod=
e class=3D"filename">urxvtperl</code> man pages.
              </p>
              <p>
                If you use a Desktop Environment, a menu entry can be
                included, issuing, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</=
code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /usr/shar=
e/applications/urxvt.desktop &lt;&lt; "EOF" &amp;&amp;
<code class=3D"literal">[Desktop Entry]
Encoding=3DUTF-8
Name=3DRxvt-Unicode Terminal
Comment=3DUse the command line
GenericName=3DTerminal
Exec=3Durxvt
Terminal=3Dfalse
Type=3DApplication
Icon=3Dutilities-terminal
Categories=3DGTK;Utility;TerminalEmulator;
#StartupNotify=3Dtrue
Keywords=3Dconsole;command line;execute;</code>
EOF

update-desktop-database -q</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                For that, you need <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
desktop-file-utils" title=3D"desktop-file-utils-0.27">desktop-file-utils-0.=
27</a>
                and at least one of <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.l=
inuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html=
#gnome-icon-theme" title=3D"gnome-icon-theme-3.12.0">gnome-icon-theme-3.12.=
0</a>,
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#oxygen-icons" title=
=3D"oxygen-icons-6.0.0">oxygen-icons-6.0.0</a> and <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#lxde-icon-theme" title=3D"lxde-icon-theme-0.5.1">lxde-ico=
n-theme-0.5.1</a>. Uncomment
                the line with <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D=
"quote">StartupNotify=3Dtrue</span>=E2=80=9D</span> if <a class=3D"xref" hr=
ef=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2=
-sysv-nochunks.html#startup-notification" title=3D"startup-notification-0.1=
2">startup-notification-0.12</a> is
                installed.
              </p>
