                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"xscreensaver-config" name=3D"xscreensaver-=
config"></a>Config Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/X11/app-defaults/XScreenSav=
er</code> and
                  <code class=3D"filename">~/.xscreensaver</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470483253936" name=3D"idm14047048325=
3936"></a>Linux PAM Configuration
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  If <span class=3D"application">XScreenSaver</span> has be=
en
                  built with <span class=3D"application">Linux PAM</span>
                  support, you need to create a <span class=3D"application"=
>PAM</span> configuration file, to get it
                  working correctly with BLFS.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Issue the following commands as the <code class=3D"system=
item">root</code> user to create the configuration
                  file for <span class=3D"application">Linux PAM</span>:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/pa=
m.d/xscreensaver &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal"># Begin /etc/pam.d/xscreensaver

auth    include system-auth
account include system-account

# End /etc/pam.d/xscreensaver</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
              </div>
            </div>
