          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to intel-media
              </h3>
              <p>
                The <span class=3D"application">intel-media</span> package
                provides a VA API driver for Intel GPUs that are provided
                with Broadwell CPUs and higher. This includes support for a
                variety of codecs.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470481900816" name=3D"idm140470481900816"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://g=
ithub.com/intel/media-driver/archive/intel-media-24.2.5.tar.gz">
                      https://github.com/intel/media-driver/archive/intel-m=
edia-24.2.5.tar.gz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: c602d9a3ebebb2ad8a5239dc5951c65b
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 25 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 2.1 GB (360 MB install=
ed
                      with a single GPU model)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 3.8 SBU (with parallelism=3D4 a=
nd a
                      single GPU model)
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  The tarball <code class=3D"filename">intel-media-24.2.5.t=
ar.gz</code> will extract to
                  the directory <code class=3D"filename">media-driver-intel=
-media-24.2.5</code>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470481890096" name=3D"idm140470481890096"></=
