blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#cmake" title=3D"CMa=
ke-3.30.2">CMake-3.30.2</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfro=
mscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#intel-=
gmmlib" title=3D"Intel-gmmlib-22.4.1">Intel-gmmlib-22.4.1</a>, <a class=3D"=
xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-B=
OOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libva" title=3D"libva-2.22.0">libva-2.22.0</a>,
                and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.=
org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#xorg-env" title=
=3D"Setting up the Xorg Build Environment">Xorg build
                environment</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"intel-media-kernel" name=3D"intel-media-kernel"></=
a>Kernel Configuration
              </h3>
              <p>
                Enable the following options in the kernel configuration.
                Recompile the kernel if necessary:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"blue">D</span>evice Driv=
ers ---&gt;
  <span class=3D"blue">G</span>raphics support ---&gt;
    &lt;*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">D</span>irect Rendering Manager (XFree=
86 4.1.0 and higher DRI support) ---&gt;
                                                                      ...  =
[DRM]
      &lt;*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">I</span>ntel 8xx/9xx/G3x/G4x/HD Grap=
hics                         [DRM_I915]</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of intel-media
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  This package takes a long time to build because it compil=
es
                  code specific to each individual generation of Intel GPUs
                  and for a variety of media codecs.
                </p>
                <p>
                  If you know the model of your Intel GPU, you can pass the
                  <code class=3D"option">-D{GEN{8,9,11,12},MTL,ARL}=3DOFF</=
code>
                  option to the <span class=3D"command"><strong>cmake</stro=
ng></span> command but leaving
                  the option for your GPU out. Note that the <span class=3D=
"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D"quote">GEN</span>=E2=80=9D</span> number he=
re
                  is the generation of the GPU, not the CPU. For example,
                  with an Intel Core i7-1065G7 CPU shipping a 11th-generati=
on
                  Intel GPU, the <code class=3D"option">-D{GEN{8,9,12},MTL,=
ARL}=3DOFF</code> option can be
                  used so the code specific to the other generations of Int=
el
                  GPUs won't be built.
                </p>
                <p>
                  To determine the model of the Intel GPU, install <a class=
=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BL=
FS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#pciutils" title=3D"pciutils-3.13.0">pciutil=
s-3.13.0</a> and run <span class=3D"command"><strong>lspci -nn | grep -Ei
                  'VGA|DISPLAY'</strong></span> first. It will output some
                  information about the GPU. If the output contains
                  <code class=3D"literal">Meteor Lake</code>, the GPU model=
 is
                  <code class=3D"literal">MTL</code>. Otherwise, follow
                  <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://dgpu-docs.intel.com/de=
vices/hardware-table.html">https://dgpu-docs.intel.com/devices/hardware-tab=
le.html</a>
                  to find the entry for your GPU and the model of the GPU
                  should be in the <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span cla=
ss=3D"quote">Architecture</span>=E2=80=9D</span> column. The Xe and
                  Xe-HPG architectures are covered by the <code class=3D"li=
teral">GEN12</code> model.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">intel-media</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

cmake -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=3D$XORG_PREFIX \
      -D INSTALL_DRIVER_SYSCONF=3DOFF        \
      -D BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease                \
      -G Ninja                             \
      -W no-dev ..                         &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
            </div>
