he
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

cmake -D CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=3D/usr \
      -D CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DRelease  \
      -D MOD_QT=3DOFF                \
      -D MOD_QT6=3DON                \
      -W no-dev .. &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite. However a tes=
t
                .mp4 file can be played in a local graphical environment wi=
th
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>./out/bin/melt
                &lt;filename&gt;.mp4</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  This application uses advanced graphical capabilities. In
                  some cases, firmware for your specific graphics adaptor m=
ay
                  be needed. See <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linu=
xfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#vi=
deo-firmware" title=3D"Firmware for Video Cards">the section called
                  =E2=80=9CFirmware for Video Cards=E2=80=9D</a> for more i=
nformation.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
