            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Pipewire
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">pipewire</span> by runn=
ing
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup ..                 \
      --prefix=3D/usr            \
      --buildtype=3Drelease      \
      -D session-managers=3D"[]" &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the result, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong>=
ninja test</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D
                session-managers=3D"[]"</code></em>: This switch allows
                specifying the session managers to build as subprojects. We
                specify an empty list to prevent <span class=3D"command"><s=
trong>meson</strong></span> from downloading any
                external copy of the session managers. A Pipewire session
                manager recommended by the PipeWire developers for general
                use, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch=
.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#wireplumber" t=
itle=3D"Wireplumber-0.5.5">Wireplumber-0.5.5</a>, is available as a
                separate BLFS package. Build it after installing Pipewire i=
f
                you need to run the Pipewire daemon (for example in order t=
o
                support <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscra=
tch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#snapshot" t=
itle=3D"Snapshot-46.3">Snapshot-46.3</a>).
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D docs=3Dtrue</code>: This switch e=
nables
                the generation of HTML documentation. The optional
                dependencies for documentation need to be installed for thi=
s
                to work.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D man=3Dtrue</code>: This switch en=
ables
                the generation of manual pages. The optional dependencies f=
or
                documentation need to be installed for this to work.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D ffmpeg=3Denabled</code>: This swi=
tch
                enables using ffmpeg for audio conversion as a SPA backend.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">-D vulkan=3Denabled</code>: This swi=
tch
                enables using Vulkan for video rendering as a SPA backend.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">pipewire, pw-cat, pw-cli,
                    pw-config, pw-dot, pw-dump, pw-jack, pw-link,
                    pw-loopback, pw-metadata, pw-mididump, pw-mon,
                    pw-profiler, pw-reserve, pw-top, pw-v4l2, spa-acp-tool,
