            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Wireplumber
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Wireplumber</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup --prefix=3D/usr --buildtype=3Drelease -D system-lua=3Dtrue .. &=
amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>ninja test</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install</kbd=
></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>-D system-lua=3Dtrue</code></=
em>:
                This switch enables using the system version of Lua. Omit
                this switch if you have not installed Lua, but note that
                <span class=3D"application">meson</span> will download and
                install it's own version.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Wireplumber
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470479739808" name=3D"idm14047047973=
9808"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  In order for Wireplumber to be used by Pipewire,
                  Wireplumber must be configured to start when a desktop
                  environment is started.
                </p>
                <p>
                  First, create a shell script that will start Wireplumber
                  and Pipewire in the correct order as the <code class=3D"s=
ystemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /usr/bi=
n/pipewire-launcher.sh &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">#!/bin/sh
# Begin /usr/bin/pipewire-launcher.sh

# Start Pipewire first.
exec /usr/bin/pipewire &amp;

# Wait for a second for Pipewire to launch.
sleep 1

# Start Wireplumber now that Pipewire has been started.
exec /usr/bin/wireplumber &amp;
# End /usr/bin/pipewire-launcher.sh</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Next, make this shell script executable as the <code clas=
s=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">chmod +x /usr/bi=
n/pipewire-launcher.sh</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Finally, create an XDG Autostart file that will run
                  <span class=3D"command"><strong>/usr/bin/pipewire-launche=
r.sh</strong></span>
                  when a desktop environment is started, as the <code class=
=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt; /etc/xd=
g/autostart/pipewire.desktop &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">[Desktop Entry]
Version=3D1.0
Name=3DPipewire
Comment=3DStarts the Pipewire and Wireplumber daemons
Exec=3D/usr/bin/pipewire-launcher.sh
Terminal=3Dfalse
Type=3DApplication</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Now that Wireplumber is configured to start when a deskto=
p
                  environment is started, it is recommended that you log ou=
t
                  of your session and log back in again.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
