              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#cups" title=3D"Cups=
-2.4.10">Cups-2.4.10</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470477568112" name=3D"idm140470477568112"></=
a>Recommended (at runtime)
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                Two families of DyeSub photo printers each require another
                library at runtime. Unless you have one of these devices yo=
u
                will not want these libraries.
              </p>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                For the Sinfonia S6145 and the Ciaat Brava 21, <a class=3D"=
ulink" href=3D"https://git.shaftnet.org/gitea/slp/selphy_print/src/branch/m=
aster/lib6145">
                libS6145ImageReProcess</a>, see <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"=
https://www.peachyphotos.com/blog/posts/201601301524-sinfonia-chc-s6145-cs2=
-and-ciaat-brava-21-revited/">
                Peachy Photos (Sinfonia)</a> for instructions on how to bui=
ld
                and test this.
              </p>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                For the Mitsubishi D70 family and the similar Kodak 305,
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://git.shaftnet.org/gitea/s=
lp/selphy_print/src/branch/master/lib70x">
                libMitsuD70ImageReProcess</a>, see <a class=3D"ulink" href=
=3D"https://www.peachyphotos.com/blog/posts/201610061508-mitsubishi-cp-d70-=
family-working/">
                Peachy Photos (Mitsubishi CP-D70)</a> for instructions on h=
ow
                to build and test this.
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470477561328" name=3D"idm140470477561328"></=
a>Optional (to Regenerate
                Documentation)
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#imagemagick" title=
=3D"ImageMagick-7.1.1-36">ImageMagick-7.1.1-36</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#texlive" title=3D"texlive-20240312-source">texlive-202403=
12</a> (or <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/=
downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#tl-installer" title=3D"i=
nstall-tl-unx">install-tl-unx</a>), <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.l=
inuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html=
#doxygen" title=3D"Doxygen-1.12.0">Doxygen-1.12.0</a>, and
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#docbook-utils" titl=
e=3D"DocBook-utils-0.6.14">DocBook-utils-0.6.14</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"gutenprint-escputil" name=3D"gutenprint-escputil">=
</a>Kernel Configuration
              </h3>
              <p>
                If you intend to use <span class=3D"application">escputil</=
span> with a USB-connected Epson
                Stylus printer for commands such as <span class=3D"command"=
><strong>--ink-level</strong></span> which need to
                access the raw device, you must enable the kernel's usblp
                driver. Enable the following options in your kernel
                configuration and recompile the kernel:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"screen"><span class=3D"blue">D</span>evice Driv=
ers ---&gt;
  [*] <span class=3D"blue">U</span>SB support ---&gt;                      =
                       [USB_SUPPORT]
    &lt;*/M&gt; <span class=3D"blue">U</span>SB Printer support            =
                          [USB_PRINTER]</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Gutenprint
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Gutenprint</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sed -i 's|$(P=
ACKAGE)/doc|doc/$(PACKAGE)-$(VERSION)|' \
       {,doc/,doc/developer/}Makefile.in &amp;&amp;

./configure --prefix=3D/usr                 \
            --disable-static              \
            --without-gimp2               \
            --without-gimp2-as-gutenprint &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make check</strong></span>. The tests take
                a very long time and use a lot of disk space. When last
                tested (version 5.2.15 in June 2019) this needed 75 SBU and
                13.5 GB to complete the tests (one test, rastertogutenprint
                failed because the CUPS ppds are for a previous version.
                Maybe genppds should be run before the tests). Note that th=
e
                tests used only one CPU.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install &amp;=
&amp;
install -v -m755 -d /usr/share/doc/gutenprint-5.3.4/api/gutenprint{,ui2} &a=
mp;&amp;
install -v -m644    doc/gutenprint/html/* \
                    /usr/share/doc/gutenprint-5.3.4/api/gutenprint &amp;&am=
p;
install -v -m644    doc/gutenprintui2/html/* \
                    /usr/share/doc/gutenprint-5.3.4/api/gutenprintui2</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sed -i '...'
                ...Makefile.in</strong></span>: This command is used so tha=
t
                the package documentation is installed in the conventional
                <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/doc</code> directory
                structure instead of <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/gu=
tenprint/doc</code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-static</code></em>:
                This switch prevents installation of static versions of the
                libraries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--without-gimp2</code></em>: =
This
                switch disables support for GIMP because it has not been
                updated to support GIMP3 yet.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring Gutenprint
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470477530304" name=3D"idm14047047753=
0304"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  For <span class=3D"application">CUPS</span> to see newly
                  installed print drivers, it has to be restarted (as the
                  <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user):
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">/etc/rc.d/init.d=
/cups restart</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  Then point your web browser to <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D=
"http://localhost:631/">http://localhost:631/</a> to add a
                  new printer to <span class=3D"application">CUPS</span>.
                </p>
              </div>
