tp://www.net-snmp.org/">Net-SNMP</a>, <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"http://cyb=
erelk.net/tim/libieee1284/">libieee1284</a>,
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"http://www.gphoto.org/">libgphot=
o2</a>, and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs=
/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#texlive" title=3D"texli=
ve-20240312-source">texlive-20240312</a> (or <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"http=
s://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-noch=
unks.html#tl-installer" title=3D"install-tl-unx">install-tl-unx</a>)
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"kernel" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                <a id=3D"sane-kernel" name=3D"sane-kernel"></a>Kernel
                Configuration, Drivers and Additional Packages
              </h3>
              <p>
                To access your scanner, you will probably need the related
                kernel drivers and/or additional support packages. A SCSI
                scanner will need SCSI drivers, a parallel port scanner nee=
ds
                parallel port support (you should use enhanced EPP modes) a=
nd
                perhaps <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"http://cyberelk.net/tim/=
libieee1284/">libieee1284</a>, and a
                USB scanner will need the <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https:/=
/www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunk=
s.html#libusb" title=3D"libusb-1.0.27">libusb-1.0.27</a> package. For HP
                devices, you may need <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://so=
urceforge.net/projects/hplip/files/hplip/">hplip</a>.
                Ensure you have the necessary drivers properly configured t=
o
                access the devices.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of SANE
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470477337280" name=3D"idm14047047733=
7280"></a>Installation of SANE
                        Backends
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  The <span class=3D"application">SANE</span> daemon should=
 run
                  with its own group. Create this group by issuing the
                  following command as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root<=
/code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">groupadd -g 70 s=
canner</kbd></pre>
                <div class=3D"admon note">
                  <h3>
                    Note
                  </h3>
                  <p>
                    <span class=3D"command"><strong>configure</strong></spa=
n>
                    assumes that the user building <span class=3D"applicati=
on">SANE</span> Backends is a member of the
                    <code class=3D"systemitem">scanner</code> group for tes=
ting
                    the existence of this group. As a result, the user
                    building the package needs to be added to the
                    <code class=3D"systemitem">scanner</code> group. Add th=
e
                    user to the <code class=3D"systemitem">scanner</code> g=
roup
                    by issuing the following command as the <code class=3D"=
systemitem">root</code> user:
                  </p>
                  <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">usermod -G sca=
nner -a <em class=3D"replaceable"><code>username</code></em></kbd></pre>
                  <p>
                    After adding the <code class=3D"systemitem">scanner</co=
de>
                    group as above, you will need to log out and back in to
                    activate it.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <p>
                  For a USB scanner, if you are linking to <a class=3D"xref=
" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-=
12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libusb" title=3D"libusb-1.0.27">libusb-1.0.27</a>,
                  include the configure switch --enable-libusb_1_0. Install
                  <span class=3D"application">SANE</span> Backends by runni=
ng
                  the following commands:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">sg scanner =
-c "                                 \
PYTHON=3Dpython3 ./configure --prefix=3D/usr        \
                           --sysconfdir=3D/etc    \
                           --localstatedir=3D/var \
                           --with-lockdir=3D/run/lock \
                           --docdir=3D/usr/share/doc/sane-backends-1.2.1" &=
amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><stro=
ng>make check</strong></span>.
                </p>
                <p>
                  Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
                </p>
                <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install    =
                                     &amp;&amp;
install -m 644 -v tools/udev/libsane.rules           \
                  /etc/udev/rules.d/65-scanner.rules &amp;&amp;
mkdir -p          /run/lock/sane &amp;&amp;
chgrp -v scanner  /run/lock/sane</kbd></pre>
                <p>
                  With the scanner on, run <span class=3D"command"><strong>=
scanimage -L</strong></span> and the name
                  and location of the device should appear. Of course, you
                  need the device drivers configured, in order to run this
                  test.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sg scanner -c
                "..."</strong></span>: runs the command between double quot=
es
                with principal group <code class=3D"systemitem">scanner</co=
de>.
                This may be needed if the user has been newly added to grou=
p
                scanner, and has not logged out and in.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>PYTHON=3Dpython3</code></em>:=
 This
                switch forces the build system to use Python 3 instead of
                Python 2.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--sysconfdir=3D/etc</code></e=
m>:
                This switch installs the configuration files in <code class=
=3D"filename">/etc/sane.d</code> instead of <code class=3D"filename">/usr/e=
tc/sane.d</code>.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"configuration" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Configuring SANE
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"sane-config" name=3D"sane-config"></a>Conf=
ig
                        Files
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>
                  <code class=3D"filename">/etc/sane.d/*.conf</code>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"sect3" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
                <div class=3D"titlepage">
                  <div>
                    <div>
                      <h4 class=3D"title">
                        <a id=3D"idm140470477297632" name=3D"idm14047047729=
7632"></a>Configuration Information
                      </h4>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class=3D"sect4">
                  <div class=3D"titlepage">
                    <div>
                      <div>
                        <h5 class=3D"title">
                          <a id=3D"idm140470477296944" name=3D"idm140470477=
296944"></a>Backend Configuration
                        </h5>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <p>
                    The backend configuration files are located in
                    <code class=3D"filename">/etc/sane.d</code>. Informatio=
n
                    for configuring the various backends can be found by
                    using the man(5) page for the desired backend. Run
                    <span class=3D"command"><strong>man sane-<em class=3D"r=
eplaceable"><code>&lt;backend&gt;</code></em></strong></span>,
                    substituting the desired backend.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    Add any users that will use a scanner to the <code clas=
s=3D"systemitem">scanner</code> group.
                  </p>
                  <p>
                    If you want to access a network scanner, include two
                    lines in <code class=3D"filename">net.conf</code>, as t=
he
                    <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user (make sure =
to
                    replace &lt;server_ip&gt; by the actual value):
                  </p>
                  <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">cat &gt;&gt; /=
etc/sane.d/net.conf &lt;&lt; "EOF"
<code class=3D"literal">connect_timeout =3D 60
&lt;server_ip&gt;</code>
EOF</kbd></pre>
                  <p>
                    On the server side, include the client ip in the access
                    list of <code class=3D"filename">/etc/sane.d/saned.conf=
</code>, restart the
                    <span class=3D"command"><strong>saned</strong></span>
                    daemon, and make sure the firewall, if any, is open to
                    the client.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div class=3D"sect4">
                  <div class=3D"titlepage">
                    <div>
                      <div>
                        <h5 class=3D"title">
                          <a id=3D"idm140470477285344" name=3D"idm140470477=
285344"></a>General Information
                        </h5>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <p>
                    For general information about configuring and using
                    <span class=3D"application">SANE</span>, see <span clas=
s=3D"command"><strong>man sane</strong></span>. For
                    information about USB scanning devices, run <span class=
=3D"command"><strong>man sane-usb</strong></span>. For
                    information about SCSI devices, run <span class=3D"comm=
and"><strong>man sane-scsi</strong></span>.
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div class=3D"sect4">
                  <div class=3D"titlepage">
                    <div>
                      <div>
                        <h5 class=3D"title">
                          <a id=3D"idm140470477280960" name=3D"idm140470477=
280960"></a>Configuration and setup of
                          the 'saned' daemon
                        </h5>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <p>
                    The <span class=3D"command"><strong>saned</strong></spa=
n>
                    daemon is not meant to be used for untrusted clients. Y=
ou
                    should provide <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
fw-firewall" title=3D"Setting Up a Network Firewall">Firewalling</a>
                    protection to ensure only trusted clients access the
                    daemon. Due to the complex security requirements to
                    ensure only trusted clients access the daemon, BLFS doe=
s
                    not provide instructions to configure the <span class=
=3D"command"><strong>saned</strong></span> daemon. Some good
                    (but outdated) information for setting up and securing
                    the <span class=3D"command"><strong>saned</strong></spa=
n>
                    daemon can be found at <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https=
://penguin-breeder.org/sane/saned/">https://penguin-breeder.org/sane/saned/=
</a>.
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">gamma4scanimage, sane-config,
                    saned, sane-find-scanner, scanimage, and umax_pp</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Libraries:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">libsane.so and numerous scanner
                    backend modules</span>
                  </div>
