aita-1.5.3</a>,
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libwebp" title=3D"l=
ibwebp-1.4.0">libwebp-1.4.0</a>, and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.=
linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.htm=
l#sane" title=3D"SANE-1.2.1">SANE-1.2.1</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of Simple-scan
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Simple-scan</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">mkdir build &=
amp;&amp;
cd    build &amp;&amp;

meson setup --prefix=3D/usr --buildtype=3Drelease .. &amp;&amp;
ninja</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ninja install &amp=
;&amp;
gtk-update-icon-cache -qtf /usr/share/icons/hicolor</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--buildtype=3Drelease</code><=
/em>:
                Specify a buildtype suitable for stable releases of the
                package, as the default may produce unoptimized binaries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>gtk-update-icon-cache
                [...]</strong></span>: This command updates the system-wide
                GTK+ icon cache since Simple-scan's build system does not
                update it to account for the icons that it installs.
              </p>
            </div>
