                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470477168528" name=3D"idm140470477168528"></=
a>Additional Downloads
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Required patch: <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/sgml-common-0.6.3-manpage-1.patch"=
>
                      https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/sg=
ml-common-0.6.3-manpage-1.patch</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of SGML Common
              </h3>
              <p>
                Instead of the normal convention of including the autotools
                files in the package, the maintainers included symlinks to
                the files in <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/automake</=
code>. For previous versions
                of <span class=3D"application">Automake</span> this convent=
ion
                is correct, but recent versions of <span class=3D"applicati=
on">Automake</span> install the internal files in
                version specific directories. This causes the <span class=
=3D"command"><strong>configure</strong></span> script to abort.
