            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of OpenSP
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">OpenSP</span> by runnin=
g
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">patch -Np1 -i=
 ../OpenSP-1.5.2-gcc14-1.patch          &amp;&amp;
sed -i 's/32,/253,/' lib/Syntax.cxx                  &amp;&amp;
sed -i 's/LITLEN          240 /LITLEN          8092/' \
    unicode/{gensyntax.pl,unicode.syn}               &amp;&amp;

./configure --prefix=3D/usr                              \
            --disable-static                           \
            --disable-doc-build                        \
            --enable-default-catalog=3D/etc/sgml/catalog \
            --enable-http                              \
            --enable-default-search-path=3D/usr/share/sgml &amp;&amp;

make pkgdatadir=3D/usr/share/sgml/OpenSP-1.5.2</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make check</strong></span>. As many as nine
                of the 23 tests may fail. Do not be alarmed.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make pkgdatadir=3D=
/usr/share/sgml/OpenSP-1.5.2 \
     docdir=3D/usr/share/doc/OpenSP-1.5.2      \
     install &amp;&amp;

ln -v -sf onsgmls   /usr/bin/nsgmls   &amp;&amp;
ln -v -sf osgmlnorm /usr/bin/sgmlnorm &amp;&amp;
ln -v -sf ospam     /usr/bin/spam     &amp;&amp;
ln -v -sf ospcat    /usr/bin/spcat    &amp;&amp;
ln -v -sf ospent    /usr/bin/spent    &amp;&amp;
ln -v -sf osx       /usr/bin/sx       &amp;&amp;
ln -v -sf osx       /usr/bin/sgml2xml &amp;&amp;
ln -v -sf libosp.so /usr/lib/libsp.so</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sed -i
                's/32,/253,/...unicode.syn}</strong></span>: These seds
                prevent some annoying messages that may otherwise appear
                while running <span class=3D"command"><strong>openjade</str=
ong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-static</code></em>:
                This switch prevents installation of static versions of the
                libraries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-http</code></em>: Th=
is
                switch adds support for HTTP.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-doc-build</code></e=
m>:
                This switch prevents the <span class=3D"command"><strong>co=
nfigure</strong></span> script checking
                if you have <span class=3D"application">xmlto</span> instal=
led.
                If you have <span class=3D"application">xmlto</span>, you c=
an
                remove this option.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-default-catalog=3D/e=
tc/sgml/catalog</code></em>:
                This switch sets the path to the centralized catalog.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-default-search-path<=
/code></em>:
                This switch sets the default value of <code class=3D"envar"=
>SGML_SEARCH_PATH</code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--enable-xml-messages</code>: This
                switch adds support for XML Formatted Messages.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>make
                pkgdatadir=3D/usr/share/sgml/OpenSP-1.5.2</strong></span> :
                This sets the pkgdatadir variable in the <code class=3D"fil=
ename">Makefile</code> from <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/OpenSP</cod=
e> to <code class=3D"filename">/usr/share/sgml/OpenSP-1.5.2</code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>ln -v -sf ...</strong></spa=
n>:
                These commands create the <span class=3D"application">SP</s=
pan>
                equivalents of <span class=3D"application">OpenSP</span>
                executables and libraries.
              </p>
            </div>
