w.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/docbook-utils-0.6.14-grep_fix-1.pa=
tch">
                      https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/do=
cbook-utils-0.6.14-grep_fix-1.patch</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470476705696" name=3D"idm140470476705696"></=
a>DocBook-utils Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470476704992" name=3D"idm140470476704992"></=
a>Required
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#openjade" title=3D"=
OpenJade-1.3.2">OpenJade-1.3.2</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.l=
inuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html=
#docbook-dsssl" title=3D"docbook-dsssl-1.79">docbook-dsssl-1.79</a>, and <a=
 class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/sta=
ble/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#sgml-dtd-3" title=3D"docbook-3.1-dtd"=
>docbook-3.1-dtd</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470476701664" name=3D"idm140470476701664"></=
a>Recommended (Runtime Dependencies
                Only)
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#perl-sgmlspm" title=
=3D"SGMLSpm-1.1">SGMLSpm-1.1</a> (for conversion to man and
                texinfo), and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfr=
omscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#lynx"=
 title=3D"Lynx-2.9.2">Lynx-2.9.2</a> or <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://w=
ww.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.=
html#Links" title=3D"Links-2.30">Links-2.30</a> or <a class=3D"ulink" href=
=3D"http://w3m.sourceforge.net/">W3m</a> (for conversion to
                ASCII text)
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of DocBook-utils
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">DocBook-utils</span> by
                running the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">patch -Np1 -i=
 ../docbook-utils-0.6.14-grep_fix-1.patch &amp;&amp;
sed -i 's:/html::' doc/HTML/Makefile.in                &amp;&amp;

./configure --prefix=3D/usr --mandir=3D/usr/share/man      &amp;&amp;
make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not come with a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make docdir=3D/usr=
/share/doc install</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                Many packages use an alternate name for the <span class=3D"=
application">DocBook-utils</span> scripts. If you wish to
                create these alternate names, use the following command as
                the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">for doctype in htm=
l ps dvi man pdf rtf tex texi txt
do
    ln -svf docbook2$doctype /usr/bin/db2$doctype
done</kbd></pre>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  The <span class=3D"command"><strong>jw</strong></span> sc=
ript
                  uses the <span class=3D"command"><strong>which</strong></=
span> command to locate
                  required utilities. You must install <a class=3D"xref" hr=
ef=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2=
-sysv-nochunks.html#which" title=3D"Which-2.21 and Alternatives">Which-2.21=
</a>
                  before attempting to use any of the <span class=3D"applic=
ation">DocBook-utils</span> programs.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>patch -Np1 -i
                ../docbook-utils-0.6.14-grep_fix-1.patch</strong></span>:
                This patch corrects the syntax in the jw (Jade Wrapper)
                script which is at the heart of much db2* processing, so th=
at
                the current version of <span class=3D"application">grep</sp=
an>
                will not reject it.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sed -i 's:/html::'
                doc/HTML/Makefile.in</strong></span>: This command changes
                the installation directory of the HTML documents.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>docdir=3D/usr/share/doc</code=
></em>: This
                option is placed on the <span class=3D"command"><strong>mak=
e
                install</strong></span> line because it is not recognized b=
y
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>configure</strong></span>.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">docbook2dvi, docbook2html,
                    docbook2man, docbook2pdf, docbook2ps, docbook2rtf,
                    docbook2tex, docbook2texi, docbook2txt, jw, and
                    sgmldiff</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Libraries:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">None</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Directories:</stro=
ng>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">/usr/share/doc/docbook-utils-0.=
6.14
                    and /usr/share/sgml/docbook/utils-0.6.14</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Symlinks:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">db2dvi, db2html, db2man, db2pdf=
,
                    db2ps, db2rtf, db2tex, db2texi, and db2txt</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"variablelist">
                <h4>
                  <a id=3D"idm140470476669632" name=3D"idm140470476669632">=
</a>Short Descriptions
                </h4>
                <table border=3D"0" class=3D"variablelist">
                  <colgroup>
                    <col align=3D"left" valign=3D"top">
                    <col>
                  </colgroup>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"docbook2" name=3D"docbook2"></a><span cl=
ass=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>docbook2*</strong></span></spa=
n>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          are simple one-line wrapper scripts to <span clas=
s=3D"command"><strong>jw</strong></span>. They are
                          provided as easy-to-remember names used to conver=
t
                          DocBook or other SGML files to the respective
                          format
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"db2" name=3D"db2"></a><span class=3D"ter=
m"><span class=3D"command"><strong>db2*</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          are symlinks pointing at the respectively named
                          <span class=3D"command"><strong>docbook2*</strong=
></span>
                          commands, created to satisfy some program's use o=
f
                          these names
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"jw" name=3D"jw"></a><span class=3D"term"=
><span class=3D"command"><strong>jw</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a script used to convert DocBook or other SGML
                          files to various output formats. It hides most of
                          <span class=3D"application">OpenJade</span>'s
                          complexity and adds comfortable features
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"sgmldiff" name=3D"sgmldiff"></a><span cl=
ass=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>sgmldiff</strong></span></span=
>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is used to compare two SGML files and only return
                          the differences in the markup. This is especially
                          useful to compare files that should be identical
                          except for language differences in the content
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
