              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">Enscript</span> by runn=
ing
                the following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">./configure -=
-prefix=3D/usr              \
            --sysconfdir=3D/etc/enscript \
            --localstatedir=3D/var       \
            --with-media=3DLetter &amp;&amp;
make &amp;&amp;

pushd docs &amp;&amp;
  makeinfo --plaintext -o enscript.txt enscript.texi &amp;&amp;
popd</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you have <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#texlive=
" title=3D"texlive-20240312-source">texlive-20240312</a> installed, you
                can create Postscript and PDF documentation by issuing (doe=
s
                not support parallel make):
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">make -j1 -C d=
ocs ps pdf</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make check</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install &amp;=
&amp;

install -v -m755 -d /usr/share/doc/enscript-1.6.6 &amp;&amp;
install -v -m644    README* *.txt docs/*.txt \
                    /usr/share/doc/enscript-1.6.6</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                If you built Postscript and PDF documentation, install it
                using the following command as the <code class=3D"systemite=
m">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">install -v -m644 d=
ocs/*.{dvi,pdf,ps} \
                 /usr/share/doc/enscript-1.6.6</kbd></pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
