          <div class=3D"titlepage">
            <div>
              <div>
                <h2 class=3D"title">
                  <a id=3D"texlive" name=3D"texlive"></a>texlive-20240312-s=
ource
                </h2>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to TeX Live from source
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  According to <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://www.tug.o=
rg/historic/">https://www.tug.org/historic/</a>
                  the master site in France only supports ftp and rsync. No=
w
                  that ftp is generally deprecated, that page has links to
                  mirrors, some of which support https, e.g. in Utah and
                  Chemnitz as well as in China. If you prefer to use a
                  different mirror from the example links here, you will ne=
ed
                  to navigate to systems/historic/texlive/2024 or
                  systems/texlive/2024 as the case may be.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                Most of TeX Live can be built from source without a
                pre-existing installation, but <span class=3D"application">=
xindy</span> (for indexing) needs working
                versions of <span class=3D"command"><strong>latex</strong><=
/span> and <span class=3D"command"><strong>pdflatex</strong></span> when co=
nfigure is
                run, and the test suite and install for <span class=3D"comm=
and"><strong>asy</strong></span> (for vector graphics)
                will fail if TeX has not already been installed.
                Additionally, <span class=3D"application">biber</span> is n=
ot
                provided within the <span class=3D"application">texlive</sp=
an>
                source and the version of <span class=3D"application">dvisv=
gm</span> in the <span class=3D"application">texlive</span> tree cannot be =
built if shared
                system libraries are used.
              </p>
              <p>
                All of those packages are dealt with on their own pages and
                can be built after installing this package. If you have not
                already done so, you should start at <a class=3D"xref" href=
=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-s=
ysv-nochunks.html#tex-path" title=3D"Setting the PATH for TeX Live">Setting=
 the
                PATH for TeX Live</a> so that the final commands to
                initialize the new installation will be found.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470475720560" name=3D"idm140470475720560"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://f=
tp.math.utah.edu/pub/tex/historic/systems/texlive/2024/texlive-20240312-sou=
rce.tar.xz">
                      https://ftp.math.utah.edu/pub/tex/historic/systems/te=
xlive/2024/texlive-20240312-source.tar.xz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 1da2f08e3ba4a3708870dd088c1d6823
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 67 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 9.1 GB including the
                      additional download and the tests, 8.3 GB installed
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: 4.6 SBU including the additiona=
l
                      download and the tests, building with parallelism=3D4
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470475712976" name=3D"idm140470475712976"></=
a>Required Additional Downloads
              </h4>
              <p>
                Much of the texlive environment (including scripts,
                documentation, fonts, and various other files) is not part =
of
                the source tarball. You must download it separately. This
                will give you all of the additional files which are provide=
d
                by a full install of the binary version, as there is no
                realistic way to restrict which parts get installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                Because of the size of this package, it is unlikely to be
                mirrored by BLFS mirrors. If you are unable to download the
                files for this package, go to https://www.ctan.org/mirrors/
                to find a more-accessible mirror.
              </p>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://f=
tp.math.utah.edu/pub/tex/historic/systems/texlive/2024/texlive-20240312-tex=
mf.tar.xz">
                      https://ftp.math.utah.edu/pub/tex/historic/systems/te=
xlive/2024/texlive-20240312-texmf.tar.xz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: e67ce334dd0fddda5f4a87b4fcaaf48f
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 4.0 GB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <p>
                The tlpdb database is shipped as a separate tarball. The
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>texdoc</strong></span> prog=
ram
                needs a cache file derived from this (and will create the
                cache on its first run).
              </p>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://f=
tp.tu-chemnitz.de/pub/tug/historic/systems/texlive/2024/texlive-20240312-ex=
tra.tar.xz">
                      https://ftp.tu-chemnitz.de/pub/tug/historic/systems/t=
exlive/2024/texlive-20240312-extra.tar.xz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 1bd045bd1673ce61bde590c10b86c6cc
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 1.9 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Required patch: <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/texlive-20240312-source-upstream_f=
ixes-1.patch">
                      https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/te=
xlive-20240312-source-upstream_fixes-1.patch</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470475698384" name=3D"idm140470475698384"></=
a>TeX
                Live from source Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470475697680" name=3D"idm140470475697680"></=
a>Recommended
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#x-window-system" ti=
tle=3D"Chapter&nbsp;24.&nbsp;Graphical Environments">a graphical
                environment</a>
              </p>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                The source ships with its own versions of <span class=3D"em=
phasis"><em>many</em></span> libraries, and will use them
                unless it is forced to use the system versions. The followi=
ng
                are recommended so that the system version will be used:
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#cairo" title=3D"Cai=
ro-1.18.0">Cairo-1.18.0</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfro=
mscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#fontco=
nfig" title=3D"Fontconfig-2.15.0">Fontconfig-2.15.0</a>, <a class=3D"xref" =
href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12=
.2-sysv-nochunks.html#freetype2" title=3D"FreeType-2.13.3">FreeType-2.13.3<=
/a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downlo=
ads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gc" title=3D"GC-8.2.6">GC-8.2.=
6</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/down=
loads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#graphite2" title=3D"Graphite=
2-1.3.14">Graphite2-1.3.14</a>,
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#harfbuzz" title=3D"=
harfBuzz-9.0.0">harfBuzz-9.0.0</a> (built with graphite2
                enabled), <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromsc=
ratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#icu" titl=
e=3D"icu-75.1">ICU-75.1</a>, <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfro=
mscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#libpap=
er" title=3D"libpaper-2.2.5">libpaper-2.2.5</a> (used by at least
                context and xelatex), and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https:/=
/www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunk=
s.html#libpng" title=3D"libpng-1.6.43">libpng-1.6.43</a>
              </p>
              <p class=3D"recommended">
                Furthermore, the instructions below assume you are using th=
e
                layout described in <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.l=
inuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html=
#tex-path" title=3D"Setting the PATH for TeX Live">Setting the PATH for TeX
                Live</a>.
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470475686048" name=3D"idm140470475686048"></=
a>Optional
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                The source ships with its own versions of several libraries
                which are either not under active development, or only used
                for limited functionality. If you install these, as with so=
me
                other optional dependencies in this book you will need to
                tell <span class=3D"command"><strong>configure</strong></sp=
an>
                to use the system versions. <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"http=
s://libgd.github.io/">GD</a>, <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://www.t1lib.=
org/">t1lib</a>, <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://github.com/gdraheim/zzi=
plib/">ZZIPlib</a>, <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://scripts.sil.org/cms/=
scripts/page.php?site_id=3Dnrsi&amp;id=3DTECkitDownloads">
                TECkit</a>
              </p>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470475680048" name=3D"idm140470475680048"></=
a>Runtime dependencies
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"optional">
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://www.python.org/downloads=
/release/python-2718/">Python2</a>
                is used by the unmaintained ebong CTAN module (intended for
                writing Bengali in Rapid Roman Format). <code class=3D"file=
name">/usr/bin/python</code> is also in the shebang line
                for the latex-papersize and lilyglyphs scripts, and
                documentation at CTAN says both modules have been updated t=
o
                work with python3. In pythontex there are scripts to invoke
                python3 or python2 according to the system's version of
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>python</strong></span>.
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#ruby" title=3D"Ruby=
-3.3.4">Ruby-3.3.4</a> is used by two scripts, one is
                for pTex (Japanese vertical writing) and the other is
                match_parens which might be generally useful. The perl modu=
le
                <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://cpan.metacpan.org/author=
s/id/S/SR/SREZIC/Tk-804.036.tar.gz">
                Tk</a>, which needs to be run from an X11 session to run th=
e
                tests and requires <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.li=
nuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#=
tk" title=3D"Tk-8.6.14">Tk-8.6.14</a> is used by one of the scripts for
                ptex and is needed for texdoctk (a GUI interface for findin=
g
                documentation files and opening them with the appropriate
                viewer). <span class=3D"command"><strong>ps2pdf</strong></s=
pan>, from <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/=
downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#gs" title=3D"ghostscript=
-10.03.1">ghostscript-10.03.1</a>, is used by
                some utilities and scripts.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of TeX Live
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install TeX Live by running the following commands:
              </p>
              <div class=3D"admon caution">
                <h3>
                  Caution
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If you wish to upgrade to current <span class=3D"applicat=
ion">texlive</span> on an older system where extra
                  packages (<span class=3D"application">asymptote</span>,
                  <span class=3D"application">dvisvgm</span>, or <span clas=
s=3D"application">xindy</span>) have been installed, you will
                  need to reinstall those as well as fixing up your
                  <code class=3D"literal">PATH</code> for <code class=3D"li=
teral">$TEXLIVE_PREFIX</code>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  A successful install requires some texlive commands to be
                  run as the root user, so we will export the TEXARCH
                  variable to let <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> us=
e
                  it.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                Now, as a normal user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">export TEXARC=
H=3D$(uname -m | sed -e 's/i.86/i386/' -e 's/$/-linux/') &amp;&amp;

patch -Np1 -i ../texlive-20240312-source-upstream_fixes-1.patch &amp;&amp;

mkdir texlive-build &amp;&amp;
cd    texlive-build &amp;&amp;

../configure -C                                   \
    --prefix=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX                      \
    --bindir=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX/bin/$TEXARCH         \
    --datarootdir=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX                 \
    --includedir=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX/include          \
    --infodir=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX/texmf-dist/doc/info \
    --libdir=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX/lib                  \
    --mandir=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX/texmf-dist/doc/man   \
    --disable-native-texlive-build                \
    --disable-static --enable-shared              \
    --disable-dvisvgm                             \
    --with-system-cairo                           \
    --with-system-fontconfig                      \
    --with-system-freetype2                       \
    --with-system-gmp                             \
    --with-system-graphite2                       \
    --with-system-harfbuzz                        \
    --with-system-icu                             \
    --with-system-libgs                           \
    --with-system-libpaper                        \
    --with-system-libpng                          \
    --with-system-mpfr                            \
    --with-system-pixman                          \
    --with-system-zlib                            \
    --with-banner-add=3D" - BLFS" &amp;&amp;

make</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To test the results, issue: <span class=3D"command"><strong=
>make -k check</strong></span>. One test
                <code class=3D"filename">psutils.test</code> is known to fa=
il
                if using system libpaper because TeX Live includes old
                versions of both <span class=3D"application">psutils</span>=
 and
                <span class=3D"application">libpaper</span> which result in=
 a
                difference in the final decimal places of the psresize test=
.
                The <span class=3D"application">libpaper</span> developer d=
oes
                not think this is significant.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install-strip=
 &amp;&amp;
make texlinks      &amp;&amp;
mkdir -pv                                $TEXLIVE_PREFIX/tlpkg/TeXLive/ &am=
p;&amp;
install -v -m644 ../texk/tests/TeXLive/* $TEXLIVE_PREFIX/tlpkg/TeXLive/ &am=
p;&amp;
tar -xf ../../texlive-20240312-extra.tar.xz -C $TEXLIVE_PREFIX/tlpkg --stri=
p-components=3D2</kbd></pre>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  Only run <span class=3D"command"><strong>make
                  texlinks</strong></span> once. If it is rerun, it can
                  change all the program symlinks so that they point to
                  themselves and are useless.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                Now install the additional files as the <code class=3D"syst=
emitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">tar -xf ../../texl=
ive-20240312-texmf.tar.xz -C $TEXLIVE_PREFIX --strip-components=3D1</kbd></=
pre>
              <p>
                Still as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user,
                initialize the new system (the command <span class=3D"comma=
nd"><strong>fmtutil-sys --all</strong></span> will
                produce a <span class=3D"emphasis"><em>lot</em></span> of
                output):
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">mktexlsr &amp;&amp=
;
fmtutil-sys --all</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                To allow <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscr=
atch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#evince" ti=
tle=3D"Evince-46.3.1">Evince-46.3.1</a> or <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https:=
//www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochun=
ks.html#dvisvgm" title=3D"dvisvgm-3.4">dvisvgm-3.4</a> to link to
                <code class=3D"filename">libkpathsea.so</code>, as the
                <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user (re)create a
                symlink from <code class=3D"filename">/usr/lib</code>:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">ln -svf $TEXLIVE_P=
REFIX/lib/libkpathsea.so{,.6} /usr/lib</kbd></pre>
              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  TeX Live does not include the source for ConTeXt, only th=
e
                  items that are at CTAN. Trying to build ConTeXt purely fr=
om
                  source on a BLFS TeX Live system is a niche usage and loo=
ks
                  as if it will be more trouble than it is worth.
                </p>
                <p>
                  If you wish to use ConTeXt with <span class=3D"command"><=
strong>luametatex</strong></span> (most of the
                  old MKII and MKIV code was removed from TeX Live 2023 by
                  the ConTeXt developer), starting with the binary (only
                  installing ConTeXt, 753 MB in March 2024) would probably =
be
                  the easiest way to bootstrap it. The source for
                  <span class=3D"command"><strong>luametatex</strong></span=
>
                  can be pulled with git from <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"ht=
tps://github.com/contextgarden/luametatex/tags">github
                  luametatex</a>, compiled with meson and ninja, and
                  installed by copying to the correct program directory. Th=
is
                  should avoid having to fix all the symlinks etc and also
                  avoid including the many unrelated parts of texmf-dist. S=
ee
                  comments 1 to 5 of <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://wik=
i.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/ticket/17823">#17823</a>.
                </p>
              </div>
              <p>
                You can now proceed to <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.h=
tml#asymptote" title=3D"asymptote-2.91">asymptote-2.91</a>, <a class=3D"xre=
f" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK=
-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#biber" title=3D"biber-2.20">biber-2.20</a>, <a cla=
ss=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/=
BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#dvisvgm" title=3D"dvisvgm-3.4">dvisvgm-3.=
4</a>
                and / or <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscr=
atch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#xindy" tit=
le=3D"xindy-2.5.1">xindy-2.5.1</a> if you wish to install them.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>-C</strong></span>: creates
                config.cache, which saves significant time in a parallel
                build.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--prefix=3D</code></em>, <em =
class=3D"parameter"><code>--bindir=3D</code></em>, <em class=3D"parameter">=
<code>--datarootdir=3D</code></em>, and other
                <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D"quote">dir</s=
pan>=E2=80=9D</span>
                switches: these switches ensure that the files installed fr=
om
                source will overwrite any corresponding files previously
                installed by <span class=3D"application">install-tl-unx</sp=
an>
                so that the alternative methods of installing <span class=
=3D"application">texlive</span> are consistent.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--includedir=3D</code></em>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--libdir=3D</code></em> : the=
se
                switches ensure that the libraries and include files will b=
e
                within the directories for this year's texlive.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-static</code></em>:
                This switch prevents installation of static versions of the
                libraries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--enable-shared</code></em>: =
Use
                shared versions of <code class=3D"filename">libkpathsea</co=
de>,
                <code class=3D"filename">libptexenc</code>, <code class=3D"=
filename">libsynctex</code>, <code class=3D"filename">libtexlua52</code> an=
d <code class=3D"filename">libtexluajit</code>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--with-system-</code></em>...=
:
                Unless this parameter is used, the included versions of the=
se
                libraries will be statically compiled into the programs whi=
ch
                need them. If you decided not to install a recommended
                library, omit the corresponding switch.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--disable-dvisvgm</code></em>=
: As
                noted above, the shipped version of dvisvgm, which has
                modified configuration files, cannot be built with shared
                system libraries.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>make texlinks</strong></spa=
n> :
                this runs the texlinks.sh script to create symbolic links
                from formats to engines. In practice, several of the target=
s
                such as <span class=3D"command"><strong>xetex</strong></spa=
n>
                are now separate binaries and for these it will report "fil=
e
                already exists".
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>tar -xf
                texlive-20240312-texmf.tar.xz -C $TEXLIVE_PREFIX
                --strip-components=3D1</strong></span>: the tarball contain=
s
                the files for the texmf-dist directory, and because of its
                size we do not want to waste time and space untarring it an=
d
                then copying the files.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>install -v -m644
                ../texk/tests/TeXLive/*
                $TEXLIVE_PREFIX/tlpkg/TeXLive/</strong></span>: This puts t=
he
                perl modules <code class=3D"filename">TLConfig.pm</code> an=
d
                <code class=3D"filename">TLUtils.pm</code> into the directo=
ry
                where the binary installer puts them - it is at the start o=
f
                the perl @INC@ PATH within texlive when installed using the
                above configure switches. Without these modules, texlive is
                unusable.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>mktexlsr</strong></span>:
                Create an <code class=3D"filename">ls-R</code> file which l=
ists
                what was installed - this is used by kpathsea to find files=
.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>fmtutil-sys
                --all</strong></span>: This initializes the TeX formats,
                Metafont bases and Metapost mems.
              </p>
              <p>
                <code class=3D"option">--without-x</code>: use this if you =
do
                not have Xorg installed.
              </p>
              <p>
                There are many other '--disable' or '--without' options. So=
me
                of them such as <code class=3D"option">--without-texinfo</c=
ode>
                are accepted but no longer do anything, others will prevent=
 a
                program being built - but the far greater amount of space
                used for the related items in texmf means there is no obvio=
us
                benefit from disabling a few of the programs.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"content" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Contents
              </h3>
              <div class=3D"segmentedlist">
                <div class=3D"seglistitem">
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Programs:</strong>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">Over 300 binaries and symlinks =
to
                    scripts</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Libraries:</strong=
>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">libkpathsea.so, libptexenc.so,
                    libsynctex.so, libtexlua52.so, libtexluajit.so</span>
                  </div>
                  <div class=3D"seg">
                    <strong class=3D"segtitle">Installed Directories:</stro=
ng>
                    <span class=3D"segbody">$TEXLIVE_PREFIX/bin,
                    $TEXLIVE_PREFIX/include, $TEXLIVE_PREFIX/lib,
                    $TEXLIVE_PREFIX/texmf-dist</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class=3D"variablelist">
                <h4>
                  <a id=3D"idm140470475587136" name=3D"idm140470475587136">=
</a>Short Descriptions
                </h4>
                <table border=3D"0" class=3D"variablelist">
                  <colgroup>
                    <col align=3D"left" valign=3D"top">
                    <col>
                  </colgroup>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"texlive-programs" name=3D"texlive-progra=
ms"></a><span class=3D"term"><span class=3D"command"><strong>TeX&nbsp;progr=
ams</strong></span></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          The programs included in <span class=3D"applicati=
on">TeX</span> are too numerous to
                          individually list. Please refer to the individual
                          program HTML and PDF pages in the various html,
                          man, or pdf files within the subdirectories of
                          <code class=3D"filename">2024/texmf-dist/</code>.
                          Using <span class=3D"command"><strong>texdoc
                          pdflatex</strong></span> ( replace <span class=3D=
"emphasis"><em>pdflatex</em></span> with the
                          command name ) may also be useful
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"libkpathsea" name=3D"libkpathsea"></a><s=
pan class=3D"term"><code class=3D"filename">libkpathsea.so</code></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          (kpathsearch) exists to look up a file in a list =
of
                          directories and is used by <span class=3D"command=
"><strong>kpsewhich</strong></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"libptexenc" name=3D"libptexenc"></a><spa=
n class=3D"term"><code class=3D"filename">libptexenc.so</code></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is a library for Japanese pTeX (publishing TeX)
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"libsynctex" name=3D"libsynctex"></a><spa=
n class=3D"term"><code class=3D"filename">libsynctex.so</code></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          is the SyncTeX (Synchronize TeXnology) parser
                          library
                        </p>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <p>
                          <a id=3D"libtexlua52" name=3D"libtexlua52"></a><s=
pan class=3D"term"><code class=3D"filename">libtexlua52.so</code></span>
                        </p>
                      </td>
