              <div class=3D"admon note">
                <h3>
                  Note
                </h3>
                <p>
                  If you have updated to a new release of texlive-source,
                  biber and its perl dependencies are still present in
                  <code class=3D"filename">/usr</code> and do not need to b=
e
                  rebuilt. However, biblatex installs in <code class=3D"fil=
ename">/opt/texlive/2024</code> and does need to be
                  reinstalled.
                </p>
                <p>
                  If you installed the above dependencies using the BLFS
                  instructions for each of them, <span class=3D"command"><s=
trong>perl ./Build.PL</strong></span> will
                  complain that Mozilla::CA is not installed, but that is n=
ot
                  needed unless CPAN was used to install the modules. BLFS
                  patches LWP::Protocol::https to use the system
                  certificates, Mozilla::CA uses old certificates.
                </p>
