          <div class=3D"sect1" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
            <div class=3D"package" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Introduction to xindy
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"application">Xindy</span> is an index proces=
sor
                that can be used to generate book-like indexes for arbitrar=
y
                document-preparation systems. This includes systems such as
                TeX and LaTeX, the roff-family, and SGML/XML-based systems
                (e.g., HTML) that process some kind of text and generate
                indexing information.
              </p>
              <p>
                This package is known to build and work properly using an L=
FS
                12.2 platform.
              </p>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470475325024" name=3D"idm140470475325024"></=
a>Package Information
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download (HTTP): <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://t=
ug.ctan.org/support/xindy/base/xindy-2.5.1.tar.gz">
                      https://tug.ctan.org/support/xindy/base/xindy-2.5.1.t=
ar.gz</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download MD5 sum: 221acfeeb0f6f8388f89a59c56491041
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Download size: 506 KB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated disk space required: 15 MB
                    </p>
                  </li>
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Estimated build time: less than 0.1 SBU
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470475317664" name=3D"idm140470475317664"></=
a>Required Additional Downloads
              </h4>
              <div class=3D"itemizedlist">
                <ul class=3D"compact">
                  <li class=3D"listitem">
                    <p>
                      Required patch: <a class=3D"ulink" href=3D"https://ww=
w.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/xindy-2.5.1-upstream_fixes-2.patch=
">
                      https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/patches/blfs/12.2/xi=
ndy-2.5.1-upstream_fixes-2.patch</a>
                    </p>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <h4>
                <a id=3D"idm140470475314896" name=3D"idm140470475314896"></=
a>Xindy Dependencies
              </h4>
              <h5>
                <a id=3D"idm140470475314208" name=3D"idm140470475314208"></=
a>Required
              </h5>
              <p class=3D"required">
                <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/=
blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#clisp" title=3D"Cli=
sp-2.49">Clisp-2.49</a> and <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfrom=
scratch.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#texlive=
" title=3D"texlive-20240312-source">texlive-20240312</a>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"installation" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Installation of xindy
              </h3>
              <p>
                Install <span class=3D"application">xindy</span> by running=
 the
                following commands:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"userinput"><kbd class=3D"command">export TEXARC=
H=3D$(uname -m | sed -e 's/i.86/i386/' -e 's/$/-linux/') &amp;&amp;

sed -i "s/ grep -v '^;'/ awk NF/" make-rules/inputenc/Makefile.in &amp;&amp=
;

sed -i 's%\(indexentry\)%\1\\%' make-rules/inputenc/make-inp-rules.pl &amp;=
&amp;

patch -Np1 -i ../xindy-2.5.1-upstream_fixes-2.patch &amp;&amp;

./configure --prefix=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX              \
            --bindir=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX/bin/$TEXARCH \
            --datarootdir=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX         \
            --includedir=3D/usr/include             \
            --libdir=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX/texmf-dist   \
            --mandir=3D$TEXLIVE_PREFIX/texmf-dist/doc/man &amp;&amp;

make LC_ALL=3DPOSIX</kbd></pre>
              <p>
                This package does not have a test suite.
              </p>
              <p>
                Now, as the <code class=3D"systemitem">root</code> user:
              </p>
              <pre class=3D"root"><kbd class=3D"command">make install</kbd>=
</pre>
            </div>
            <div class=3D"commands" lang=3D"en" xml:lang=3D"en">
              <h3 class=3D"sect2">
                Command Explanations
              </h3>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sed -i "s/ grep -v '^;'/ aw=
k
                NF/" ...</strong></span>: The build sorts files in
                latin{1..3} encodings to create latin.xdy, and unicode
                versions of these to create utf8.xdy after using <span clas=
s=3D"command"><strong>grep -v '^;'</strong></span> to remove
                blank lines. With <span class=3D"application">grep-2.23</sp=
an>
                any data not in the expected encoding is treated as binary,
                resulting in a useless file. This command uses an alternati=
ve
                way of removing blank lines.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sed -i 's%\(indexentry\)%\1=
\\%'
                ...</strong></span>: A regexp contains <code class=3D"liter=
al">indexentry{</code> - perl has warned about the
                unescaped left brace for some time and now treats it as
                illegal. Change it to <code class=3D"literal">indexentry\{<=
/code>, doubling the backslash for
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>sed</strong></span>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>patch -Np1 -i
                ../xindy-2.5.1-upstream_fixes-2.patch</strong></span>:
                <span class=3D"application">Xindy</span> is now maintained =
at
                CTAN. This patch updates the source with some of the change=
s
                made there (but ignoring changes which were only made to
                allow for spaces in pathnames and some trivial recent
                changes).
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--prefix=3D</code></em>, <em =
class=3D"parameter"><code>--bindir=3D</code></em>, <em class=3D"parameter">=
<code>--datarootdir=3D</code></em>, and other
                <span class=3D"quote">=E2=80=9C<span class=3D"quote">dir</s=
pan>=E2=80=9D</span>
                switches: these switches ensure that the files installed fr=
om
                source will overwrite any corresponding files previously
                installed by <span class=3D"application">install-tl-unx</sp=
an>
                so that the alternative methods of installing <span class=
=3D"application">texlive</span> are consistent.
              </p>
              <p>
                <em class=3D"parameter"><code>--includedir=3D/usr/include</=
code></em>: This
                parameter ensures that the <code class=3D"filename">kpathse=
a</code> headers from <a class=3D"xref" href=3D"https://www.linuxfromscratc=
h.org/blfs/downloads/stable/BLFS-BOOK-12.2-sysv-nochunks.html#texlive" titl=
e=3D"texlive-20240312-source">texlive-20240312</a> will be found.
              </p>
              <p>
                <span class=3D"command"><strong>make
                LC_ALL=3DPOSIX</strong></span>: with the current version of
                <span class=3D"application">coreutils</span> it is essentia=
l to
                build <span class=3D"application">xindy</span> in the POSIX=
 (or
                C) locale because in a UTF-8 locale the file <code class=3D=
"filename">latin.xdy</code> will contain only a heading and
                then a line '<code class=3D"literal">Binary file (standard
                input) matches</code>' instead of the many lines of
                <span class=3D"application">lisp</span> merge-rule commands=
 it
                ought to contain.
              </p>
            </div>
